
3
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:24,775
[popping]

4
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:44,461
[soft rustling]

5
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,269
[KAGAYA]
Within the next five days,

6
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:02,980
Muzan will come.

7
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:12,113
I will be the bait you use.

8
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:15,784
When he comes,
I need you to behead him.

9
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:23,250
Master, what leads you
to believe he'll find you?

10
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:26,211
[Kagaya chuckles weakly]

11
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:28,964
My intuition. That's all.

12
00:01:29,715 --> 00:01:31,466
Nothing beyond that.

13
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:35,012
But listen,
the others can't know.

14
00:01:35,554 --> 00:01:40,225
They would never agree
to using me as bait like this.

15
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:42,603
They would sooner die
than do it.

16
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:47,649
You're the only one
that I can ask, Gyomei.

17
00:01:49,944 --> 00:01:53,530
Even if you behead him,
he won't die.

18
00:01:53,572 --> 00:01:54,990
♪

19
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:59,202
There's likely only one way
to destroy Muzan.

20
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:02,831
Trapping him in place
until sunlight shines upon him.

21
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:06,418
If beheading isn't enough
to kill him,

22
00:02:06,460 --> 00:02:08,503
there's only one option left.

23
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:13,258
You all must endure a battle
until the sun rises.

24
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:15,552
Yes, sir.

25
00:02:16,971 --> 00:02:19,848
If that is your wish,
then so be it, Master.

26
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,104
[KAGAYA] Thank goodness.

27
00:02:30,943 --> 00:02:34,362
Gyomei, after I have perished,

28
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:37,741
please do not let
any more of my children

29
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:39,284
be sent to their graves.

30
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:42,203
That is my wish.

31
00:02:57,344 --> 00:02:59,471
[♪ tense music playing]

32
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:01,765
[MUZAN] You think
you've driven me into a corner

33
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:03,182
with your little plan?

34
00:03:05,019 --> 00:03:08,563
But you are all about to be
going straight to hell!

35
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:10,732
Mark my words, Demon Slayers.

36
00:03:10,774 --> 00:03:14,402
I'll massacre every one of you
before sunrise!

37
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,696
[grunts angrily]

38
00:03:15,737 --> 00:03:17,280
[Nakime plucking biwa strings]

39
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:21,242
You're the only one
going to hell!

40
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:22,995
And you won't get away!

41
00:03:23,996 --> 00:03:26,081
Oh, is that so?

42
00:03:26,123 --> 00:03:28,207
Let's see you try.

43
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:31,170
Tanjiro Kamado!

44
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,838
[rumbling]

45
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,256
I will defeat you!

46
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:38,760
Muzan Kibutsuji!

47
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:43,974
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA
THE MOVIE: INFINITY CASTLE

48
00:03:45,184 --> 00:03:47,686
[♪ opening theme song playing]

49
00:03:51,023 --> 00:03:52,691
What is this place?

50
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:55,318
Everything's upside down.

51
00:03:56,528 --> 00:03:57,529
KILL

52
00:03:57,988 --> 00:04:00,407
Was all of this made using
the enemy's Blood Demon Art?

53
00:04:02,993 --> 00:04:05,204
I don't understand
what's happening,

54
00:04:05,244 --> 00:04:08,247
except that Ms. Tamayo
was restraining Muzan.

55
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:12,711
Even so, how long
can she keep that up?

56
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:15,254
[screaming]

57
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:17,007
[IGURO] Calm down, Kanroji.

58
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:18,759
[gasps] Yes!

59
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,761
[IGURO] Stay with me.

60
00:04:33,272 --> 00:04:34,273
[gasps]

61
00:04:37,485 --> 00:04:39,780
[Gyomei grunts]

62
00:04:54,044 --> 00:04:55,503
[effort grunts]

63
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:57,172
[effort grunts]

64
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:18,277
[TANJIRO] I need to reach Muzan
as soon as possible

65
00:05:18,317 --> 00:05:21,320
and defeat him
by whatever means!

66
00:05:25,117 --> 00:05:26,910
[grunts]

67
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:29,830
[♪ Gregorian chanting]

68
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:31,414
That's the bottom!

69
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:33,292
I'll be killed at this speed!

70
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,543
I'll use a move
to change directions.

71
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,754
Then find something
to grab on to.

72
00:05:37,796 --> 00:05:39,006
DESTROY

73
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,590
[♪ music intensifies]

74
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:45,220
It didn't work. I can't
break away from this free fall.

75
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,474
DESTROYER OF DEMONS

76
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:06,867
[♪ low tense music playing]

77
00:06:18,253 --> 00:06:19,838
[♪ music fades]

78
00:06:27,012 --> 00:06:29,139
[Tanjiro panting]

79
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:35,979
[GIYU] You all right?

80
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:39,941
Yes. Thanks for your help.

81
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,568
[sighs in relief]

82
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:43,320
You really saved--

83
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:47,991
Water Breathing, First Form:

84
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:49,659
Water Surface Slash.

85
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:52,954
[GIYU] Tanjiro!

86
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,584
[♪ intense music playing]

87
00:06:59,294 --> 00:07:01,255
[hinges creaking]

88
00:07:03,257 --> 00:07:04,549
[snarling]

89
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,561
[BOTH] Water Breathing.

90
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,397
[TANJIRO] Sixth Form.

91
00:07:18,437 --> 00:07:19,856
[GIYU] Third Form.

92
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,193
[TANJIRO] Whirlpool!

93
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:24,819
[GIYU] Flowing Dance.

94
00:07:30,449 --> 00:07:31,701
[Tanjiro groans nervously]

95
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:34,537
Mr. Giyu's amazing.

96
00:07:35,538 --> 00:07:37,999
He can tell exactly which move
I'm gonna use.

97
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:39,709
Then he follows up with one

98
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:42,212
that prevents
any kind of friendly fire.

99
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,714
He's unbelievable.

100
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:47,801
Just what's behind those eyes?

101
00:07:47,842 --> 00:07:49,970
[stifled whimpering]

102
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:52,055
If I'm not mistaken...

103
00:07:52,471 --> 00:07:53,723
this is the place

104
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,934
that Shinazugawa and Iguro
mentioned.

105
00:07:55,976 --> 00:07:58,019
[♪ Gregorian chanting]

106
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:00,688
Which means

107
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:03,817
Kibutsuji's plan
was to gather everyone here,

108
00:08:03,858 --> 00:08:06,445
then kill us all
in one fell swoop.

109
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:11,866
From here on out, we'll need
to be even more vigilant.

110
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,868
Right.

111
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,414
- Let's go.
- Right!

112
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:18,457
PITTER PATTER

113
00:08:18,497 --> 00:08:20,708
[♪ dramatic music playing]

114
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,473
[demons snarling]

115
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:43,106
[IGURO]
Serpent Breathing, Fifth Form:

116
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:52,324
Slithering Serpent!

117
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:58,621
You demon scum!
Stay away from Kanroji!

118
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:00,374
[squealing]

119
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:02,834
Mr. Iguro is so cool!

120
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:05,837
- Are you hurt?
- No, not at all!

121
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,797
- Then, let's go.
- Okay!

122
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:10,758
[Kanroji squealing]

123
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:21,144
[grunts]

124
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:29,777
Tokito!

125
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:32,322
[demons snarling]

126
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:38,953
[MUICHIRO] There's a whole lot
of demons, huh?

127
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:40,663
[GYOMEI] It would seem
they've been given

128
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:42,581
the strength of the Lower Ranks.

129
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:45,877
It's clear that they're being
used to try and exhaust us.

130
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,672
[metallic rattling]

131
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:50,882
[MUICHIRO] Hmm.

132
00:09:51,632 --> 00:09:53,051
What of the Master?

133
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:57,013
[GYOMEI] He has departed
from this world.

134
00:09:57,556 --> 00:10:00,058
It was a truly noble end.

135
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:02,477
Knowing him,

136
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:06,189
he never would have allowed
himself to be caught unawares.

137
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:09,067
Did he sacrifice himself?

138
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:13,863
[GYOMEI] Indeed. The Master
did not have much time left.

139
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,122
[MUICHIRO] Master.

140
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:31,672
Back when I was mortally wounded
by a demon

141
00:10:31,714 --> 00:10:33,758
and found myself
teetering on the edge

142
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,385
between life and death...

143
00:10:36,261 --> 00:10:38,138
...he stayed by my side.

144
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:43,768
He did the same
for every Corps member

145
00:10:43,810 --> 00:10:45,562
who was on the brink of death.

146
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,232
Like a father.

147
00:10:51,443 --> 00:10:53,236
[GYOMEI] Yes, I know.

148
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:56,781
[MUICHIRO] Muzan not only
took my brother from me,

149
00:10:57,324 --> 00:10:58,908
but our father as well.

150
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:01,453
That bastard.

151
00:11:01,495 --> 00:11:02,870
Damn him!

152
00:11:03,246 --> 00:11:05,457
I swear I'll make him suffer.

153
00:11:05,499 --> 00:11:07,584
I'll send him straight to hell!

154
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,337
[GYOMEI] You're not alone.

155
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:17,676
Trust me, we all feel the same.

156
00:11:22,432 --> 00:11:24,725
DESTROY

157
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,978
[SHINAZUGAWA]
Forgive me, Master.

158
00:11:28,605 --> 00:11:30,773
I couldn't protect you.

159
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:36,655
[distorted grunting]

160
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:39,574
[blade rasps]

161
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:44,745
[♪ upbeat music playing]

162
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:49,543
There's no end
to you lowlifes, huh?

163
00:11:50,126 --> 00:11:52,337
[demon cackling]

164
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:54,755
That's just fine by me.

165
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,757
I'll kill all of you!

166
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:06,184
[INOSUKE] Hyah!

167
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:09,646
Make way! I'm coming through!

168
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:11,898
[chuckles]

169
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:14,775
Whole lotta falling
happening here!

170
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:19,738
Hyah! Pretty rude to just
drop me in here out of nowhere!

171
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:22,367
Though I've been itching to see
how my training's paying off.

172
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:26,454
So with that in mind,
let's test it out on you chubs!

173
00:12:26,496 --> 00:12:27,788
[chuckles]

174
00:12:27,830 --> 00:12:30,083
Let's go!

175
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:32,751
[grunting]

176
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,423
[Genya panting]

177
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:39,551
Where am I?
The Demon Headquarters?

178
00:12:39,593 --> 00:12:41,094
Where are the others?

179
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,304
Big Brother.

180
00:12:44,347 --> 00:12:46,433
I hope you're safe, too.

181
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:52,813
[ZENITSU] I just heard a sound.

182
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,858
Could it be that
he's somewhere nearby?

183
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:59,487
[demons snarling]

184
00:13:01,406 --> 00:13:02,949
You'll regret this.

185
00:13:04,659 --> 00:13:06,369
I won't forgive you.

186
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:08,413
Not in a million years.

187
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:21,301
♪

188
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:34,355
[SHINOBU] I smell blood.

189
00:13:43,531 --> 00:13:45,158
What is this place?

190
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:54,793
[chomping]

191
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:03,217
[DEMON] Hmm?

192
00:14:04,511 --> 00:14:06,179
Oh, my. You're here.

193
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:07,846
UPPER TWO

194
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:09,848
Oh! And you're a girl, too!

195
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:14,103
What a young and tasty morsel
we have. [chuckles]

196
00:14:14,813 --> 00:14:18,274
I'll have to properly thank
Nakime for this later.

197
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:22,737
[Shinobu panting]

198
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:32,747
[whimpers softly]

199
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:35,500
[KANAE] Shinobu.

200
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:38,712
You must leave
the Demon Slayer Corps.

201
00:14:40,547 --> 00:14:43,383
I know that
you've trained really hard

202
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:46,386
and you're fighting
to make a difference.

203
00:14:46,885 --> 00:14:50,014
- [sobbing softly]
- But I don't think you'll...

204
00:14:50,682 --> 00:14:51,725
[sighs softly]

205
00:14:51,766 --> 00:14:53,434
[stifled sobbing]

206
00:14:55,687 --> 00:14:59,482
I want you to live the life
of a happy, normal girl.

207
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:03,236
To be able to see
your own hair turn gray.

208
00:15:04,738 --> 00:15:05,697
DESTROYER OF DEMONS

209
00:15:05,739 --> 00:15:08,324
Really... you've done enough.

210
00:15:08,366 --> 00:15:10,785
[SHINOBU] No! [sobbing]
Can't stop now!

211
00:15:10,827 --> 00:15:13,954
I will avenge you
if it's the last thing I do!

212
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:16,416
This demon! I need to know...

213
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,459
I have to know
what it looked like!

214
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:21,504
Please, Big Sister,
I'm begging you!

215
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:22,839
Tell me!

216
00:15:23,381 --> 00:15:27,468
I could never live a normal life
knowing someone did this to you!

217
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:29,262
[sobbing] Please!

218
00:15:30,597 --> 00:15:31,848
[sighs weakly]

219
00:15:33,932 --> 00:15:35,309
[KANAE] It was a demon

220
00:15:35,351 --> 00:15:38,271
with a blood-stained pattern
on his head.

221
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:43,109
[DEMON] I must say, it's very
nice to meet you, miss.

222
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:45,779
You may refer to me as Doma.

223
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:49,449
Ah, what a wonderful night!

224
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:54,078
[SHINOBU] Such a warm smile
and gentle voice.

225
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:57,832
There's a soft,
benevolent presence to him.

226
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,795
[woman weakly] Please, help me.

227
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,171
Please help me!

228
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:05,548
Shh.

229
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:07,926
Can't you see that
we're talking?

230
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,680
Hmm?

231
00:16:12,722 --> 00:16:14,181
[SHINOBU] Are you all right?

232
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:16,183
[DOMA] Wow!

233
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:19,228
That was fast.
Are you a Hashira?

234
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:21,272
[labored breathing]

235
00:16:22,022 --> 00:16:23,483
[squelching]

236
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:26,694
- [gasps]
- [♪ unsettling music playing]

237
00:16:27,821 --> 00:16:29,823
[DOMA]
Oh, don't worry about that.

238
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,783
You can just leave her
right there.

239
00:16:31,825 --> 00:16:34,118
I'll make
a proper meal of her later.

240
00:16:34,577 --> 00:16:35,620
[exhales]

241
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:38,915
And this demon...

242
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:41,125
the weapon he used,

243
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:44,337
it was a pair of sharp fans.

244
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:46,798
[metallic scraping]

245
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,384
As the founder
of the Eternal Paradise Faith,

246
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:52,386
it is my sworn duty to see that

247
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,931
all my followers
attain happiness.

248
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:58,016
I'll be sure
to consume her completely.

249
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:01,312
[SHINOBU] There's no doubt.

250
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:03,898
This is the demon
who killed my sister.

251
00:17:05,358 --> 00:17:07,276
Attaining happiness?

252
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:08,945
For who exactly?

253
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:12,365
This girl was horrified,
crying out for help.

254
00:17:12,866 --> 00:17:14,701
- And that's why I saved her.
- [fans scraping]

255
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:18,162
Her suffering
has come to an end.

256
00:17:18,496 --> 00:17:20,038
No more pain.

257
00:17:20,373 --> 00:17:21,708
No more fear.

258
00:17:22,709 --> 00:17:24,919
Everyone is afraid of death.

259
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:27,922
So I help them
by consuming them.

260
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:33,135
This way, they get to live on
within me for all eternity.

261
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:35,930
I take in their entire being.

262
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:38,182
Blood. Desires.

263
00:17:38,725 --> 00:17:40,434
Even the last bit of their sinew

264
00:17:40,935 --> 00:17:43,730
- and help their souls transcend.
- [♪ unsettling music playing]

265
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:46,399
What you're spouting
is sheer nonsense.

266
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:48,860
And to say it with such glee...

267
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:51,278
You truly make me sick!

268
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,280
Aw.

269
00:17:53,907 --> 00:17:57,577
I can't believe you'd say that
after we'd only just met.

270
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:59,286
Oh, I see.

271
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:01,581
Oh, you poor thing.

272
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:04,291
Did something unfortunate
happen?

273
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,877
Let's hear it.

274
00:18:05,919 --> 00:18:07,378
Go on, tell me.

275
00:18:08,713 --> 00:18:11,883
"Unfortunate" doesn't begin
to describe it!

276
00:18:11,925 --> 00:18:15,053
You are the one who killed
my big sister, weren't you?

277
00:18:15,093 --> 00:18:18,096
Does the haori I'm wearing
mean nothing to you?!

278
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:19,390
Huh?

279
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:22,018
♪

280
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:25,563
[blade rasps]

281
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:31,027
[flesh squelching]

282
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:32,862
[DOMA] That's right.

283
00:18:32,946 --> 00:18:36,032
It belonged to the girl
who used Flower Breathing.

284
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:38,910
Such a sweet, gentle child.

285
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,455
The sun came up
and cut our time short.

286
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:43,873
I remember.

287
00:18:43,915 --> 00:18:46,500
It's a shame I didn't get-- Her.

288
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:49,587
[SHINOBU] Insect Breathing,

289
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:52,381
Dance of the Bee Sting:
True Flutter.

290
00:18:53,758 --> 00:18:55,593
A marvelous thrust.

291
00:18:55,635 --> 00:18:57,553
I hardly even saw it.

292
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:01,265
Blood Demon Art:

293
00:19:02,349 --> 00:19:04,518
Frozen Lotus.

294
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:07,063
[Shinobu shivering] So cold.

295
00:19:07,105 --> 00:19:09,440
It feels like my lungs
are bursting.

296
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:11,651
[DOMA] Hmm.

297
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:13,861
Look at that. You are fast.

298
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,489
Unfortunately for you,

299
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:19,659
those thrusts aren't enough
to kill a demon.

300
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:20,910
[slurps]

301
00:19:21,661 --> 00:19:22,787
[rattling]

302
00:19:22,829 --> 00:19:24,538
Aim for here.

303
00:19:25,039 --> 00:19:27,625
You need to chop off my head.

304
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:29,669
DESTROY

305
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:32,588
My thrusts alone
may not be enough,

306
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:34,090
but what of this?

307
00:19:34,132 --> 00:19:36,216
- [clanks]
- [ratchets, clicks]

308
00:19:37,175 --> 00:19:38,176
[Doma groans]

309
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,805
[SHINOBU] Time to see
whether this toxin

310
00:19:40,847 --> 00:19:42,598
works on an Upper Rank.

311
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:48,938
Sister, lend me
your strength, please.

312
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:50,982
[retches]

313
00:19:51,024 --> 00:19:52,900
[straining] This poison.

314
00:19:52,942 --> 00:19:56,112
It's clearly far stronger
than the strain you used

315
00:19:56,154 --> 00:19:58,948
up on Rui's mountain. [wheezing]

316
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:01,701
[SHINOBU] So they did
exchange information.

317
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:04,537
This is the drawback
to using poison.

318
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:08,582
[DOMA] He told me that
you've been changing concoction

319
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:11,919
for each demon you face.
[straining]

320
00:20:11,961 --> 00:20:14,296
- [coughs, retches]
- [blood splatters]

321
00:20:15,006 --> 00:20:16,757
[wheezing]

322
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:20,928
Oh, my.

323
00:20:20,970 --> 00:20:25,391
It would seem that I've already
neutralized all of your poison.

324
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:26,726
How rude of me.

325
00:20:26,767 --> 00:20:30,063
And after you'd made it
just for me.

326
00:20:30,563 --> 00:20:32,481
That sword of yours,

327
00:20:33,024 --> 00:20:36,276
it makes quite an interesting
sound when you sheathe it.

328
00:20:37,028 --> 00:20:40,364
Is that where you change
what poison you use?

329
00:20:40,406 --> 00:20:43,201
Yay! This is fun!

330
00:20:44,035 --> 00:20:46,913
Who knew being poisoned
was so invigorating?

331
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:48,706
It's almost addictive.

332
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:51,209
What will the next formula
be like? [chuckles]

333
00:20:51,249 --> 00:20:53,627
Come on, let's give it a try.

334
00:20:55,253 --> 00:20:57,255
- [swishing]
- [rattling]

335
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,301
Very well then,

336
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:03,429
I'll oblige.

337
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:04,513
See...

338
00:21:08,226 --> 00:21:11,020
...I'd already anticipated
this would happen.

339
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,481
[Doma chuckling]
Is your next batch set?

340
00:21:15,024 --> 00:21:16,859
I'm ready whenever you are.

341
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:24,117
I know I just said
to give it a try...

342
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:28,579
...but you could at least
change up your offense.

343
00:21:30,706 --> 00:21:32,625
- [metallic clanking]
- [Doma chuckles]

344
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,087
- [continues chuckling]
- [grunts]

345
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:45,012
What's this?

346
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:47,514
You seem to be
slower than earlier.

347
00:21:47,556 --> 00:21:49,058
So sad.

348
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:52,519
[SHINOBU] Insect Breathing,
Dance of the Horsefly:

349
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:54,563
Enticing Slash!

350
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:05,283
Oh, my.
You were able to land a hit.

351
00:22:05,323 --> 00:22:08,161
The way you got through
all my defenses,

352
00:22:08,202 --> 00:22:09,662
it's amazing!

353
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:11,205
I'm truly impressed.

354
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:14,250
It's almost enough
to bring a tear to my eye.

355
00:22:14,292 --> 00:22:16,502
Come on,
what are you waiting for?

356
00:22:16,543 --> 00:22:20,506
Hurry up and attack me again,
before I stop the poison.

357
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:23,176
Please? You're doing so well.

358
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:25,011
Maybe the next attack kills me.

359
00:22:25,052 --> 00:22:26,095
[disgruntled sigh]

360
00:22:29,932 --> 00:22:33,477
[laughs] Yes! That's the spirit!

361
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,899
Ever since I was a child,

362
00:22:38,941 --> 00:22:40,943
I was kind and clever.

363
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:43,988
I always helped those
who were in need

364
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:46,490
and led them
to the path of happiness.

365
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:49,327
It was my duty after all.

366
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:53,789
[DOMA'S FATHER] His eyes
have the colors of a rainbow.

367
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:57,918
And this gray hair
is proof of his innocence.

368
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:00,880
This child is truly special.

369
00:23:01,379 --> 00:23:04,091
Surely he can hear
the voices of the gods.

370
00:23:04,133 --> 00:23:06,010
[♪ slow piano notes playing]

371
00:23:06,052 --> 00:23:09,763
[DOMA] My parents were
hopelessly naive simpletons.

372
00:23:10,348 --> 00:23:11,891
You'd have to be

373
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:15,769
in order to found a religion
like the Eternal Paradise Faith.

374
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:18,314
I pitied them,

375
00:23:18,356 --> 00:23:21,901
so I always played along
with their make-believe ideas.

376
00:23:23,027 --> 00:23:25,946
I never once heard
the voice of the gods.

377
00:23:26,864 --> 00:23:29,575
At first, I didn't know
how to deal

378
00:23:29,616 --> 00:23:33,162
with the hordes of people
worshiping and praying to me.

379
00:23:34,121 --> 00:23:37,166
Seeing these grown-ups
come crying to a child

380
00:23:37,208 --> 00:23:40,294
saying they were suffering,
pleading for help,

381
00:23:40,336 --> 00:23:43,714
made me worry
if they were sick in the head.

382
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:48,677
After nearly putting me to sleep
with their personal stories,

383
00:23:48,719 --> 00:23:50,388
they would bow to me,

384
00:23:50,428 --> 00:23:53,057
asking to be guided to paradise.

385
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:54,850
I cried.

386
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:58,229
"You poor things," I thought.

387
00:23:58,729 --> 00:24:00,773
"Paradise doesn't even exist.

388
00:24:01,439 --> 00:24:05,569
It's just a fairy tale
concocted by deluded humans.

389
00:24:06,653 --> 00:24:09,156
There are no gods or Buddhas."

390
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:12,285
These people
had lived for decades,

391
00:24:12,326 --> 00:24:15,495
yet they still couldn't grasp
that simple truth.

392
00:24:16,038 --> 00:24:19,166
When you die,
you return to nothingness.

393
00:24:19,208 --> 00:24:21,335
All feeling ceases.

394
00:24:22,086 --> 00:24:23,796
Your heart stops.

395
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:25,589
Your brain stops.

396
00:24:25,631 --> 00:24:27,925
You rot and return to the earth.

397
00:24:28,426 --> 00:24:31,595
Such is the fate
of every living creature.

398
00:24:33,764 --> 00:24:37,017
To be too foolish
to accept reality,

399
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:39,812
what a hard life that must be.

400
00:24:40,813 --> 00:24:44,024
I want to bring happiness
to these pitiful people.

401
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:46,193
I want to save them.

402
00:24:47,069 --> 00:24:51,449
I truly believe
that is my purpose here.

403
00:24:55,453 --> 00:24:56,412
[squelches]

404
00:24:56,454 --> 00:24:57,579
[blade rasps]

405
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:00,291
- Aw. Still nothing.
- [metallic rattling]

406
00:25:00,333 --> 00:25:02,001
And that was number five.

407
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:03,543
What will you do?

408
00:25:04,086 --> 00:25:06,546
The toxin's
getting less effective.

409
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:09,716
How many more times
do you think you can adapt it?

410
00:25:10,301 --> 00:25:12,636
- Oh! Are you out of breath now?
- [panting]

411
00:25:13,179 --> 00:25:14,805
Look at all that sweat.

412
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:16,182
Are you all right?

413
00:25:16,807 --> 00:25:19,852
[SHINOBU] So, this is the power
of an Upper Rank.

414
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,604
None of my poisons are working.

415
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:26,692
He's adapting too fast
to keep up with.

416
00:25:28,861 --> 00:25:31,238
Your alveoli must be dead now.

417
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:33,366
[crystals tinkling]

418
00:25:33,407 --> 00:25:34,783
Painful.

419
00:25:34,825 --> 00:25:38,162
You did breathe it in,
my Blood Demon Art.

420
00:25:40,331 --> 00:25:43,167
[SHINOBU] He turns
his frozen blood into mist

421
00:25:43,209 --> 00:25:45,543
and disperses it with his fans.

422
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:48,672
Even breathing around him
is dangerous now.

423
00:25:54,428 --> 00:25:55,553
[clangs]

424
00:25:55,595 --> 00:25:56,638
[ratchets, clicks]

425
00:25:57,097 --> 00:26:00,684
This time, I'll increase
the dose with multiple strikes!

426
00:26:01,519 --> 00:26:04,730
Insect Breathing,
Dance of the Dragonfly:

427
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:06,399
♪

428
00:26:11,569 --> 00:26:13,864
Compound Eye Hexagon!

429
00:26:16,409 --> 00:26:17,784
I can't believe it!

430
00:26:17,826 --> 00:26:19,786
Such blazing speed!

431
00:26:19,828 --> 00:26:23,332
You might be the fastest Hashira
I've ever met.

432
00:26:25,709 --> 00:26:27,127
- [blood squelches]
- [gasps]

433
00:26:27,627 --> 00:26:30,047
[SHINOBU] He... got me.

434
00:26:30,089 --> 00:26:31,340
[grunts]

435
00:26:31,382 --> 00:26:33,133
Forget the poison.

436
00:26:33,175 --> 00:26:35,344
Why not try to decapitate me?

437
00:26:35,886 --> 00:26:38,305
With your speed,
you might have won.

438
00:26:39,265 --> 00:26:41,475
[laughs sarcastically]
Maybe not.

439
00:26:41,517 --> 00:26:43,727
I mean, you are small.

440
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:45,771
[gasps, breathing shakily]

441
00:26:47,565 --> 00:26:50,650
[SHINOBU] Why are my hands
so small? I wonder.

442
00:26:52,403 --> 00:26:55,573
How come I was never able
to grow taller?

443
00:26:57,491 --> 00:27:00,327
If my stature
were just a little bigger,

444
00:27:00,786 --> 00:27:04,206
could I have been able to behead
and defeat a demon?

445
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,543
The longer
your arms and legs are,

446
00:27:07,585 --> 00:27:09,420
the more muscles you have,

447
00:27:09,462 --> 00:27:12,047
which means more strength
in your attacks.

448
00:27:13,507 --> 00:27:15,175
[♪ tender music playing]

449
00:27:15,217 --> 00:27:18,137
My sister
was also of small frame,

450
00:27:18,178 --> 00:27:20,055
but she was taller than I.

451
00:27:22,182 --> 00:27:24,810
How I envy Mr. Himejima.

452
00:27:25,394 --> 00:27:27,896
Seeing someone like him
come to the rescue

453
00:27:27,938 --> 00:27:29,731
would give anyone relief.

454
00:27:33,569 --> 00:27:36,696
I know what my sister
really wanted to say,

455
00:27:37,406 --> 00:27:39,492
but didn't have the heart to.

456
00:27:42,911 --> 00:27:44,413
[DOMA] Oh, no!

457
00:27:44,455 --> 00:27:46,499
Have our games come to an end?

458
00:27:46,873 --> 00:27:48,417
That's too bad.

459
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:51,420
[metallic rattling]

460
00:27:52,004 --> 00:27:55,090
[SHINOBU] "I don't think
you'll win against that demon."

461
00:27:55,633 --> 00:27:57,884
[voice breaking] That's what
you were going to say.

462
00:27:57,926 --> 00:28:00,387
But you stopped yourself,
didn't you?

463
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:02,680
[KANAE] Pull yourself together.

464
00:28:08,312 --> 00:28:10,272
This is no time for tears.

465
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:12,983
[SHINOBU] Sister.

466
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:15,152
[KANAE] Stand up.

467
00:28:15,194 --> 00:28:18,614
[SHINOBU] I can't.
I've lost so much blood.

468
00:28:18,656 --> 00:28:21,950
My left lung is punctured
and I can't even breathe.

469
00:28:22,493 --> 00:28:24,161
You can and you will.

470
00:28:24,744 --> 00:28:28,207
Stand up.
You are a Hashira, Shinobu.

471
00:28:28,624 --> 00:28:30,417
[grunting softly]

472
00:28:31,043 --> 00:28:34,004
If you've made up your mind
to defeat him, then do so.

473
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:35,713
No excuses.

474
00:28:37,090 --> 00:28:39,552
Win by whatever means you can.

475
00:28:40,093 --> 00:28:42,179
Remember your promise,

476
00:28:42,221 --> 00:28:43,889
to me and Kanao.

477
00:28:46,392 --> 00:28:47,643
[SHINOBU] Kanao.

478
00:28:50,646 --> 00:28:52,523
[DOMA] Forgive me.

479
00:28:52,565 --> 00:28:54,983
You must be suffering right now.

480
00:28:55,025 --> 00:28:57,152
[whimpering softly]

481
00:28:58,736 --> 00:28:59,905
[gasps]

482
00:28:59,946 --> 00:29:02,032
I know that you have it in you.

483
00:29:02,408 --> 00:29:03,783
Do your best.

484
00:29:04,742 --> 00:29:06,662
- Huh?
- [metallic rattling]

485
00:29:07,829 --> 00:29:08,914
[quivers]

486
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:14,712
Wait. Are you... standing up?
[exclaims in amazement]

487
00:29:14,752 --> 00:29:16,338
Scary.

488
00:29:16,380 --> 00:29:18,674
Are you actually a human?

489
00:29:18,716 --> 00:29:22,802
I slashed your collarbone,
your lungs, and your ribs.

490
00:29:23,929 --> 00:29:25,972
At your diminutive size

491
00:29:26,014 --> 00:29:28,308
and the amount of blood
you've lost,

492
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:30,394
how are you not dead right now?

493
00:29:30,436 --> 00:29:31,478
[coughs]

494
00:29:31,520 --> 00:29:33,063
See? Right there.

495
00:29:33,105 --> 00:29:36,066
There clearly is blood
gurgling in your lungs.

496
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:38,694
The pain must be unimaginable.

497
00:29:39,152 --> 00:29:41,905
Surrender and I'll put an end
to your suffering.

498
00:29:41,947 --> 00:29:43,240
It'll be quick.

499
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:46,076
It's too late for you.

500
00:29:46,118 --> 00:29:47,869
So, just let go.

501
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:50,623
[SHINOBU] I'll make a go
for his neck this time

502
00:29:50,664 --> 00:29:54,084
and put everything I have left
into this strike!

503
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:58,505
Insect Breathing,
Dance of the Centipede.

504
00:29:59,005 --> 00:30:00,132
[DOMA] Hmm?

505
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,175
[SHINOBU]
Hundred-Legged Zigzag.

506
00:30:03,009 --> 00:30:04,886
[♪ dramatic music playing]

507
00:30:06,972 --> 00:30:08,098
[groans]

508
00:30:25,115 --> 00:30:27,951
[DOMA] It feels like
she's everywhere at once.

509
00:30:28,786 --> 00:30:31,288
Just her movement
destroyed the bridge.

510
00:30:32,122 --> 00:30:33,915
[squeaking]

511
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:36,251
So fast. I can't follow her.

512
00:30:37,127 --> 00:30:38,337
[impact grunts]

513
00:30:42,591 --> 00:30:43,634
From below?

514
00:30:43,676 --> 00:30:44,926
[gasps]

515
00:30:47,721 --> 00:30:49,222
[Shinobu grunts]

516
00:30:52,892 --> 00:30:55,979
- [glass shatters]
- [♪ music swells, fades]

517
00:30:57,606 --> 00:30:59,274
[SHINOBU]
Back when I was a child...

518
00:31:00,776 --> 00:31:02,778
...I thought of happiness
like a road,

519
00:31:02,820 --> 00:31:05,322
one that stretched on
into the distance

520
00:31:05,364 --> 00:31:07,449
with no end in sight.

521
00:31:07,491 --> 00:31:09,075
[laughter]

522
00:31:09,117 --> 00:31:10,452
[blood splatters]

523
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:13,747
It wasn't until it was destroyed

524
00:31:13,789 --> 00:31:15,915
that I finally realized

525
00:31:15,957 --> 00:31:19,919
the road beneath my feet
was but a thin sheet of glass.

526
00:31:19,961 --> 00:31:22,339
♪

527
00:31:22,381 --> 00:31:26,968
However, some haven't had
the glass broken yet.

528
00:31:27,803 --> 00:31:32,307
All I wanted after being saved
was to become stronger...

529
00:31:33,308 --> 00:31:37,479
...so that some day,
I could protect those people.

530
00:31:38,896 --> 00:31:42,735
So... we made a promise.

531
00:31:44,944 --> 00:31:50,450
To vanquish the demons
as many as we could, together.

532
00:31:51,117 --> 00:31:52,703
[♪ poignant music playing]

533
00:31:53,579 --> 00:31:56,456
In hopes that the pain
we suffered

534
00:31:56,498 --> 00:31:59,084
would never be felt by another.

535
00:32:07,634 --> 00:32:09,469
Even if I'm weak...

536
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:16,309
...even if I can't
decapitate demons,

537
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:18,604
if I can take down just one,

538
00:32:18,645 --> 00:32:20,898
I can save dozens of lives.

539
00:32:20,938 --> 00:32:23,024
And if that demon's
an Upper Rank,

540
00:32:23,692 --> 00:32:25,943
it could mean saving hundreds.

541
00:32:27,529 --> 00:32:30,741
It's not a matter
of can or cannot.

542
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:33,786
This is something I have to do.

543
00:32:38,998 --> 00:32:40,542
Are you angry?

544
00:32:42,502 --> 00:32:46,005
[SHINOBU] Yes.
I am angry, Tanjiro.

545
00:32:46,047 --> 00:32:47,424
I'm furious.

546
00:32:48,174 --> 00:32:49,342
In fact...

547
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:52,679
...I'm always angry.

548
00:32:52,721 --> 00:32:54,556
How could I not be?

549
00:32:56,850 --> 00:32:58,852
My parents were killed.

550
00:33:00,270 --> 00:33:02,689
My older sister was killed.

551
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:07,235
My Tsuguko, other than Kanao,
were killed.

552
00:33:08,236 --> 00:33:10,071
And those poor girls.

553
00:33:10,739 --> 00:33:12,407
If it weren't for the demons...

554
00:33:12,908 --> 00:33:15,828
If it weren't for the demons
that killed their loved ones,

555
00:33:16,495 --> 00:33:19,623
they'd be living happily
with their families.

556
00:33:21,124 --> 00:33:22,125
[♪ discordant music playing]

557
00:33:22,167 --> 00:33:25,337
It's all so infuriating!

558
00:33:25,378 --> 00:33:27,756
Stop messing with me, damn it!

559
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:32,344
Why the hell isn't my poison
working on this prick?

560
00:33:33,136 --> 00:33:34,930
You bastard!

561
00:33:34,972 --> 00:33:36,348
[exhales]

562
00:33:36,389 --> 00:33:38,475
[ice crackling]

563
00:33:46,149 --> 00:33:48,777
I'm moved! You did your best!

564
00:33:48,819 --> 00:33:51,070
Even though you're so weak.

565
00:33:51,112 --> 00:33:53,239
You must have worked
so incredibly hard

566
00:33:53,281 --> 00:33:55,325
to get to this point. [sobbing]

567
00:33:55,367 --> 00:33:57,494
You're weaker than your sister,

568
00:33:57,536 --> 00:33:59,997
and yet, you somehow
outlived her.

569
00:34:00,497 --> 00:34:03,583
[sniffles] It's a miracle
you survived this long.

570
00:34:03,625 --> 00:34:04,751
[body cracking]

571
00:34:04,793 --> 00:34:06,211
[coughs]

572
00:34:06,252 --> 00:34:07,546
Even when hope is gone,

573
00:34:07,587 --> 00:34:10,047
humans always fight
to the bitter end.

574
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:12,509
Humans are so foolish.

575
00:34:12,551 --> 00:34:15,178
But that's what makes them
so beautiful.

576
00:34:16,053 --> 00:34:18,682
I deem you worthy
of becoming part of me.

577
00:34:19,182 --> 00:34:22,268
[sobbing] You and I
shall share eternity!

578
00:34:25,605 --> 00:34:27,566
Do you have any last words?

579
00:34:28,149 --> 00:34:29,401
I'm listening.

580
00:34:34,197 --> 00:34:37,034
Rot in hell, you bastard!

581
00:34:41,038 --> 00:34:43,331
[exclaims in horror] Master!

582
00:34:46,334 --> 00:34:47,753
[bones crunching]

583
00:34:48,587 --> 00:34:51,548
[exclaims in anguish]

584
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:53,717
[bones crunching]

585
00:34:59,347 --> 00:35:00,724
[clangs]

586
00:35:03,602 --> 00:35:05,186
[clatters]

587
00:35:05,896 --> 00:35:07,522
[quivering]

588
00:35:08,356 --> 00:35:11,317
[screaming in agony]

589
00:35:12,027 --> 00:35:14,029
♪

590
00:35:15,030 --> 00:35:17,741
[ZENITSU] I can't shake
the feeling he's here.

591
00:35:17,783 --> 00:35:19,158
He must be.

592
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:22,203
He's got a score to settle
with me, too.

593
00:35:29,502 --> 00:35:30,879
The people we love,

594
00:35:30,921 --> 00:35:34,382
the people we hold dear
are so precious.

595
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:37,427
We take for granted
that they'll always be there.

596
00:35:37,886 --> 00:35:41,848
However, that's just
a selfish delusion.

597
00:35:41,890 --> 00:35:43,809
Flower Breathing...

598
00:35:44,309 --> 00:35:46,436
[ZENITSU] Because the thought
of living without them

599
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:48,396
is simply unbearable.

600
00:35:48,438 --> 00:35:49,689
...Fourth Form:

601
00:35:50,356 --> 00:35:52,567
Crimson Hanagoromo!

602
00:35:52,609 --> 00:35:54,402
[shatters]

603
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:56,655
[grunts]

604
00:35:59,282 --> 00:36:02,327
[DOMA] Wow!
You nearly got me there.

605
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:08,667
[ZENITSU] "They'll always be
alive and close by."

606
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:12,462
It's a naive thought, I know,

607
00:36:13,046 --> 00:36:14,923
but we all wanna believe it.

608
00:36:18,135 --> 00:36:21,554
Would you mind holding off
your attacks for just a second?

609
00:36:21,596 --> 00:36:24,641
- I'm trying to absorb her.
- [flesh squelching]

610
00:36:27,435 --> 00:36:29,562
[seething]

611
00:36:32,065 --> 00:36:33,566
[DOMA] How strange.

612
00:36:33,608 --> 00:36:36,277
You're not taking the bait,
are you?

613
00:36:36,945 --> 00:36:38,989
What she did earlier,

614
00:36:39,031 --> 00:36:41,616
that motion she made
with her fingers.

615
00:36:42,075 --> 00:36:45,037
Was that her warning you
of my powers?

616
00:36:45,537 --> 00:36:48,373
I'm impressed she thought
to do that so quickly.

617
00:36:48,832 --> 00:36:50,583
Good job you did it.

618
00:36:51,126 --> 00:36:53,003
Too bad it doesn't matter.

619
00:36:53,503 --> 00:36:55,505
- [flesh squelching]
- [clatters]

620
00:36:55,547 --> 00:36:58,717
Well, in case
you were wondering,

621
00:36:59,258 --> 00:37:02,428
your master was tastier
than I imagined.

622
00:37:02,470 --> 00:37:03,722
[slurps]

623
00:37:04,263 --> 00:37:06,016
And now, you're here.

624
00:37:06,058 --> 00:37:09,477
It's just one feast
after another, it seems.

625
00:37:10,269 --> 00:37:13,398
Ah, this truly is...

626
00:37:13,982 --> 00:37:16,442
a wonderful night.

627
00:37:17,027 --> 00:37:20,197
[seething]

628
00:37:29,789 --> 00:37:31,124
You can't hide.

629
00:37:31,708 --> 00:37:33,043
Come out.

630
00:37:33,877 --> 00:37:36,253
Have some dignity and face me.

631
00:37:38,798 --> 00:37:41,676
[DEMON] Sounds like someone
ought to teach you some manners.

632
00:37:41,718 --> 00:37:43,970
Did you forget
that I'm your senior?

633
00:37:44,554 --> 00:37:48,016
You look a little stronger
than the last time I saw ya.

634
00:37:48,725 --> 00:37:52,687
It's too bad you still reek
of being a pathetic weakling.

635
00:37:55,314 --> 00:37:56,273
[clatters]

636
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:57,650
UPPER SIX

637
00:37:57,692 --> 00:38:01,905
It's been a while,
hasn't it... Zenitsu?

638
00:38:01,947 --> 00:38:03,740
[chuckles]

639
00:38:04,699 --> 00:38:06,118
[ZENITSU] Kaigaku.

640
00:38:06,159 --> 00:38:08,536
You don't get my respect.

641
00:38:08,912 --> 00:38:10,455
You're a demon.

642
00:38:10,496 --> 00:38:12,373
You'll be treated as such.

643
00:38:20,132 --> 00:38:21,174
[Nakime plucking biwa strings]

644
00:38:21,216 --> 00:38:22,634
- [rumbles]
- [Tanjiro gasps]

645
00:38:22,675 --> 00:38:23,718
[grunts]

646
00:38:25,762 --> 00:38:28,265
Water Breathing, Ninth Form:

647
00:38:30,058 --> 00:38:32,435
Splashing Water Flow, Turbulent!

648
00:38:33,519 --> 00:38:34,854
[grunts]

649
00:38:34,896 --> 00:38:36,106
Stay focused!

650
00:38:36,148 --> 00:38:37,398
All right!

651
00:38:38,608 --> 00:38:40,693
This place is insane.

652
00:38:40,735 --> 00:38:43,320
The building keeps shifting
and rearranging itself

653
00:38:43,362 --> 00:38:45,031
as if it's alive.

654
00:38:45,073 --> 00:38:47,909
I can tell that
it's trying to separate us.

655
00:38:48,994 --> 00:38:51,663
We have to regroup
with the other Corps members

656
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:54,082
and stay together
till we reach Muzan!

657
00:38:57,961 --> 00:38:59,879
[cawing]

658
00:39:00,297 --> 00:39:02,007
[cawing]

659
00:39:02,048 --> 00:39:03,675
Attention!

660
00:39:03,716 --> 00:39:05,927
Shinobu Kocho is dead!

661
00:39:06,594 --> 00:39:09,014
She fought valiantly
against Upper Two

662
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:10,765
but was defeated!

663
00:39:17,981 --> 00:39:20,233
- [gasps]
- [muted silence]

664
00:39:23,653 --> 00:39:25,822
[♪ poignant music playing]

665
00:39:27,199 --> 00:39:29,326
[inaudible laughter]

666
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:44,257
[seething]

667
00:39:47,844 --> 00:39:49,762
[cawing]

668
00:39:52,015 --> 00:39:53,308
[GIYU] Strange.

669
00:39:53,350 --> 00:39:55,894
There's a piece of paper
wrapped around its neck.

670
00:39:56,393 --> 00:39:58,230
How are the crows already here?

671
00:39:59,231 --> 00:40:02,025
[♪ epic dramatic music playing]

672
00:40:02,692 --> 00:40:04,485
Shinobu is dead,

673
00:40:04,527 --> 00:40:06,612
but we must push forward.

674
00:40:06,988 --> 00:40:09,574
Think only of what must be done
for victory.

675
00:40:10,075 --> 00:40:11,201
[KUINA, KANATA] Right.

676
00:40:13,494 --> 00:40:14,871
And what about the others?

677
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:17,290
I need reports
on their whereabouts.

678
00:40:18,791 --> 00:40:20,501
[KANATA]
Center of the 40th vertical

679
00:40:20,543 --> 00:40:22,379
and 12th horizontal levels.

680
00:40:22,419 --> 00:40:24,047
[fight grunts]

681
00:40:24,089 --> 00:40:26,049
The Corps members
are fighting off

682
00:40:26,091 --> 00:40:29,010
what appears to be
at least ten demons.

683
00:40:30,803 --> 00:40:34,140
[fight grunts]

684
00:40:35,892 --> 00:40:38,895
However, more than 30 demons
are moving in their direction

685
00:40:38,937 --> 00:40:40,397
from behind the walls.

686
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:48,654
[KIRIYA]
Using Mr. Yushiro's eyes,

687
00:40:48,696 --> 00:40:51,199
we're able to see
Blood Demon Arts,

688
00:40:51,241 --> 00:40:54,451
something that isn't possible
to do with the human eye.

689
00:40:55,370 --> 00:40:57,580
Each red light
is a Blood Demon Art.

690
00:40:57,622 --> 00:41:00,917
The more intense they glow,
the more potent their power.

691
00:41:01,793 --> 00:41:04,421
In this place, the entire area,

692
00:41:04,461 --> 00:41:07,757
buildings and all, must also be
a Blood Demon Art.

693
00:41:08,507 --> 00:41:11,510
There's seemingly
no end in sight to it.

694
00:41:13,930 --> 00:41:15,932
What incredible power!

695
00:41:17,267 --> 00:41:18,768
A demon labyrinth

696
00:41:18,810 --> 00:41:21,271
with the ability
to branch out endlessly.

697
00:41:24,565 --> 00:41:26,359
And here we lie at its center,

698
00:41:26,401 --> 00:41:29,279
trapped within the walls
of this infinite castle.

699
00:41:29,988 --> 00:41:31,572
[KAKUSHI 1] This one's finished.

700
00:41:33,450 --> 00:41:36,828
[KIRIYA] However, it's not as if
we've been caught off guard.

701
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:37,829
KAKUSHI

702
00:41:38,121 --> 00:41:41,291
My father prepared
for this day meticulously.

703
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:44,210
With Gyomei's cooperation,

704
00:41:44,252 --> 00:41:46,254
he had the Hashira
within arm's reach

705
00:41:46,296 --> 00:41:47,839
to mobilize at any time.

706
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:50,842
To prevent the Corps members
from being isolated,

707
00:41:50,883 --> 00:41:53,636
he sent the Kasugai Crows
to gather them into groups

708
00:41:53,678 --> 00:41:54,637
and waited.

709
00:41:55,763 --> 00:41:59,351
He enlisted the aid
of Ms. Tamayo and Mr. Yushiro.

710
00:41:59,392 --> 00:42:00,601
And finally,

711
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:03,520
to ensure that
their plan would succeed,

712
00:42:04,022 --> 00:42:06,607
my sisters and our parents

713
00:42:07,108 --> 00:42:09,277
readily sacrificed their lives.

714
00:42:12,613 --> 00:42:14,115
We cannot lose,

715
00:42:14,657 --> 00:42:16,075
no matter what!

716
00:42:19,287 --> 00:42:21,914
[♪ music intensifies]

717
00:42:22,581 --> 00:42:24,376
Amongst the Blood Demon Arts,

718
00:42:24,417 --> 00:42:27,670
there are five traces of power
that tower over the rest

719
00:42:27,712 --> 00:42:29,714
as if flaunting their strength.

720
00:42:30,340 --> 00:42:32,717
These must be Upper Ranks.

721
00:42:33,426 --> 00:42:34,969
One of them is at the same spot

722
00:42:35,011 --> 00:42:37,305
where Shinobu
was last seen fighting.

723
00:42:37,889 --> 00:42:39,307
Found another!

724
00:42:39,391 --> 00:42:42,352
Upper Six and Zenitsu have just
encountered each other!

725
00:42:42,394 --> 00:42:43,978
An Upper Rank!

726
00:42:44,020 --> 00:42:45,188
Is he alone?

727
00:42:45,230 --> 00:42:47,773
[KUINA] He is.
It looks to be a one-on-one!

728
00:42:47,815 --> 00:42:50,693
[KIRIYA] A Hinoe can't beat
an Upper Rank by themself.

729
00:42:50,735 --> 00:42:51,861
Send backup!

730
00:42:57,492 --> 00:42:58,743
[KAIGAKU] Hmm.

731
00:42:58,784 --> 00:43:00,870
What, you're frozen in fear?

732
00:43:00,912 --> 00:43:02,997
Guess some things never change.

733
00:43:03,039 --> 00:43:05,291
Once a coward, always a coward.

734
00:43:06,292 --> 00:43:08,336
Did you ever become a Hashira?

735
00:43:08,378 --> 00:43:10,422
[scoffs] Guess not.

736
00:43:10,463 --> 00:43:11,756
That's too bad.

737
00:43:12,257 --> 00:43:16,428
Got any new techniques?
Or still just First Form?

738
00:43:17,470 --> 00:43:19,097
For an Upper Rank bottom feeder

739
00:43:19,138 --> 00:43:21,266
who's nothing more
than a spare blade,

740
00:43:21,307 --> 00:43:23,560
you're sure acting
awfully proud.

741
00:43:24,436 --> 00:43:27,272
[Kaigaku sarcastically]
Wow! [laughs]

742
00:43:27,313 --> 00:43:30,442
Who taught you to talk
like that? New friends?

743
00:43:30,942 --> 00:43:33,278
[ZENITSU] Why the hell
did you become a demon?

744
00:43:33,778 --> 00:43:35,947
[laughs] You'd never understand.

745
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:38,491
You were supposed to succeed
Thunder Breathing!

746
00:43:38,533 --> 00:43:39,992
But you tarnished it!

747
00:43:41,453 --> 00:43:42,579
Huh?

748
00:43:42,619 --> 00:43:44,872
[ZENITSU]
After you became a demon,

749
00:43:44,914 --> 00:43:46,124
he...

750
00:43:47,792 --> 00:43:49,502
He committed seppuku!

751
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:51,254
[♪ poignant music playing]

752
00:43:51,296 --> 00:43:52,671
[voice breaking] Even worse,

753
00:43:53,214 --> 00:43:54,924
he did it by himself.

754
00:43:56,134 --> 00:43:58,177
He was all alone!

755
00:43:59,387 --> 00:44:01,097
Because of that,
no one was there

756
00:44:01,139 --> 00:44:02,765
to put him out of his misery.

757
00:44:02,807 --> 00:44:06,018
He bled out
and died a painful death.

758
00:44:06,060 --> 00:44:07,853
It's your fault!

759
00:44:07,895 --> 00:44:11,065
Gramps died the most
agonizing death possible

760
00:44:11,107 --> 00:44:13,234
all because
the Thunder Breathing rights

761
00:44:13,276 --> 00:44:14,444
produced a demon!

762
00:44:16,154 --> 00:44:18,323
Why the hell should I care?

763
00:44:18,781 --> 00:44:21,200
Gramps died? So what?

764
00:44:21,242 --> 00:44:22,659
Want me to cry?

765
00:44:22,701 --> 00:44:25,204
Did you expect me
to give it to him?

766
00:44:25,246 --> 00:44:26,498
Well, I don't.

767
00:44:26,789 --> 00:44:30,084
In fact, I don't care for anyone
who doesn't appreciate me.

768
00:44:30,126 --> 00:44:31,961
No matter what,

769
00:44:32,003 --> 00:44:33,838
this is who I am.

770
00:44:33,879 --> 00:44:36,966
Take the side
of whoever knows my worth.

771
00:44:37,008 --> 00:44:38,176
[laughs]

772
00:44:39,093 --> 00:44:41,387
If the old geezer
really did die in agony,

773
00:44:41,429 --> 00:44:43,139
then I couldn't be happier.

774
00:44:43,181 --> 00:44:46,351
I slaved away
for that ungrateful bastard.

775
00:44:46,392 --> 00:44:48,645
And what does he do to repay me?

776
00:44:48,685 --> 00:44:50,522
He makes you my co-successor

777
00:44:50,563 --> 00:44:52,565
instead of just letting me
carry the torch!

778
00:44:52,607 --> 00:44:54,150
I hope he rots!

779
00:44:54,691 --> 00:44:56,819
Former Hashira or not,

780
00:44:56,861 --> 00:45:00,281
I would never shed a tear
over some senile geezer.

781
00:45:00,323 --> 00:45:03,117
[laughs boorishly]

782
00:45:05,453 --> 00:45:08,122
[ZENITSU] Gramps knew
exactly what he was doing.

783
00:45:08,623 --> 00:45:11,834
We were made co-successors
because we're weak.

784
00:45:11,876 --> 00:45:14,212
I was only able to use
the First Form

785
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:17,089
while you could use
everything but First Form.

786
00:45:17,714 --> 00:45:19,758
I can't help
but feel sorry for Gramps

787
00:45:19,800 --> 00:45:22,220
that he has two
useless successors!

788
00:45:22,261 --> 00:45:24,096
[KAIGAKU]
Don't lump us together!

789
00:45:24,138 --> 00:45:26,224
I'm nothing like you!

790
00:45:26,723 --> 00:45:31,020
Thunder Breathing, Fourth Form:
Distant Thunder!

791
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:33,231
[♪ intense dramatic music
playing]

792
00:45:34,524 --> 00:45:35,900
[gasps]

793
00:45:38,735 --> 00:45:41,030
You're so slow, scum.

794
00:45:41,072 --> 00:45:42,657
- [groans]
- [blood splatters]

795
00:45:46,619 --> 00:45:49,330
[KAIGAKU]
What the hell? He got me.

796
00:45:49,372 --> 00:45:50,998
His speed is unreal.

797
00:45:51,040 --> 00:45:53,585
He never moved like that.

798
00:45:53,626 --> 00:45:55,336
He's changed.

799
00:45:56,879 --> 00:45:59,173
But he's not the only one.

800
00:46:03,094 --> 00:46:05,221
[wet squelching]

801
00:46:09,642 --> 00:46:12,895
There's no shame in kneeling
down before the powerful

802
00:46:12,937 --> 00:46:14,439
if it means surviving.

803
00:46:14,939 --> 00:46:16,815
As long as you're alive,

804
00:46:16,857 --> 00:46:18,651
you can still win.

805
00:46:20,027 --> 00:46:23,197
Only once you die have you lost.

806
00:46:23,698 --> 00:46:26,992
Even if you have to beg
on your hands and knees.

807
00:46:27,535 --> 00:46:30,829
Even if you're without a home
and have to drink from a puddle.

808
00:46:31,289 --> 00:46:34,791
Even if they condemn you
for stealing money.

809
00:46:35,792 --> 00:46:37,128
As long as you're alive,

810
00:46:37,169 --> 00:46:39,547
there's still a future
where you can win.

811
00:46:40,047 --> 00:46:43,676
Believing that
is all that's kept me going.

812
00:46:45,637 --> 00:46:48,055
[KOKUSHIBO]
Forfeit your humanity

813
00:46:48,097 --> 00:46:51,643
and limitless power
will be within reach.

814
00:46:52,143 --> 00:46:55,313
Should my Lord
choose to acknowledge you,

815
00:46:55,354 --> 00:46:58,775
demon blood
shall course through your veins.

816
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:01,902
[Kaigaku quivers]

817
00:47:02,570 --> 00:47:04,447
The stronger the swordsman,

818
00:47:04,489 --> 00:47:07,784
the longer it takes for him
to become a demon.

819
00:47:08,576 --> 00:47:12,246
It took me three days
to fully transform.

820
00:47:12,747 --> 00:47:15,583
Turning a breathing technique
user into a demon

821
00:47:15,625 --> 00:47:17,335
is no small feat.

822
00:47:17,376 --> 00:47:19,170
Doing such a thing will require

823
00:47:19,211 --> 00:47:22,047
an exorbitant amount
of my Lord's blood.

824
00:47:22,799 --> 00:47:24,759
And though it is rare,

825
00:47:24,801 --> 00:47:26,678
some people,
for whatever reason,

826
00:47:26,719 --> 00:47:29,221
are physically incapable
of becoming demons.

827
00:47:29,263 --> 00:47:30,264
Huh?

828
00:47:30,889 --> 00:47:33,850
[KOKUSHIBO] I'm curious to see
how you will fare.

829
00:47:33,892 --> 00:47:35,561
UPPER ONE

830
00:47:36,061 --> 00:47:37,229
[quivers]

831
00:47:37,271 --> 00:47:39,940
You must appreciate this blood.

832
00:47:39,982 --> 00:47:45,070
Even holding it as you are now
is an honor you cannot fathom.

833
00:47:45,112 --> 00:47:47,448
Should you spill a single drop,

834
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:50,493
I'll have you dismembered
in an instant

835
00:47:50,535 --> 00:47:52,745
before it touches the ground.

836
00:47:52,787 --> 00:47:54,163
[gasps in horror]

837
00:47:54,871 --> 00:47:56,499
[breathing shakily]

838
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:02,296
[KAIGAKU] Even now,
I remember the terror I felt.

839
00:48:02,338 --> 00:48:06,384
Like every cell in my body
was screaming in anguish.

840
00:48:08,969 --> 00:48:11,222
Compared to what I felt then,

841
00:48:11,263 --> 00:48:12,807
this is nothing.

842
00:48:12,849 --> 00:48:15,351
- He's just a punk.
- [clatters]

843
00:48:15,393 --> 00:48:16,811
He might be stronger,

844
00:48:16,853 --> 00:48:18,937
but he's not on par
with an Upper Rank.

845
00:48:19,814 --> 00:48:24,068
Zenitsu Agatsuma
is and always will be trash.

846
00:48:24,109 --> 00:48:26,028
He's a despicable crybaby

847
00:48:26,070 --> 00:48:28,573
without a shred of dignity
or valor!

848
00:48:28,614 --> 00:48:30,616
Somebody, help!

849
00:48:30,658 --> 00:48:35,162
I fell in a pitfall
and twisted my ankle!

850
00:48:35,830 --> 00:48:37,623
[KAIGAKU] The disrespect!

851
00:48:37,665 --> 00:48:41,377
As if I'd be co-successor
with that sniveling loser!

852
00:48:41,918 --> 00:48:43,838
[JIGORO] Here you are, Kaigaku.

853
00:48:44,380 --> 00:48:46,923
- [ZENITSU] Hey, Gramps?
- [KAIGAKU] Hmm?

854
00:48:46,965 --> 00:48:50,219
It looks a little big on me,
don't you think?

855
00:48:50,261 --> 00:48:52,513
- Maybe I'll grow into it...
- [KAIGAKU] I'm supposed to be

856
00:48:52,555 --> 00:48:55,099
- that idiot's equal?
- [both laughing]

857
00:48:56,225 --> 00:48:58,770
That's gotta be
some kind of sick joke!

858
00:48:58,811 --> 00:49:00,104
[seething]

859
00:49:00,605 --> 00:49:03,065
The old bastard deserved to die!

860
00:49:03,107 --> 00:49:05,359
And if you miss him so dearly,

861
00:49:05,401 --> 00:49:07,862
then I'll see to it
you join him!

862
00:49:09,154 --> 00:49:12,116
[ZENITSU] I was only ever able
to learn the First Form.

863
00:49:12,157 --> 00:49:15,994
However, you were able to learn
everything but the First Form.

864
00:49:17,204 --> 00:49:18,623
[♪ tender music playing]

865
00:49:18,664 --> 00:49:19,916
Gramps knew that.

866
00:49:20,458 --> 00:49:23,502
His solution
was having us both succeed

867
00:49:23,544 --> 00:49:25,296
the Thunder Breathing technique.

868
00:49:27,882 --> 00:49:29,592
But you denied him that.

869
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:32,553
You became a demon

870
00:49:32,595 --> 00:49:34,597
purely to reject him.

871
00:49:35,556 --> 00:49:37,809
- [crackling]
- It's coming!

872
00:49:37,850 --> 00:49:40,686
Thunder Breathing, Second Form:

873
00:49:41,270 --> 00:49:42,647
Rice Spirit!

874
00:49:42,688 --> 00:49:44,774
[♪ dramatic synth music playing]

875
00:49:44,816 --> 00:49:47,568
[ZENITSU] He attacked five times
in one breath.

876
00:49:48,193 --> 00:49:50,446
- [Kaigaku yells]
- [effort grunts, strains]

877
00:49:50,488 --> 00:49:52,406
How many people
have you devoured?

878
00:49:52,448 --> 00:49:55,534
You can't even tell right
from wrong anymore!

879
00:49:55,576 --> 00:49:58,579
I'm more aware of those
than I've ever been!

880
00:49:59,789 --> 00:50:01,123
What's the matter?

881
00:50:01,206 --> 00:50:04,418
Aren't you supposed to be
the old geezer's favorite?

882
00:50:04,919 --> 00:50:06,504
- [grunts]
- If you are,

883
00:50:06,545 --> 00:50:08,673
then show me
what he passed down to you!

884
00:50:08,714 --> 00:50:12,217
It's the only technique
you've got, so use it!

885
00:50:12,259 --> 00:50:13,427
[Zenitsu grunts]

886
00:50:14,804 --> 00:50:17,890
Go all out.
Use everything you got.

887
00:50:17,932 --> 00:50:19,809
- [groans angrily]
- And don't you dare hold back

888
00:50:19,851 --> 00:50:22,186
- for a second!
- [determined grunt]

889
00:50:26,983 --> 00:50:28,567
[ZENITSU] Thunder Breathing...

890
00:50:30,945 --> 00:50:32,363
...First Form...

891
00:50:32,738 --> 00:50:33,739
[scoffs]

892
00:50:34,323 --> 00:50:36,241
...Thunderclap and Flash.

893
00:50:39,119 --> 00:50:40,579
[effort grunts]

894
00:50:40,621 --> 00:50:42,206
[laughs boisterously]

895
00:50:42,247 --> 00:50:45,584
As if a basic attack
like charging me head-on

896
00:50:45,626 --> 00:50:47,336
would ever find its mark.

897
00:50:47,378 --> 00:50:49,129
Don't make me laugh!

898
00:50:50,923 --> 00:50:52,591
Thunder Breathing,

899
00:50:52,633 --> 00:50:55,970
Third Form: Thunder Swarm!

900
00:50:58,180 --> 00:51:00,224
[grunting]

901
00:51:01,475 --> 00:51:03,895
[ZENITSU] He's attacking me
from every angle at once.

902
00:51:03,936 --> 00:51:05,354
[KAIGAKU] What's the matter?

903
00:51:05,396 --> 00:51:07,606
Don't tell me
you're done already!

904
00:51:08,816 --> 00:51:10,609
[ZENITSU]
Thunder Breathing, First Form:

905
00:51:10,651 --> 00:51:13,278
Thunderclap and Flash:
Eight Fold!

906
00:51:17,742 --> 00:51:20,327
- That's not gonna work!
- [Zenitsu grunts]

907
00:51:20,828 --> 00:51:23,956
Thunder Breathing, Fifth Form:

908
00:51:26,333 --> 00:51:27,877
Heat Lightning!

909
00:51:28,377 --> 00:51:30,838
- Ah!
- Gotcha!

910
00:51:31,505 --> 00:51:35,009
How does the bite of my Blood
Demon Art-enhanced sword feel?

911
00:51:35,051 --> 00:51:37,845
- [electricity crackling]
- Each strike on contact

912
00:51:37,887 --> 00:51:40,514
leaves a wound
that burns your skin.

913
00:51:41,097 --> 00:51:44,727
This proves those who recognize
my talents and value are right!

914
00:51:45,269 --> 00:51:48,522
And those that dismiss
or condemn me are wrong!

915
00:51:49,065 --> 00:51:52,818
Do you get it now?
This is the power I have!

916
00:51:53,318 --> 00:51:55,487
My power as a demon that is!

917
00:51:55,947 --> 00:51:58,156
All you know how to do
is use First Form,

918
00:51:58,198 --> 00:52:01,243
yet that geezer chose
to make you his successor!

919
00:52:01,285 --> 00:52:03,996
And, boy,
what a mistake that was!

920
00:52:10,294 --> 00:52:11,629
So, that's it.

921
00:52:11,670 --> 00:52:14,381
This is the path
that you've chosen to take.

922
00:52:15,883 --> 00:52:17,426
[weakly] I already knew.

923
00:52:18,094 --> 00:52:19,595
I knew, but...

924
00:52:21,513 --> 00:52:23,181
[sword scraping]

925
00:52:24,767 --> 00:52:27,728
With this strike, I'll end this.

926
00:52:27,770 --> 00:52:29,229
You're finished!

927
00:52:29,271 --> 00:52:30,940
- [crackling]
- Thunder Breathing...

928
00:52:30,982 --> 00:52:33,985
- [rumbling]
- ...Sixth Form:

929
00:52:37,822 --> 00:52:41,117
- [crackling]
- [♪ music intensifies]

930
00:52:42,158 --> 00:52:44,829
Rumble and Flash!

931
00:52:44,870 --> 00:52:48,791
That strike I landed will keep
crackling through your flesh!

932
00:52:48,833 --> 00:52:52,795
This is the power that I gained
by becoming a demon.

933
00:52:52,837 --> 00:52:54,379
Get it now?

934
00:52:54,421 --> 00:52:56,924
I've long surpassed
Thunder Breathing!

935
00:52:58,717 --> 00:53:00,886
[laughs boisterously]

936
00:53:00,928 --> 00:53:02,638
You and I aren't equals.

937
00:53:02,680 --> 00:53:04,056
And we never have been.

938
00:53:04,598 --> 00:53:06,350
I'm better than all of you.

939
00:53:07,351 --> 00:53:08,602
Guess the old bastard

940
00:53:08,644 --> 00:53:10,771
shouldn't have put
his trust in you after all.

941
00:53:10,813 --> 00:53:13,607
[laughs boisterously]

942
00:53:15,317 --> 00:53:17,820
[JIGORO] Come on,
be more like Kaigaku!

943
00:53:18,320 --> 00:53:21,907
He's your senior,
so follow his example, you hear?

944
00:53:21,949 --> 00:53:24,160
Hang on. Isn't the First Form

945
00:53:24,200 --> 00:53:26,787
pretty much the entire basis
of Thunder Breathing?

946
00:53:26,829 --> 00:53:29,414
Yeah, and it's the only one
he can't do.

947
00:53:29,456 --> 00:53:31,709
You know what that means,
don't ya?

948
00:53:31,750 --> 00:53:34,045
That even though
he's mastered other forms,

949
00:53:34,086 --> 00:53:35,587
he's still a weakling.

950
00:53:35,629 --> 00:53:37,006
Yep, exactly.

951
00:53:37,048 --> 00:53:39,675
The way he shows off, though?
He's got such an ego.

952
00:53:39,717 --> 00:53:42,260
[BOY 1] No way
he becomes a Hashira.

953
00:53:42,302 --> 00:53:44,388
[BOY 2] Yeah,
he'll die before then.

954
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:45,514
[♪ gentle music playing]

955
00:53:45,556 --> 00:53:47,641
What did I do to deserve that?

956
00:53:49,101 --> 00:53:51,979
I heard you went and punched
someone from a higher rank.

957
00:53:52,437 --> 00:53:55,357
Don't go around making trouble,
you trash!

958
00:53:55,399 --> 00:53:58,944
It's embarrassing even being
seen in the same room as you.

959
00:54:01,488 --> 00:54:04,742
[ZENITSU] I was fully aware
that you hated me, Kaigaku.

960
00:54:04,783 --> 00:54:08,579
And to be perfectly honest,
I hated you, too.

961
00:54:09,705 --> 00:54:13,709
Even so, I couldn't help
but respect you as well.

962
00:54:14,210 --> 00:54:17,379
You never stopped
working towards your goals.

963
00:54:18,214 --> 00:54:20,256
Despite our differences,

964
00:54:20,298 --> 00:54:22,718
I looked up to you
as an example.

965
00:54:23,219 --> 00:54:25,637
You really were a special guy.

966
00:54:27,223 --> 00:54:28,933
It wasn't just me.

967
00:54:28,974 --> 00:54:31,476
Gramps thought
you were remarkable, too.

968
00:54:32,477 --> 00:54:36,023
But I guess you weren't
satisfied with that, were you?

969
00:54:36,732 --> 00:54:38,400
No matter the day,

970
00:54:38,442 --> 00:54:42,487
the only sound that came
from you was discontent.

971
00:54:42,529 --> 00:54:43,739
[soft tinkling]

972
00:54:43,781 --> 00:54:46,742
It was like the box
where you kept your joy

973
00:54:46,784 --> 00:54:48,202
had a hole in it.

974
00:54:49,828 --> 00:54:52,414
And that joy kept leaking out.

975
00:54:53,832 --> 00:54:55,834
If the hole isn't mended,

976
00:54:56,292 --> 00:54:58,921
happiness will always be
out of reach.

977
00:55:01,339 --> 00:55:04,509
Gramps,
I'm sorry we're fighting...

978
00:55:05,469 --> 00:55:06,887
...but he and I

979
00:55:07,512 --> 00:55:09,932
must walk separate paths.

980
00:55:16,063 --> 00:55:18,232
- [clangs]
- [crackling]

981
00:55:19,441 --> 00:55:20,609
[KAIGAKU] Huh?

982
00:55:21,152 --> 00:55:23,237
He's still holding on?

983
00:55:23,279 --> 00:55:24,362
[electricity crackling]

984
00:55:24,404 --> 00:55:27,074
[♪ synth music playing]

985
00:55:31,287 --> 00:55:32,496
[power surging]

986
00:55:32,537 --> 00:55:33,956
What the hell?

987
00:55:42,547 --> 00:55:43,715
[ZENITSU] Brother...

988
00:55:44,591 --> 00:55:46,802
- ...I'm sorry.
- [gasps]

989
00:55:47,385 --> 00:55:49,554
[♪ music intensifies]

990
00:56:05,654 --> 00:56:09,365
Thunder Breathing, Seventh Form:

991
00:56:09,407 --> 00:56:11,035
[roaring]

992
00:56:12,286 --> 00:56:14,538
God of Fire Thunder.

993
00:56:21,712 --> 00:56:23,214
[KAIGAKU] That...

994
00:56:23,547 --> 00:56:25,299
was so fast.

995
00:56:25,799 --> 00:56:28,177
That move. What was it?

996
00:56:28,552 --> 00:56:30,179
Unbelievable.

997
00:56:30,221 --> 00:56:33,098
How come I've never seen
that technique until now?

998
00:56:34,016 --> 00:56:36,643
Damn you. Damn you!

999
00:56:36,685 --> 00:56:39,855
I always knew that stupid geezer
liked you more than me!

1000
00:56:39,897 --> 00:56:42,858
Why else would he only
teach you that technique?!

1001
00:56:42,900 --> 00:56:44,735
You're wrong.

1002
00:56:44,776 --> 00:56:45,861
[gasps]

1003
00:56:45,903 --> 00:56:46,904
[♪ gentle music playing]

1004
00:56:47,196 --> 00:56:49,323
[ZENITSU] Gramps was never
that kind of person.

1005
00:56:50,406 --> 00:56:53,035
This technique
is something I made.

1006
00:56:53,660 --> 00:56:56,705
I created it all by myself.

1007
00:56:57,622 --> 00:56:58,916
My hope was...

1008
00:56:59,917 --> 00:57:04,963
...that one day, I'd be able
to use it to fight by your side.

1009
00:57:08,424 --> 00:57:11,136
[KAIGAKU]
How is this even possible?

1010
00:57:11,678 --> 00:57:14,348
Thunder Breathing
only has six techniques,

1011
00:57:14,390 --> 00:57:17,351
and yet he was able
to create a seventh?

1012
00:57:18,102 --> 00:57:21,855
Him? The one who can only
use the First Form?

1013
00:57:23,148 --> 00:57:26,151
He's inferior to me
in every way!

1014
00:57:26,193 --> 00:57:27,569
[groans angrily]

1015
00:57:27,611 --> 00:57:30,655
I can't accept it.
I won't accept it!

1016
00:57:30,697 --> 00:57:33,533
This must be
some kind of twisted joke!

1017
00:57:33,575 --> 00:57:37,204
Someone like me losing to him?

1018
00:57:38,122 --> 00:57:40,749
I must be going insane!

1019
00:57:42,376 --> 00:57:43,543
Wait!

1020
00:57:44,460 --> 00:57:46,380
With his strength depleted,

1021
00:57:46,422 --> 00:57:48,799
I can still have the last laugh.

1022
00:57:48,840 --> 00:57:51,635
This fall will kill him
and he can't stop it.

1023
00:57:52,344 --> 00:57:56,432
I'll be taking him to hell
with me. [laughs maliciously]

1024
00:57:56,472 --> 00:57:58,225
[YUSHIRO]
Those who never give to others

1025
00:57:58,267 --> 00:58:00,685
are never able to receive
in return.

1026
00:58:00,727 --> 00:58:01,853
Huh?

1027
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:04,440
People who have
nothing but desire

1028
00:58:04,480 --> 00:58:07,025
are no different than those
who have nothing at all.

1029
00:58:07,525 --> 00:58:10,904
And one cannot create anything
out of nothing.

1030
00:58:11,863 --> 00:58:14,741
Dying alone is pathetic,
wouldn't you say?

1031
00:58:20,914 --> 00:58:22,624
[screaming in anguish]

1032
00:58:22,666 --> 00:58:24,418
[fizzles out]

1033
00:58:32,926 --> 00:58:34,303
[gasps]

1034
00:58:34,345 --> 00:58:36,388
- [birds chirping]
- [leaves rustling]

1035
00:58:37,055 --> 00:58:38,140
Where am I?

1036
00:58:38,182 --> 00:58:40,309
- [stream trickling]
- [birds chirping]

1037
00:58:45,356 --> 00:58:46,648
[gasps]

1038
00:58:46,690 --> 00:58:48,108
Gramps!

1039
00:58:48,692 --> 00:58:50,819
[♪ tender music playing]

1040
00:58:50,861 --> 00:58:52,029
I'm sorry!

1041
00:58:52,070 --> 00:58:54,698
I... I couldn't get along
with Kaigaku!

1042
00:58:54,739 --> 00:58:57,742
I even tried
writing him letters, but...

1043
00:58:57,784 --> 00:59:00,454
But he never wrote me back.
And... [sobs]

1044
00:59:00,496 --> 00:59:01,913
...if it weren't for me,

1045
00:59:01,955 --> 00:59:04,082
he might not have ended up
the way he did.

1046
00:59:04,540 --> 00:59:06,001
I'm really sorry!

1047
00:59:06,043 --> 00:59:07,294
Forgive me!

1048
00:59:07,336 --> 00:59:10,381
I wasn't able to pay you back
for everything!

1049
00:59:10,422 --> 00:59:13,467
I really wanted you
to see me as a Hashira,

1050
00:59:13,509 --> 00:59:15,302
to make you proud.

1051
00:59:15,344 --> 00:59:16,720
I'm sorry.

1052
00:59:16,761 --> 00:59:18,514
I failed you, Gramps!

1053
00:59:21,433 --> 00:59:24,478
[sobbing] I understand
if you hate me now.

1054
00:59:25,103 --> 00:59:27,772
Please, just say something.
Anything!

1055
00:59:27,814 --> 00:59:29,149
[effort grunting]

1056
00:59:29,691 --> 00:59:32,861
Damn it! What's this
grabbing my leg?

1057
00:59:34,112 --> 00:59:36,156
Gramps! I just...

1058
00:59:36,198 --> 00:59:38,534
I need-- [grunts]

1059
00:59:39,993 --> 00:59:41,161
Damn it!

1060
00:59:41,203 --> 00:59:43,247
[effort grunting]

1061
00:59:43,288 --> 00:59:44,789
[JIGORO] Zenitsu.

1062
00:59:44,831 --> 00:59:45,874
[Zenitsu gasps softly]

1063
00:59:52,381 --> 00:59:56,301
Listen to me, lad.
You are my pride and joy.

1064
01:00:14,778 --> 01:00:16,280
[♪ music fades]

1065
01:00:19,450 --> 01:00:21,868
[MURATA] Well? Can you save him?

1066
01:00:21,910 --> 01:00:23,661
He's someone that I know.

1067
01:00:23,703 --> 01:00:26,706
I can't watch him die.
Please tell me there's a way!

1068
01:00:26,748 --> 01:00:29,000
Keep your voice down.
You're not helping.

1069
01:00:29,042 --> 01:00:31,711
Just watch out
for enemy ambushes.

1070
01:00:31,753 --> 01:00:34,131
At least then you'll actually be
doing something useful.

1071
01:00:34,172 --> 01:00:35,549
[grunting angrily]

1072
01:00:35,591 --> 01:00:38,510
Excuse me? And just
who the hell are you, huh?

1073
01:00:38,552 --> 01:00:41,138
I better not find out
you're a lower rank than I am!

1074
01:00:41,179 --> 01:00:44,808
I'm a demon. I don't care
about your hierarchy.

1075
01:00:45,601 --> 01:00:47,852
This'll slow
the Blood Demon Art.

1076
01:00:47,894 --> 01:00:49,771
But if these cracks
keep spreading,

1077
01:00:49,813 --> 01:00:52,274
it'll travel all the way
to his eyes.

1078
01:00:52,983 --> 01:00:54,526
Hey, can you hear me?

1079
01:00:55,026 --> 01:00:56,236
[groans]

1080
01:00:56,945 --> 01:00:58,654
[all three exclaim]

1081
01:00:58,696 --> 01:01:01,450
Your bedside manner
really sucks, you know that?

1082
01:01:01,492 --> 01:01:03,201
I'm also using a hemostatic,

1083
01:01:03,243 --> 01:01:05,120
but I still can't get
the bleeding to stop.

1084
01:01:05,162 --> 01:01:06,121
What did I say?!

1085
01:01:06,330 --> 01:01:08,499
Don't listen to him.
You're gonna be fine.

1086
01:01:08,540 --> 01:01:09,958
I swear
you'll pull through this!

1087
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:11,335
Yeah, you can do it!

1088
01:01:11,376 --> 01:01:13,378
Fight on! Fight on!

1089
01:01:13,420 --> 01:01:15,380
The only reason
you're alive right now

1090
01:01:15,422 --> 01:01:16,965
is because
the Upper Rank you fought

1091
01:01:17,007 --> 01:01:19,343
still hadn't mastered
his own techniques.

1092
01:01:19,843 --> 01:01:21,803
That was lucky for you.

1093
01:01:22,346 --> 01:01:23,972
If you'd fought him
a year from now,

1094
01:01:24,014 --> 01:01:25,849
you would have died instantly.

1095
01:01:26,517 --> 01:01:27,725
[Murata groaning]

1096
01:01:27,767 --> 01:01:29,603
Could you stop
with the doom and gloom?

1097
01:01:29,645 --> 01:01:31,729
Consider his feelings!

1098
01:01:31,771 --> 01:01:34,107
[breathing heavily]

1099
01:01:38,278 --> 01:01:41,448
Hey, don't pretend like
I'm the one in the wrong here.

1100
01:01:43,367 --> 01:01:45,076
What? What are you pointing at?

1101
01:01:45,118 --> 01:01:47,663
[YUSHIRO] Your screaming let
the demons know we're here.

1102
01:01:47,703 --> 01:01:49,623
[all screaming]

1103
01:01:49,665 --> 01:01:51,166
Don't say I didn't warn you.

1104
01:01:51,208 --> 01:01:52,626
[snarling]

1105
01:01:52,668 --> 01:01:56,547
Hey, it was Yushiro, right?
Take care of Agatsuma!

1106
01:01:57,088 --> 01:01:58,882
- Charge!
- [all grunting]

1107
01:02:00,676 --> 01:02:03,679
Murata, please take care of them
quickly, okay?

1108
01:02:03,719 --> 01:02:05,889
I'm gonna give you
such an earful later!

1109
01:02:05,930 --> 01:02:08,183
- Damn.
- [demon snarling]

1110
01:02:08,892 --> 01:02:11,269
Water Breathing, Second Form:

1111
01:02:11,311 --> 01:02:14,398
Water Wheel! [yells]

1112
01:02:15,773 --> 01:02:17,234
We're gonna head them off.

1113
01:02:17,275 --> 01:02:18,860
Follow my lead, everyone!

1114
01:02:18,902 --> 01:02:21,112
[all yelling]

1115
01:02:21,154 --> 01:02:22,780
- [footsteps receding]
- [grunts]

1116
01:02:28,870 --> 01:02:31,039
[♪ foreboding music playing]

1117
01:02:35,793 --> 01:02:37,212
This is bad.

1118
01:02:37,254 --> 01:02:38,963
They're gonna run into "him."

1119
01:02:42,175 --> 01:02:44,469
[TANJIRO] We haven't encountered
any Upper Ranks.

1120
01:02:44,928 --> 01:02:47,389
Are we still that far
from Muzan?

1121
01:02:47,431 --> 01:02:49,474
I hope the others are all right.

1122
01:02:52,686 --> 01:02:54,187
Miss Shinobu...

1123
01:02:55,021 --> 01:02:57,190
we're going to win this battle.

1124
01:02:57,232 --> 01:02:59,984
For you. For everyone!

1125
01:03:01,152 --> 01:03:02,738
- [loud crash]
- [gasps]

1126
01:03:02,778 --> 01:03:04,780
That jolt! What was that?

1127
01:03:05,282 --> 01:03:06,491
Mr. Giyu!

1128
01:03:06,533 --> 01:03:07,534
Stay there!

1129
01:03:07,951 --> 01:03:09,785
- Keep calm.
- [grunts]

1130
01:03:11,162 --> 01:03:13,123
[TANJIRO]
Is someone else fighting?

1131
01:03:13,164 --> 01:03:15,292
Are we about to lose
another comrade?

1132
01:03:15,333 --> 01:03:17,544
- [♪ intriguing music playing]
- [loud thuds]

1133
01:03:21,214 --> 01:03:24,175
No, it's something else.

1134
01:03:24,217 --> 01:03:25,761
And it's coming this way.

1135
01:03:26,762 --> 01:03:27,887
[sniffs]

1136
01:03:28,346 --> 01:03:30,766
This... This scent.

1137
01:03:39,399 --> 01:03:41,693
[GIYU] Above us!
Get back, Tanjiro!

1138
01:03:42,569 --> 01:03:43,695
[grunts]

1139
01:03:45,781 --> 01:03:47,783
[DEMON] Long time no see.

1140
01:03:49,409 --> 01:03:52,245
It's commendable
you got this far.

1141
01:03:52,828 --> 01:03:55,332
Especially for a puny insect.

1142
01:03:55,373 --> 01:03:56,458
UPPER THREE

1143
01:03:56,958 --> 01:03:59,835
Don't you agree, Tanjiro?!

1144
01:03:59,877 --> 01:04:01,129
[Tanjiro seething]

1145
01:04:02,255 --> 01:04:05,008
Akaza!

1146
01:04:07,010 --> 01:04:09,179
[♪ low tense music playing]

1147
01:04:12,683 --> 01:04:14,225
[heavy burbling]

1148
01:04:30,701 --> 01:04:32,828
[breathing heavily]

1149
01:04:37,582 --> 01:04:40,335
[TAMAYO] This place...
If I had to guess,

1150
01:04:40,377 --> 01:04:42,504
this fleshy cocoon
is breaking down

1151
01:04:42,546 --> 01:04:43,797
and disposing the drug

1152
01:04:43,839 --> 01:04:46,842
that's rescinding
his demon form.

1153
01:04:47,467 --> 01:04:49,302
Muzan Kibutsuji,

1154
01:04:49,344 --> 01:04:54,015
I had sworn to destroy you
by any means necessary.

1155
01:04:54,599 --> 01:04:58,854
Yet, at this moment,
I am powerless to do so.

1156
01:04:59,563 --> 01:05:00,896
[loud thump]

1157
01:05:00,938 --> 01:05:02,607
[grunting]

1158
01:05:06,110 --> 01:05:10,073
Soon enough,
I'll be absorbed as well.

1159
01:05:10,866 --> 01:05:13,577
Please, someone. Anyone!

1160
01:05:13,618 --> 01:05:15,286
Come quickly!

1161
01:05:15,995 --> 01:05:17,622
I beg you!

1162
01:05:20,625 --> 01:05:22,753
[fight grunts]

1163
01:05:24,546 --> 01:05:26,715
[♪ intense music playing]

1164
01:05:31,927 --> 01:05:35,014
[KIRIYA] According to Father,
if Muzan should die,

1165
01:05:35,056 --> 01:05:37,517
the other demons
will also perish.

1166
01:05:38,727 --> 01:05:42,689
By that logic, it's clear
that Muzan is still alive.

1167
01:05:43,981 --> 01:05:45,483
At this very moment,

1168
01:05:45,525 --> 01:05:48,445
Ms. Tamayo must be
suppressing his powers.

1169
01:05:49,362 --> 01:05:50,697
If she weren't,

1170
01:05:51,239 --> 01:05:54,158
he would surely be aware
of Yushiro's watchful gaze.

1171
01:05:55,201 --> 01:05:57,829
Before Muzan's powers
are fully restored,

1172
01:05:57,871 --> 01:06:01,249
we must do whatever it takes
to see that he's defeated.

1173
01:06:03,084 --> 01:06:04,502
I have to wonder, though,

1174
01:06:04,544 --> 01:06:07,963
inside of this
infinite castle...

1175
01:06:08,924 --> 01:06:11,301
...will we really
be able to find him

1176
01:06:11,342 --> 01:06:13,094
and put an end to it all?

1177
01:06:18,433 --> 01:06:20,435
No need to be nervous.

1178
01:06:21,018 --> 01:06:23,396
You're doing a fine job,
my child.

1179
01:06:25,356 --> 01:06:28,568
Muzan will surely reveal himself
once more,

1180
01:06:29,277 --> 01:06:31,780
just as he did when he found me.

1181
01:06:33,989 --> 01:06:38,703
When it comes to this man,
that's simply his nature.

1182
01:06:39,454 --> 01:06:40,789
[gasps]

1183
01:06:44,250 --> 01:06:46,043
[KIRIYA] I understand, Father.

1184
01:06:46,753 --> 01:06:49,422
I will see to it
our plan succeeds.

1185
01:06:50,841 --> 01:06:53,468
We must find him before
the Corps members' strength

1186
01:06:53,510 --> 01:06:54,678
is fully depleted,

1187
01:06:54,719 --> 01:06:57,096
and settle this
once and for all.

1188
01:06:57,472 --> 01:06:58,640
[Gyomei grunts]

1189
01:07:03,186 --> 01:07:04,312
[distorted grunting]

1190
01:07:07,482 --> 01:07:09,651
- [grunting]
- [KAKUSHI 1] Protect them!

1191
01:07:09,693 --> 01:07:11,152
[KAKUSHI 2] Everybody, group up!

1192
01:07:11,194 --> 01:07:12,570
We have to form a wall!

1193
01:07:12,612 --> 01:07:14,614
Get their attention
off the Hashira!

1194
01:07:14,656 --> 01:07:17,074
Please, sir!
Go on ahead without us!

1195
01:07:17,617 --> 01:07:19,661
You as well! We got this!

1196
01:07:19,703 --> 01:07:20,996
Are you certain?

1197
01:07:21,621 --> 01:07:23,999
- [both grunting]
- [groans]

1198
01:07:25,583 --> 01:07:26,877
[thuds]

1199
01:07:29,337 --> 01:07:32,047
We are!
Just defeat Kibutsuji!

1200
01:07:32,089 --> 01:07:33,424
Please, sir!

1201
01:07:34,009 --> 01:07:35,426
Very well, then.

1202
01:07:35,468 --> 01:07:38,262
I will put my faith
in your efforts here.

1203
01:07:38,304 --> 01:07:39,472
Tokito!

1204
01:07:41,140 --> 01:07:42,392
[KAKUSHI 1] All right!

1205
01:07:42,517 --> 01:07:45,395
Let's show them the fruits
of our Hashira training!

1206
01:07:45,436 --> 01:07:46,730
[ALL] Right!

1207
01:07:46,771 --> 01:07:48,899
[♪ epic cinematic music playing]

1208
01:07:50,358 --> 01:07:52,527
[fight grunts]

1209
01:07:53,862 --> 01:07:56,197
[KIRIYA] Everyone, thank you.

1210
01:07:56,698 --> 01:07:59,868
I know Father would be proud
to see you giving it your all.

1211
01:08:05,498 --> 01:08:07,667
[♪ melancholic music playing]

1212
01:08:10,336 --> 01:08:12,589
- [whimpering]
- [KIRIYA] Stop that!

1213
01:08:13,297 --> 01:08:15,216
You must keep your hands moving.

1214
01:08:15,800 --> 01:08:18,011
Right now, we need to focus.

1215
01:08:19,763 --> 01:08:20,889
[KANATA] Yes.

1216
01:08:24,141 --> 01:08:27,395
Master Kiriya
is quite impressive.

1217
01:08:28,521 --> 01:08:30,273
It's clear
he's still in mourning

1218
01:08:30,314 --> 01:08:32,107
over the loss of the Master,

1219
01:08:32,149 --> 01:08:34,360
yet his duty is unwavering.

1220
01:08:35,028 --> 01:08:38,406
He's led the Demon Slayer Corps
rather splendidly.

1221
01:08:39,866 --> 01:08:42,744
Wouldn't you agree, Mr. Rengoku?

1222
01:08:43,703 --> 01:08:45,329
I would, indeed.

1223
01:08:46,706 --> 01:08:49,459
These children
are still young in years,

1224
01:08:49,500 --> 01:08:52,629
but their resolve
is anything but childish.

1225
01:08:53,797 --> 01:08:55,840
I swear to protect them.

1226
01:08:56,382 --> 01:08:58,843
Just as Kyojuro did before me,

1227
01:08:59,343 --> 01:09:01,888
I will risk my own life
to do so.

1228
01:09:06,183 --> 01:09:08,561
[Nezuko whimpers in pain]

1229
01:09:15,192 --> 01:09:18,237
[SAKONJI] I didn't think
she would suffer this much.

1230
01:09:19,322 --> 01:09:22,784
The Master was working
with a demon named Tamayo

1231
01:09:22,826 --> 01:09:25,286
who delivered this antidote.

1232
01:09:25,328 --> 01:09:28,331
I've administered it
as she instructed.

1233
01:09:29,582 --> 01:09:31,084
Even so,

1234
01:09:31,126 --> 01:09:35,463
will Nezuko be able to turn
back into a human, I wonder?

1235
01:09:35,964 --> 01:09:39,174
If Nezuko
does become human again,

1236
01:09:39,216 --> 01:09:42,553
Muzan's grand scheme
will collapse.

1237
01:09:42,595 --> 01:09:44,055
His thousand-year quest

1238
01:09:44,097 --> 01:09:46,641
for a vessel
which can resist the sun

1239
01:09:46,683 --> 01:09:48,309
will be no more.

1240
01:09:48,810 --> 01:09:51,646
And all of the progress
he's made

1241
01:09:51,688 --> 01:09:54,315
will be wound back like a clock.

1242
01:09:55,859 --> 01:09:59,863
In the many years that we've had
to endure this nightmare,

1243
01:09:59,904 --> 01:10:01,948
Nezuko is the only demon

1244
01:10:01,990 --> 01:10:04,868
who has been able
to live in the sunlight.

1245
01:10:04,909 --> 01:10:07,078
[♪ melancholic music playing]

1246
01:10:10,165 --> 01:10:12,291
[heart beating]

1247
01:10:13,584 --> 01:10:15,086
[inhales deeply]

1248
01:10:16,337 --> 01:10:17,797
[sighs wearily]

1249
01:10:20,591 --> 01:10:22,635
"The final battle."

1250
01:10:22,677 --> 01:10:25,847
These words
echo in my mind.

1251
01:10:27,682 --> 01:10:28,975
[gulps, sighs]

1252
01:10:29,517 --> 01:10:31,268
And each time they do,

1253
01:10:31,310 --> 01:10:34,689
I can't help but tremble
as my heart beats louder.

1254
01:10:35,690 --> 01:10:40,070
This battle may finally
reach its conclusion tonight.

1255
01:10:40,945 --> 01:10:45,616
I never dreamed that I'd be
alive to witness it myself.

1256
01:10:46,826 --> 01:10:48,285
Tanjiro,

1257
01:10:48,327 --> 01:10:50,788
I sometimes
think back to the day

1258
01:10:50,830 --> 01:10:53,624
when you brought
your demon sister to me.

1259
01:10:54,042 --> 01:10:55,919
Ever since then,

1260
01:10:55,960 --> 01:11:00,381
it feels like a giant wheel
of fate has been slowly turning.

1261
01:11:01,465 --> 01:11:05,469
Perhaps it would be best to
compare the sum of our battles

1262
01:11:05,511 --> 01:11:08,305
to a giant dormant machine.

1263
01:11:08,347 --> 01:11:12,435
You and Nezuko are the small
cogs that have joined together

1264
01:11:12,476 --> 01:11:14,437
and awoken it from its slumber.

1265
01:11:15,021 --> 01:11:19,984
What was once frozen in place
has now been set into motion.

1266
01:11:20,026 --> 01:11:22,195
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1267
01:11:22,695 --> 01:11:25,990
- [moaning]
- Don't give up, Nezuko.

1268
01:11:27,491 --> 01:11:30,078
Keep up the fight, Tanjiro.

1269
01:11:30,787 --> 01:11:33,957
You both have to pull through,
no matter what!

1270
01:11:34,498 --> 01:11:36,167
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1271
01:11:36,709 --> 01:11:37,752
Fire Wheel!

1272
01:11:37,794 --> 01:11:39,921
[♪ epic dramatic music playing]

1273
01:11:40,463 --> 01:11:41,881
Go through!

1274
01:11:42,006 --> 01:11:44,801
If I can't even sever his arm,
I'll never sever his head!

1275
01:11:44,842 --> 01:11:47,053
[yelling]

1276
01:11:47,845 --> 01:11:49,097
[flesh squelches]

1277
01:11:49,555 --> 01:11:51,057
[blood splatters]

1278
01:11:51,099 --> 01:11:52,058
DESTROY

1279
01:11:52,100 --> 01:11:53,226
I got one.

1280
01:11:53,392 --> 01:11:55,310
I was able
to dodge his attack, too.

1281
01:11:55,352 --> 01:11:56,729
I can do this!

1282
01:11:57,230 --> 01:11:58,856
I couldn't aim for his head,

1283
01:11:58,898 --> 01:12:00,441
but this time, for sure!

1284
01:12:01,567 --> 01:12:04,070
Hinokami Kagura: Fake Rainbow!

1285
01:12:04,112 --> 01:12:05,155
[fizzles out]

1286
01:12:07,406 --> 01:12:09,242
[high-pitched ringing]

1287
01:12:11,368 --> 01:12:13,328
- [panting]
- [sword clatters]

1288
01:12:14,831 --> 01:12:16,791
[flesh squelching]

1289
01:12:16,833 --> 01:12:18,293
Huh?

1290
01:12:19,752 --> 01:12:20,962
[GIYU] Tanjiro.

1291
01:12:21,462 --> 01:12:23,965
You've really sharpened
your skills, haven't you?

1292
01:12:24,882 --> 01:12:26,634
It wouldn't be an exaggeration

1293
01:12:26,676 --> 01:12:29,386
to say he's at the level
of a Hashira now.

1294
01:12:30,596 --> 01:12:34,767
To think that he'd do this well
against Upper Three.

1295
01:12:34,809 --> 01:12:36,978
[♪ enchanting folk music
playing]

1296
01:12:40,064 --> 01:12:41,316
That day...

1297
01:12:42,275 --> 01:12:45,069
...I remember a boy
who felt completely helpless

1298
01:12:45,528 --> 01:12:47,780
as he collapsed
onto the cold snow,

1299
01:12:48,281 --> 01:12:51,075
begging through tears
for his sister's life.

1300
01:12:58,875 --> 01:13:01,002
But you are helpless no longer.

1301
01:13:01,502 --> 01:13:04,339
You have the strength
to fight not only for your life,

1302
01:13:04,839 --> 01:13:07,133
but also
for what's precious to you.

1303
01:13:08,801 --> 01:13:11,346
[AKAZA] "This boy is not weak.

1304
01:13:11,386 --> 01:13:13,139
Don't insult him."

1305
01:13:13,931 --> 01:13:17,434
I must admit that Kyojuro
was right when he said that.

1306
01:13:17,935 --> 01:13:20,855
You are certainly not weak.

1307
01:13:20,897 --> 01:13:23,607
In fact, I commend you.

1308
01:13:26,361 --> 01:13:28,779
Technique Development...

1309
01:13:28,821 --> 01:13:30,990
[♪ intense rock music playing]

1310
01:13:32,950 --> 01:13:36,287
Now, let's kick things off,
shall we?

1311
01:13:36,913 --> 01:13:39,040
It's time we had some fun.

1312
01:13:44,628 --> 01:13:46,672
- [rumbling]
- [heavy creaking]

1313
01:14:07,484 --> 01:14:08,736
[exhales sharply]

1314
01:14:15,076 --> 01:14:16,660
[grunts]

1315
01:14:25,420 --> 01:14:28,463
[GIYU]
Water Breathing, Third Form:

1316
01:14:28,505 --> 01:14:30,091
Flowing Dance!

1317
01:14:31,008 --> 01:14:32,969
You're a Water Hashira.

1318
01:14:33,010 --> 01:14:34,845
How lucky for me!

1319
01:14:34,887 --> 01:14:37,640
It's been 50 years
since I fought one.

1320
01:14:41,894 --> 01:14:43,520
[debris clattering]

1321
01:14:45,398 --> 01:14:49,068
Destructive Death: Disorder!

1322
01:14:50,861 --> 01:14:53,572
Water Breathing, Eleventh Form:

1323
01:14:54,324 --> 01:14:55,741
Dead Calm.

1324
01:15:00,663 --> 01:15:03,374
[AKAZA] I've never seen
that move before.

1325
01:15:03,916 --> 01:15:06,127
Perhaps the last
Water Hashira I killed

1326
01:15:06,169 --> 01:15:08,296
never had a chance to use it!

1327
01:15:08,338 --> 01:15:11,506
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:
Raging Sun!

1328
01:15:13,676 --> 01:15:14,969
He vanished!

1329
01:15:15,719 --> 01:15:16,929
Behind me!

1330
01:15:16,971 --> 01:15:18,513
Fake Rain Kagura!

1331
01:15:19,849 --> 01:15:24,187
[GIYU] Water Breathing,
Second Form: Water Wheel.

1332
01:15:27,648 --> 01:15:28,691
[yells]

1333
01:15:36,573 --> 01:15:38,617
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1334
01:15:39,743 --> 01:15:40,828
Flame Dance!

1335
01:15:41,204 --> 01:15:44,957
[AKAZA] Destructive Death,
Leg Type: Crown Splitter!

1336
01:15:45,624 --> 01:15:48,169
[TANJIRO]
I blocked it with my sword.

1337
01:15:52,465 --> 01:15:54,633
His move barely grazed me

1338
01:15:54,675 --> 01:15:56,927
and still did
this kind of damage?

1339
01:16:01,307 --> 01:16:03,142
[AKAZA] How marvelous!

1340
01:16:04,477 --> 01:16:08,231
That elegant sword skill
you're using is magnificent!

1341
01:16:08,272 --> 01:16:11,108
I must know now.
What is your name?

1342
01:16:11,150 --> 01:16:12,985
I want to remember you!

1343
01:16:15,071 --> 01:16:18,115
I don't have a name
to give to a demon like you.

1344
01:16:18,157 --> 01:16:21,035
I hate talking,
so don't speak to me!

1345
01:16:21,827 --> 01:16:23,204
Is that so?

1346
01:16:23,246 --> 01:16:25,956
You're not much
for small talk, are you?

1347
01:16:25,998 --> 01:16:30,211
Well, I happen to quite
enjoy it, so I'll ask you again.

1348
01:16:30,794 --> 01:16:32,296
What is your name?

1349
01:16:32,338 --> 01:16:34,465
[grunting]

1350
01:16:35,674 --> 01:16:37,760
- [impact grunts]
- [crumbles]

1351
01:16:38,593 --> 01:16:41,805
[AKAZA]
Destructive Death, Leg Type:

1352
01:16:41,847 --> 01:16:44,100
Explosive Flurry!

1353
01:16:47,853 --> 01:16:50,231
[yelling]

1354
01:16:55,778 --> 01:16:58,197
- [impact grunts]
- [TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu!

1355
01:16:59,740 --> 01:17:02,368
I see. That's his name.

1356
01:17:02,410 --> 01:17:04,245
Thank you for letting me know.

1357
01:17:07,748 --> 01:17:09,375
Hinokami Kagura!

1358
01:17:09,417 --> 01:17:12,503
Destructive Death:
Eight-Layered Demon Core!

1359
01:17:12,545 --> 01:17:14,838
Burning Bones, Summer Sun!

1360
01:17:21,387 --> 01:17:23,222
[panting]

1361
01:17:29,770 --> 01:17:31,646
[AKAZA] Excellent form!

1362
01:17:31,688 --> 01:17:35,610
To improve this much in such
a short time is impressive.

1363
01:17:35,650 --> 01:17:37,694
I'll give you my praise.

1364
01:17:37,736 --> 01:17:39,489
It seems obvious to me

1365
01:17:39,530 --> 01:17:42,450
that Kyojuro must have
really inspired you.

1366
01:17:42,492 --> 01:17:46,787
The night we met, you were
merely a weak, mournful child,

1367
01:17:46,829 --> 01:17:48,456
crumpled on the ground.

1368
01:17:48,498 --> 01:17:50,916
Not even worthy of being killed.

1369
01:17:50,958 --> 01:17:53,002
- But just look at you now!
- [cracking]

1370
01:17:53,043 --> 01:17:57,131
This leap in your abilities,
it's like you've been reborn!

1371
01:17:57,173 --> 01:17:59,467
My heart won't stop racing.

1372
01:17:59,509 --> 01:18:01,844
I'm truly overjoyed!

1373
01:18:01,885 --> 01:18:03,638
[snickers]

1374
01:18:04,388 --> 01:18:08,267
The night Kyojuro died,
I was glad that it happened.

1375
01:18:09,393 --> 01:18:10,353
[exclaims in disbelief]

1376
01:18:10,894 --> 01:18:12,355
How tragic would it have been

1377
01:18:12,396 --> 01:18:14,565
if he had never gotten
any stronger.

1378
01:18:15,232 --> 01:18:17,401
Such a stubborn man,
not letting go

1379
01:18:17,443 --> 01:18:20,530
of those worthless values
of staying human.

1380
01:18:21,780 --> 01:18:23,533
How dare you!

1381
01:18:30,665 --> 01:18:33,626
Shut up! Just shut up!

1382
01:18:37,421 --> 01:18:40,466
Don't you dare
even speak his name!

1383
01:18:41,551 --> 01:18:42,843
[AKAZA] What's the matter?

1384
01:18:42,885 --> 01:18:45,388
I'm only paying the man
a compliment.

1385
01:18:45,429 --> 01:18:47,223
I'm being sincere.

1386
01:18:47,264 --> 01:18:49,183
These are high words of praise.

1387
01:18:49,225 --> 01:18:50,351
[TANJIRO] You're wrong.

1388
01:18:50,393 --> 01:18:52,645
All you're doing
is insulting him!

1389
01:18:52,687 --> 01:18:55,231
You're just spitting
on his memory!

1390
01:18:55,272 --> 01:18:56,899
On all of us!

1391
01:18:57,900 --> 01:19:00,611
You couldn't be
more wrong, Tanjiro.

1392
01:19:00,653 --> 01:19:05,324
As you'll recall, the only thing
I despise is weak human beings.

1393
01:19:05,824 --> 01:19:08,743
Only a feeble weakling
is deserving of my scorn

1394
01:19:08,785 --> 01:19:10,079
and no one else.

1395
01:19:11,080 --> 01:19:12,747
That's right.

1396
01:19:12,789 --> 01:19:16,001
The mere sight of them
makes my skin crawl.

1397
01:19:16,043 --> 01:19:17,794
They make me retch!

1398
01:19:18,795 --> 01:19:21,048
Through the laws of nature,
they are weeded out

1399
01:19:21,090 --> 01:19:23,467
from this world
just as they should be.

1400
01:19:24,385 --> 01:19:27,513
Everything you just said
is wrong!

1401
01:19:28,514 --> 01:19:29,682
[AKAZA] Huh?

1402
01:19:30,933 --> 01:19:33,185
The fact
you're even alive right now,

1403
01:19:33,227 --> 01:19:34,937
isn't that proof enough?

1404
01:19:36,272 --> 01:19:39,400
As an infant,
we're all helpless.

1405
01:19:39,442 --> 01:19:41,944
We can't live
without someone else's help.

1406
01:19:42,445 --> 01:19:44,488
You're no different, Akaza.

1407
01:19:45,489 --> 01:19:47,450
Even if you don't remember,

1408
01:19:47,491 --> 01:19:49,368
there was a time
when you were protected

1409
01:19:49,410 --> 01:19:50,994
and cared for by someone.

1410
01:19:51,036 --> 01:19:52,204
I know it!

1411
01:19:52,747 --> 01:19:54,373
That's why you're alive.

1412
01:19:59,211 --> 01:20:01,964
The strong should aid
and protect the weak.

1413
01:20:02,465 --> 01:20:04,634
And in turn,
the weak become strong

1414
01:20:04,675 --> 01:20:07,844
and aid and protect
those weaker than themselves!

1415
01:20:08,387 --> 01:20:10,514
That is the law of nature.

1416
01:20:11,056 --> 01:20:14,769
Akaza, I can't tolerate
your way of thinking.

1417
01:20:15,227 --> 01:20:16,811
Here on out,

1418
01:20:16,853 --> 01:20:19,356
I won't let you
do as you please!

1419
01:20:24,361 --> 01:20:25,862
[AKAZA] I get it now.

1420
01:20:28,699 --> 01:20:33,036
I have a disgust for this boy
that's almost primal in nature.

1421
01:20:33,746 --> 01:20:37,500
Even if he's stronger,
that feeling hasn't faded.

1422
01:20:42,296 --> 01:20:44,381
[MAN] No matter who they are,

1423
01:20:44,423 --> 01:20:47,426
everyone begins life
as a newborn.

1424
01:20:47,468 --> 01:20:50,971
We learn by getting help
from those around us.

1425
01:20:51,639 --> 01:20:54,391
We are not competing
with others.

1426
01:20:54,433 --> 01:20:58,103
The only opponent
you have in life is yourself.

1427
01:20:58,729 --> 01:21:02,775
Just focus on becoming stronger
than you were yesterday.

1428
01:21:03,942 --> 01:21:07,571
If you can stay this path
for a decade or even two,

1429
01:21:07,613 --> 01:21:09,198
that would be commendable.

1430
01:21:09,699 --> 01:21:11,158
And before you know it,

1431
01:21:11,200 --> 01:21:14,036
you will be helping others
in turn.

1432
01:21:14,704 --> 01:21:16,706
[breathing shakily]

1433
01:21:20,209 --> 01:21:21,251
[gasps]

1434
01:21:22,044 --> 01:21:23,045
[TANJIRO] What was that?

1435
01:21:23,170 --> 01:21:24,921
He just swung his fist
at nothing.

1436
01:21:31,094 --> 01:21:32,887
Tanjiro.

1437
01:21:33,764 --> 01:21:36,350
You still repulse me to my core.

1438
01:21:36,392 --> 01:21:37,434
[♪ rock music playing]

1439
01:21:37,476 --> 01:21:40,103
Destructive Death,
Crushing Type:

1440
01:21:40,145 --> 01:21:42,523
Ten Thousand Leaves
Flashing Willow!

1441
01:21:45,651 --> 01:21:47,611
[TANJIRO]
This speed, it's blinding!

1442
01:21:47,653 --> 01:21:50,322
No, it's not just his speed.

1443
01:21:50,364 --> 01:21:53,659
It's his precision,
his aura, and also--

1444
01:21:56,453 --> 01:21:57,496
[grunts]

1445
01:21:58,581 --> 01:22:00,875
Destructive Death, Leg Type.

1446
01:22:00,915 --> 01:22:01,916
[TANJIRO] Below.

1447
01:22:04,086 --> 01:22:06,296
[AKAZA] Flying Planet
Thousand Wheels!

1448
01:22:12,219 --> 01:22:14,680
[TANJIRO] Even if I could
anticipate his strikes,

1449
01:22:14,722 --> 01:22:17,808
they're so powerful,
I can't completely deflect them.

1450
01:22:17,850 --> 01:22:19,976
His techniques are so precise,

1451
01:22:20,018 --> 01:22:23,313
they can pierce through any
opening, no matter how small.

1452
01:22:26,191 --> 01:22:28,652
It's like a magnet
is attracting his attacks

1453
01:22:28,694 --> 01:22:30,654
straight toward my weak points.

1454
01:22:30,696 --> 01:22:33,741
But how? What's happening?

1455
01:22:33,783 --> 01:22:36,159
What could be
causing this behavior?

1456
01:22:36,577 --> 01:22:38,704
Come on. Think.

1457
01:22:39,996 --> 01:22:41,665
What's the answer?!

1458
01:22:41,707 --> 01:22:45,085
There must be a clue
in what Akaza's said or done.

1459
01:22:45,127 --> 01:22:47,379
[Akaza grunts] Hyah!

1460
01:22:48,422 --> 01:22:51,884
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:
Solar Heat Haze!

1461
01:22:59,642 --> 01:23:01,101
[blood spurts]

1462
01:23:01,644 --> 01:23:04,396
[chuckles]
What an interesting move.

1463
01:23:04,438 --> 01:23:08,150
I dodged it at first, but then
the blade seemed to extend.

1464
01:23:08,191 --> 01:23:10,694
I don't know what kind of swing
you put behind it,

1465
01:23:10,736 --> 01:23:12,404
but the tip of your blade
wavered

1466
01:23:12,446 --> 01:23:15,699
like it was in a heat haze.
How fascinating!

1467
01:23:18,993 --> 01:23:20,995
- [grunts]
- [glass shattering]

1468
01:23:22,456 --> 01:23:24,583
[debris crumbling]

1469
01:23:26,376 --> 01:23:29,880
[TANJIRO]
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1470
01:23:30,673 --> 01:23:31,966
[clangs]

1471
01:23:32,006 --> 01:23:33,216
My sword!

1472
01:23:34,217 --> 01:23:35,594
He'll break it!

1473
01:23:36,762 --> 01:23:39,139
[effort grunts]

1474
01:23:40,432 --> 01:23:42,225
That was a strong headbutt.

1475
01:23:43,894 --> 01:23:46,062
[TANJIRO] Damn you!
Let go of me!

1476
01:23:47,397 --> 01:23:48,941
No good. [straining]

1477
01:23:48,983 --> 01:23:51,151
I can't get him
to loosen his grip.

1478
01:23:55,322 --> 01:23:56,991
[water splashing]

1479
01:24:01,996 --> 01:24:03,163
[grunts softly]

1480
01:24:03,205 --> 01:24:04,707
Mr. Giyu!

1481
01:24:05,207 --> 01:24:07,083
[Giyu sighs]

1482
01:24:08,460 --> 01:24:11,045
You're starting
to get on my nerves.

1483
01:24:11,087 --> 01:24:13,924
Thanks to you,
my back is killing me now.

1484
01:24:14,466 --> 01:24:17,636
I'm not fond of being hurled
like a rag doll.

1485
01:24:17,678 --> 01:24:19,555
I'm gonna make you pay.

1486
01:24:20,389 --> 01:24:21,974
♪

1487
01:24:22,599 --> 01:24:26,603
Personally, I'd rather not draw
my sword if I can help it.

1488
01:24:27,103 --> 01:24:29,982
And I have a hard time
justifying using deadly force

1489
01:24:30,024 --> 01:24:31,400
if unnecessary.

1490
01:24:32,651 --> 01:24:34,486
But at this moment,

1491
01:24:34,528 --> 01:24:37,990
I'm against an opponent that
demands everything from me.

1492
01:24:38,032 --> 01:24:39,575
In the short time we fought,

1493
01:24:39,616 --> 01:24:42,202
my senses have been
pushed past their limits.

1494
01:24:43,245 --> 01:24:46,040
My dormant senses
have been rudely awakened

1495
01:24:46,080 --> 01:24:49,292
and are dragging me forward
towards the enemy.

1496
01:24:50,126 --> 01:24:53,756
I now know how much
it expands one's potential

1497
01:24:53,797 --> 01:24:55,841
to have one's back
against the wall

1498
01:24:55,883 --> 01:24:57,634
with their sword raised

1499
01:24:57,676 --> 01:24:59,428
in the face of death.

1500
01:25:02,681 --> 01:25:03,891
Mr. Giyu.

1501
01:25:09,772 --> 01:25:11,356
[♪ intense music playing]

1502
01:25:20,950 --> 01:25:23,827
[AKAZA] A mark appeared
and his movements have gotten...

1503
01:25:23,869 --> 01:25:25,245
Faster!

1504
01:25:29,792 --> 01:25:33,295
[GIYU] Water Breathing,
Fourth Form: Striking Tide!

1505
01:25:34,296 --> 01:25:36,172
[grunts softly, chuckles]

1506
01:25:41,135 --> 01:25:42,262
[grunts]

1507
01:25:47,643 --> 01:25:49,311
[TANJIRO] They're both so fast.

1508
01:25:49,352 --> 01:25:52,022
Mr. Giyu's speed increased
with the mark,

1509
01:25:52,064 --> 01:25:54,274
but Akaza adapted to it
instantly.

1510
01:25:56,735 --> 01:25:59,279
Don't tell me
that's all you're capable of!

1511
01:25:59,321 --> 01:26:01,406
[Giyu groans angrily]

1512
01:26:03,366 --> 01:26:05,744
[both grunting]

1513
01:26:08,330 --> 01:26:12,126
Show me more!
Don't you dare hold back!

1514
01:26:40,946 --> 01:26:44,574
[GIYU]
Tenth Form: Constant Flux!

1515
01:26:52,082 --> 01:26:53,667
[yelling]

1516
01:27:01,633 --> 01:27:05,012
Seventh Form:
Drop Ripple Thrust!

1517
01:27:05,054 --> 01:27:07,806
Destructive Death: Disorder!

1518
01:27:18,441 --> 01:27:21,153
[TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu! Akaza!

1519
01:27:23,363 --> 01:27:24,781
Calm down!

1520
01:27:25,574 --> 01:27:27,617
[weapons clanging]

1521
01:27:28,660 --> 01:27:30,954
Think. Don't panic.

1522
01:27:30,996 --> 01:27:33,415
Whatever you do,
don't lose focus.

1523
01:27:34,041 --> 01:27:35,291
[grunts]

1524
01:27:35,500 --> 01:27:38,754
Why is it that Akaza's attacks
are always so accurate?

1525
01:27:39,671 --> 01:27:43,717
How is he able to respond
to attacks from his blind spots?

1526
01:27:44,593 --> 01:27:45,802
Think!

1527
01:27:50,348 --> 01:27:52,434
[AKAZA] Your fighting spirit
has been tempered

1528
01:27:52,475 --> 01:27:54,144
like quality steel.

1529
01:27:54,186 --> 01:27:55,645
Your name?

1530
01:27:56,312 --> 01:27:57,522
[gasps]

1531
01:27:58,523 --> 01:28:00,692
[TANJIRO]
Back when he fought Mr. Rengoku,

1532
01:28:00,734 --> 01:28:04,404
I remember Akaza using the words
"fighting spirit."

1533
01:28:05,781 --> 01:28:07,699
What did he mean by that?

1534
01:28:07,741 --> 01:28:10,619
Is he able to sense things
through fighting spirit?

1535
01:28:11,161 --> 01:28:13,914
The same way I can sense things
through scent?

1536
01:28:28,011 --> 01:28:30,222
Wherever the enemy's aiming at,

1537
01:28:30,264 --> 01:28:32,432
I get this weird
tingling feeling.

1538
01:28:32,474 --> 01:28:36,019
So, that's how you knew Gyutaro
was attacking you from behind.

1539
01:28:36,061 --> 01:28:38,230
You sure are incredible,
Inosuke.

1540
01:28:38,272 --> 01:28:40,107
[laughs boisterously]

1541
01:28:40,149 --> 01:28:43,193
Well, my skin is tougher
than most people's.

1542
01:28:43,235 --> 01:28:45,070
And whether
it's from behind or not,

1543
01:28:45,112 --> 01:28:46,280
if someone's looking at me,

1544
01:28:46,320 --> 01:28:48,073
I know just
where they're lookin'.

1545
01:28:48,115 --> 01:28:49,658
Could you show me?

1546
01:28:49,699 --> 01:28:52,161
[laughs] Sure thing!

1547
01:28:52,911 --> 01:28:54,454
[determined grunt]

1548
01:28:56,999 --> 01:28:58,708
- It's my right shoulder.
- [gasps]

1549
01:28:58,750 --> 01:29:00,543
You really got it.
That's amazing!

1550
01:29:01,086 --> 01:29:03,505
It's even easier to know
someone's looking at me

1551
01:29:03,546 --> 01:29:05,090
if they had killing intent.

1552
01:29:05,132 --> 01:29:08,551
Since anyone who can harm me
is bad news,

1553
01:29:08,593 --> 01:29:11,305
killing intent kind of
feels like it's stabbing me

1554
01:29:11,345 --> 01:29:12,806
through the skin, you know?

1555
01:29:13,723 --> 01:29:14,975
[TANJIRO] That's right.

1556
01:29:15,017 --> 01:29:17,686
Inosuke was able
to sense the invisible

1557
01:29:17,727 --> 01:29:20,396
using only his honed
sense of touch.

1558
01:29:21,106 --> 01:29:24,442
Think back.
What else did we talk about...

1559
01:29:25,152 --> 01:29:26,320
that day?

1560
01:29:26,360 --> 01:29:28,322
Where things get real tricky

1561
01:29:28,362 --> 01:29:31,365
is when someone who doesn't have
killing intent or hostility

1562
01:29:31,407 --> 01:29:32,617
is looking at me,

1563
01:29:32,659 --> 01:29:34,953
- like that tiny hag!
- Huh?

1564
01:29:35,537 --> 01:29:36,621
[INOSUKE] That old hag

1565
01:29:36,663 --> 01:29:38,623
from the house
with the wisteria mark

1566
01:29:38,665 --> 01:29:39,958
was sneaky.

1567
01:29:40,000 --> 01:29:41,626
Before I knew it...

1568
01:29:41,668 --> 01:29:42,794
Huh?

1569
01:29:44,254 --> 01:29:47,632
...she'd be sitting right
behind me holding rice balls.

1570
01:29:48,342 --> 01:29:51,427
Calling her a "hag" isn't nice.
She's elderly.

1571
01:29:51,469 --> 01:29:53,555
- Elderly hag!
- Stop that!

1572
01:29:53,596 --> 01:29:55,557
Well, that got me thinkin'.

1573
01:29:55,598 --> 01:29:59,186
If I could hide my killing
intent, then I'd be a ninja.

1574
01:29:59,228 --> 01:30:01,521
I'd be able to sneak up
on anybody.

1575
01:30:01,563 --> 01:30:03,648
- [chuckles excitedly]
- Sure.

1576
01:30:03,690 --> 01:30:06,360
But, Inosuke,
she was only sneaky

1577
01:30:06,400 --> 01:30:09,071
'cause she didn't have
the intent of harming you.

1578
01:30:09,112 --> 01:30:11,823
And I think beheading a demon
without killing intent

1579
01:30:11,865 --> 01:30:13,200
would be impossible.

1580
01:30:13,825 --> 01:30:15,202
[INOSUKE] Hmm.

1581
01:30:15,744 --> 01:30:17,746
Yeah, you're probably right.

1582
01:30:17,787 --> 01:30:20,749
A half-hearted strike
without any killing intent

1583
01:30:20,790 --> 01:30:24,336
would never be strong enough
to cut through a demon's neck.

1584
01:30:25,254 --> 01:30:27,463
[TANJIRO]
It was a casual conversation

1585
01:30:27,505 --> 01:30:30,133
but I think Inosuke
was on to something.

1586
01:30:32,344 --> 01:30:35,264
What is it that
Akaza supposedly senses?

1587
01:30:35,305 --> 01:30:37,724
What does he mean
by "fighting spirit"?

1588
01:30:37,766 --> 01:30:39,559
Is it killing intent?

1589
01:30:39,601 --> 01:30:41,103
Is it the will to fight?

1590
01:30:41,144 --> 01:30:42,771
The time spent training?

1591
01:30:42,812 --> 01:30:44,356
Or maybe the amount?

1592
01:30:45,315 --> 01:30:46,482
Is it like the way

1593
01:30:46,566 --> 01:30:48,484
I can anticipate movements
through scent?

1594
01:30:49,819 --> 01:30:51,947
There must be something I can do

1595
01:30:52,446 --> 01:30:54,241
to disrupt his compass!

1596
01:30:57,327 --> 01:30:58,620
[♪ rock music playing]

1597
01:31:04,251 --> 01:31:06,586
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1598
01:31:08,713 --> 01:31:11,674
Just one problem
with your attack.

1599
01:31:11,716 --> 01:31:13,551
You're wide open!

1600
01:31:16,096 --> 01:31:17,597
[TANJIRO] His fist!

1601
01:31:23,353 --> 01:31:24,771
[grunts]

1602
01:31:29,192 --> 01:31:30,819
[panting]

1603
01:31:30,860 --> 01:31:32,112
Fighting spirit.

1604
01:31:32,154 --> 01:31:34,448
Instincts. Compass.

1605
01:31:34,488 --> 01:31:35,740
Perception.

1606
01:31:36,241 --> 01:31:39,869
Striking with killing intent.
Sensing the invisible.

1607
01:31:39,911 --> 01:31:42,038
Executing the impossible.

1608
01:31:42,496 --> 01:31:43,748
I see.

1609
01:31:45,459 --> 01:31:47,169
So, that's it.

1610
01:31:49,963 --> 01:31:52,132
- [birds chirping]
- [leaves rustling]

1611
01:31:55,051 --> 01:31:57,595
[laughter]

1612
01:32:04,311 --> 01:32:06,688
Um, Father?
What do you think about

1613
01:32:06,729 --> 01:32:09,149
when you dance
the Hinokami Kagura?

1614
01:32:09,732 --> 01:32:13,695
If it's too tiring for you,
I can take your place next year.

1615
01:32:14,237 --> 01:32:16,572
I don't want you
to overwork yourself.

1616
01:32:18,074 --> 01:32:19,909
Thank you, Tanjiro.

1617
01:32:20,618 --> 01:32:23,121
But to be honest,
I haven't found the Kagura

1618
01:32:23,163 --> 01:32:26,540
to be the least bit tiring
over the last few years.

1619
01:32:27,167 --> 01:32:28,918
I can't quite explain it,

1620
01:32:28,960 --> 01:32:32,422
but back when I learned it
from your grandfather years ago,

1621
01:32:32,464 --> 01:32:36,468
even though I was younger,
healthier and stronger than now,

1622
01:32:36,510 --> 01:32:39,553
I found it to be
far more tiring back then.

1623
01:32:41,806 --> 01:32:43,225
[♪ poignant music playing]

1624
01:32:43,266 --> 01:32:45,977
[TANJIRO] For generations,
the Kagura was performed

1625
01:32:46,019 --> 01:32:48,771
by the Kamado family
at the start of each year.

1626
01:32:49,272 --> 01:32:51,274
It was an exhausting performance

1627
01:32:51,316 --> 01:32:54,194
that would last
from sunset till dawn.

1628
01:32:55,404 --> 01:32:57,947
There are 12 different forms
that must be repeated

1629
01:32:57,989 --> 01:32:59,908
over and over again,

1630
01:32:59,949 --> 01:33:02,536
thousands of times
before daybreak.

1631
01:33:05,372 --> 01:33:06,873
I think my exhaustion

1632
01:33:06,915 --> 01:33:09,251
was the result
of unnecessary movement.

1633
01:33:09,751 --> 01:33:11,420
Using the correct movements

1634
01:33:11,461 --> 01:33:14,339
and breathing patterns
are vital to the dance.

1635
01:33:15,090 --> 01:33:17,967
It's what allows you
to produce maximum strength

1636
01:33:18,009 --> 01:33:19,761
while using minimal actions.

1637
01:33:19,802 --> 01:33:22,805
Once you've mastered
your breathing and movement,

1638
01:33:22,847 --> 01:33:25,517
your mind will become
transparent.

1639
01:33:26,226 --> 01:33:28,019
Transparent?

1640
01:33:28,978 --> 01:33:30,730
But before any of that,

1641
01:33:30,772 --> 01:33:33,108
you must memorize
the moves of the dance

1642
01:33:33,149 --> 01:33:36,445
and slowly ingrain them
into your muscle memory.

1643
01:33:36,486 --> 01:33:39,948
In doing so,
you'll open up your five senses

1644
01:33:39,989 --> 01:33:42,451
and become aware
of the shape of your own body,

1645
01:33:42,492 --> 01:33:44,286
vessel by vessel.

1646
01:33:45,870 --> 01:33:48,915
That was the truly
strenuous part.

1647
01:33:48,957 --> 01:33:52,294
All you can think is that
even if you go on struggling,

1648
01:33:52,335 --> 01:33:54,212
you'll never succeed.

1649
01:33:54,754 --> 01:33:56,630
After you've learned
all these things

1650
01:33:56,672 --> 01:33:58,216
and committed them to memory,

1651
01:33:58,258 --> 01:34:01,428
you'll understand how to remove
what you don't need,

1652
01:34:01,470 --> 01:34:05,307
only leaving behind in your body
what is required of you,

1653
01:34:05,348 --> 01:34:07,267
closing off the rest.

1654
01:34:07,850 --> 01:34:09,102
Closing?

1655
01:34:09,852 --> 01:34:12,105
You know how people
often close their eyes

1656
01:34:12,147 --> 01:34:14,107
when they're trying
to hear better?

1657
01:34:14,857 --> 01:34:16,692
In that same way,

1658
01:34:16,734 --> 01:34:18,820
you'll pick out the things
you need the most

1659
01:34:18,861 --> 01:34:21,490
in the movement
while eliminating the rest.

1660
01:34:22,073 --> 01:34:25,868
Eventually, you will be able
to open and close the vessels

1661
01:34:25,910 --> 01:34:29,289
and muscles in your body,
as if it were second nature.

1662
01:34:29,331 --> 01:34:32,417
The same way you blink
without a second thought.

1663
01:34:33,126 --> 01:34:34,877
When that happens,

1664
01:34:34,919 --> 01:34:38,381
a path illuminated
by a bright light will open.

1665
01:34:39,633 --> 01:34:43,553
If your mind is as clear
as possible, you'll begin to see

1666
01:34:43,595 --> 01:34:46,097
the Transparent World
before you.

1667
01:34:46,139 --> 01:34:48,517
But this domain
can only be reached

1668
01:34:48,558 --> 01:34:50,477
by pushing yourself
past your limits,

1669
01:34:50,519 --> 01:34:53,146
despite the suffering
that may be required.

1670
01:34:53,687 --> 01:34:55,398
Will I ever get to see it?

1671
01:34:56,399 --> 01:34:59,861
If you work tirelessly,
then that's for you to decide.

1672
01:35:00,570 --> 01:35:02,656
There. All done.

1673
01:35:02,696 --> 01:35:03,906
[TANJIRO] Thank you.

1674
01:35:07,577 --> 01:35:10,330
Ten days before my father died,

1675
01:35:10,372 --> 01:35:13,166
an incident where a bear
began attacking people

1676
01:35:13,208 --> 01:35:15,335
happened on
a neighboring mountain.

1677
01:35:15,835 --> 01:35:18,463
We lit bonfires around the house

1678
01:35:18,505 --> 01:35:21,341
and set up multiple ropes
lined with bells.

1679
01:35:32,894 --> 01:35:34,103
Hmm?

1680
01:35:39,942 --> 01:35:41,403
[TANJURO] Tanjiro.

1681
01:35:45,699 --> 01:35:47,367
[TANJIRO] Yes, Father?

1682
01:35:48,326 --> 01:35:49,661
[TANJURO] Come with me.

1683
01:35:50,704 --> 01:35:52,664
[Tanjiro grunting, panting]

1684
01:36:02,215 --> 01:36:03,550
[grunts]

1685
01:36:22,026 --> 01:36:24,153
[breathing unsteadily]

1686
01:36:24,987 --> 01:36:27,156
[♪ dramatic sting]

1687
01:36:31,411 --> 01:36:34,706
[loud growling]

1688
01:36:38,876 --> 01:36:41,921
[TANJURO] I understand
you must be very hungry.

1689
01:36:41,963 --> 01:36:45,174
But I'm afraid I can't allow you
to come any closer.

1690
01:36:46,342 --> 01:36:49,512
If anyone were to try
and cause harm to my family,

1691
01:36:49,554 --> 01:36:52,181
I would be forced
to show you no mercy.

1692
01:36:52,682 --> 01:36:55,017
If you disregard this warning...

1693
01:36:57,979 --> 01:37:00,898
...I'll have no choice
but to take your life.

1694
01:37:01,775 --> 01:37:03,359
- [roaring]
- [bells tinkling]

1695
01:37:03,817 --> 01:37:05,320
[thuds]

1696
01:37:05,361 --> 01:37:06,529
[gasps]

1697
01:37:10,158 --> 01:37:12,160
[bells tinkling]

1698
01:37:12,201 --> 01:37:15,997
[TANJIRO] The bear's head that
was as thick as a human torso

1699
01:37:16,038 --> 01:37:19,041
dropped to the ground
with the sound of the bells.

1700
01:37:20,960 --> 01:37:23,212
My eyes couldn't follow it.

1701
01:37:23,254 --> 01:37:24,964
But if I'm not mistaken,

1702
01:37:25,006 --> 01:37:28,343
my father slashed it twice
in the blink of an eye.

1703
01:37:29,969 --> 01:37:31,513
He must have.

1704
01:37:31,554 --> 01:37:34,683
His ax wouldn't have been
able to cut through otherwise.

1705
01:37:36,184 --> 01:37:39,729
All the while,
my father's scent never wavered.

1706
01:37:39,771 --> 01:37:42,231
Before and after
beheading the bear,

1707
01:37:42,273 --> 01:37:45,819
he emitted no fear,
no killing intent.

1708
01:37:53,075 --> 01:37:55,077
I hope that you were watching.

1709
01:37:56,120 --> 01:37:58,872
A day might come
where you have to do the same.

1710
01:37:58,914 --> 01:38:00,750
[wind blowing]

1711
01:38:01,875 --> 01:38:03,961
[TANJIRO] My father
wasn't the type of person

1712
01:38:04,003 --> 01:38:05,505
to flaunt his strength.

1713
01:38:06,214 --> 01:38:08,508
I realized later on,

1714
01:38:08,550 --> 01:38:12,554
that night, he wanted me
to see it in action.

1715
01:38:13,763 --> 01:38:16,307
The movements necessary
to be able to see

1716
01:38:16,349 --> 01:38:18,976
the Transparent World
he spoke of.

1717
01:38:21,062 --> 01:38:25,567
I'm sure my father, grandfather,
and great-grandfather

1718
01:38:26,067 --> 01:38:28,236
all learned the same way.

1719
01:38:29,863 --> 01:38:32,323
Whatever you do, never give up.

1720
01:38:32,365 --> 01:38:34,576
Always stay calm and focused.

1721
01:38:35,243 --> 01:38:38,162
Any wall you come up against
can be shattered

1722
01:38:38,705 --> 01:38:40,832
if you just work tirelessly.

1723
01:38:42,542 --> 01:38:44,419
[TANJIRO] I understand, Father.

1724
01:38:44,460 --> 01:38:46,003
In that moment...

1725
01:38:46,546 --> 01:38:47,881
that's why I was able to dodge

1726
01:38:47,921 --> 01:38:51,050
Akaza's inescapable blow
to my side.

1727
01:38:53,803 --> 01:38:55,597
If I hadn't moved in time,

1728
01:38:55,638 --> 01:38:58,099
I'm positive that strike
would have killed me.

1729
01:38:58,767 --> 01:39:01,394
When I was alternating moves
with Mr. Giyu,

1730
01:39:01,436 --> 01:39:03,979
weaving my attacks
in between each of his,

1731
01:39:04,480 --> 01:39:07,901
I was protected from being hit
by those lethal blows.

1732
01:39:08,401 --> 01:39:09,569
But in that instant,

1733
01:39:09,611 --> 01:39:12,280
even Mr. Giyu
couldn't make it in time.

1734
01:39:13,531 --> 01:39:18,536
However, for whatever reason,
I knew dodging was possible.

1735
01:39:19,036 --> 01:39:21,706
And for just a split second,

1736
01:39:21,748 --> 01:39:23,625
I was able to see it.

1737
01:39:25,376 --> 01:39:27,002
That world.

1738
01:39:28,797 --> 01:39:30,799
[♪ enchanting music playing]

1739
01:39:30,840 --> 01:39:33,342
The Transparent World.

1740
01:39:35,637 --> 01:39:38,848
Even his body
started to look transparent.

1741
01:39:39,933 --> 01:39:43,770
The same is when Hantengu
was hiding inside his own heart.

1742
01:39:44,270 --> 01:39:47,398
I don't know
if I saw him or smelled him.

1743
01:39:51,861 --> 01:39:53,279
Dodge.

1744
01:39:53,321 --> 01:39:56,532
I used only the senses
that would let me do that.

1745
01:39:57,074 --> 01:40:00,787
Without thinking, my body
moved faster than ever before.

1746
01:40:02,079 --> 01:40:05,541
When I'm inside the Transparent
World my father spoke of,

1747
01:40:05,583 --> 01:40:08,878
my battle instincts
improve drastically.

1748
01:40:10,880 --> 01:40:13,132
I can see my opponent's lungs

1749
01:40:13,174 --> 01:40:15,510
and the blood moving
throughout their body.

1750
01:40:16,009 --> 01:40:18,471
I can see
my own muscles contracting

1751
01:40:18,513 --> 01:40:21,307
faster and clearer than before.

1752
01:40:24,811 --> 01:40:27,062
If I close off
the fighting spirit

1753
01:40:27,104 --> 01:40:29,732
that Akaza
must be detecting me with,

1754
01:40:29,774 --> 01:40:31,567
I can go for his neck.

1755
01:40:32,025 --> 01:40:33,820
[screeches]

1756
01:40:44,539 --> 01:40:46,081
[TANJIRO] See it.

1757
01:40:46,123 --> 01:40:47,625
See it!

1758
01:40:47,667 --> 01:40:49,752
[exhales]

1759
01:40:49,794 --> 01:40:51,004
[♪ rock music playing]

1760
01:40:51,044 --> 01:40:52,505
It looks like
you've thrown about

1761
01:40:52,547 --> 01:40:54,632
every last Water Form at me.

1762
01:40:55,257 --> 01:40:57,802
Enough is enough,
wouldn't you say?

1763
01:40:58,386 --> 01:41:00,221
I'm putting an end to this.

1764
01:41:00,262 --> 01:41:03,391
But you have my respect
for lasting so long!

1765
01:41:04,893 --> 01:41:06,019
[GIYU] What?

1766
01:41:07,144 --> 01:41:09,146
In the middle of my downswing...

1767
01:41:10,606 --> 01:41:12,441
...he hit it from the side.

1768
01:41:14,067 --> 01:41:15,820
And snapped my sword!

1769
01:41:16,404 --> 01:41:18,698
- Goodbye, Giyu.
- [impact grunts]

1770
01:41:22,827 --> 01:41:24,620
[flesh squelching]

1771
01:41:25,580 --> 01:41:28,207
[muted silence]

1772
01:41:28,958 --> 01:41:30,001
[thuds]

1773
01:41:30,043 --> 01:41:32,169
[♪ intense dramatic music
playing]

1774
01:41:42,304 --> 01:41:45,307
- [exhales]
- [flame roaring]

1775
01:41:47,977 --> 01:41:51,188
[GIYU] He stopped the attack
by cutting off his fist.

1776
01:41:51,230 --> 01:41:53,315
His breathing is different.

1777
01:41:53,357 --> 01:41:54,984
And his appearance...

1778
01:41:56,277 --> 01:41:58,696
I've been saved by Tanjiro.

1779
01:42:00,073 --> 01:42:01,991
[AKAZA]
All of the cells in my body

1780
01:42:02,033 --> 01:42:03,618
down to the ones in my hair

1781
01:42:03,659 --> 01:42:06,871
are screaming at me to kill him
as soon as possible.

1782
01:42:08,581 --> 01:42:11,626
I don't know what kind of change
he underwent, but...

1783
01:42:12,877 --> 01:42:14,587
...he's dangerous.

1784
01:42:16,129 --> 01:42:18,299
[GIYU] His focus is on Tanjiro.

1785
01:42:19,383 --> 01:42:21,010
Now's my chance.

1786
01:42:25,389 --> 01:42:28,225
[AKAZA] Technique Development,
Final Form:

1787
01:42:28,768 --> 01:42:31,144
Blue Silver Chaotic Afterglow!

1788
01:42:34,356 --> 01:42:36,734
[GIYU] His attack speed
boosted again,

1789
01:42:36,776 --> 01:42:38,486
and the force is increased.

1790
01:42:38,945 --> 01:42:42,615
My only chance now
is with Dead Calm!

1791
01:43:04,345 --> 01:43:07,180
[TANJIRO] This must be
what Father was talking about.

1792
01:43:07,682 --> 01:43:11,519
This is it.
The Transparent World.

1793
01:43:19,318 --> 01:43:25,825
Strange. It feels like
time is passing by so slowly.

1794
01:43:27,535 --> 01:43:32,205
Or maybe... their movements
just look slower now.

1795
01:43:32,247 --> 01:43:34,416
[♪ intense music continues]

1796
01:43:35,459 --> 01:43:36,794
[groans]

1797
01:43:38,171 --> 01:43:40,131
[GIYU] It's no use.

1798
01:43:40,173 --> 01:43:43,258
A hundred strikes at once
is unavoidable.

1799
01:43:43,759 --> 01:43:45,386
Even with Dead Calm,

1800
01:43:45,427 --> 01:43:48,181
I still wasn't able
to block all of them.

1801
01:43:49,515 --> 01:43:51,350
[AKAZA] Stand proud, Giyu.

1802
01:43:51,392 --> 01:43:54,227
Most wouldn't have been
able to survive that.

1803
01:43:54,269 --> 01:43:57,190
You must have evaded
my fatal blows.

1804
01:43:57,982 --> 01:44:01,986
There's no need for you to die
like Kyojuro and Tanjiro did.

1805
01:44:02,028 --> 01:44:05,073
Give up your pride
and become a demon, Giyu.

1806
01:44:06,824 --> 01:44:10,285
[GIYU] Tanjiro's behind him
and he hasn't noticed?

1807
01:44:10,828 --> 01:44:13,372
- [Akaza speaking indistinctly]
- Is he masking his presence?

1808
01:44:13,414 --> 01:44:15,041
Now's our chance!

1809
01:44:15,875 --> 01:44:17,543
Tanjiro, do it!

1810
01:44:17,585 --> 01:44:20,004
If you have the strength,
behead him.

1811
01:44:20,504 --> 01:44:22,423
Before he notices you,

1812
01:44:22,464 --> 01:44:23,966
go for it!

1813
01:44:24,008 --> 01:44:27,887
Akaza!
Prepare to be decapitated!

1814
01:44:27,929 --> 01:44:29,180
[AKAZA] Huh?

1815
01:44:33,726 --> 01:44:36,269
[GIYU] He willingly
gave himself away!

1816
01:44:36,896 --> 01:44:38,689
[AKAZA] He's still alive?

1817
01:44:39,148 --> 01:44:41,109
I never would have thought
someone like him

1818
01:44:41,150 --> 01:44:43,360
could survive
an attack like that.

1819
01:44:43,903 --> 01:44:45,613
Well, it doesn't matter.

1820
01:44:45,654 --> 01:44:48,074
After all, my Destructive Death,
Compass Needle

1821
01:44:48,116 --> 01:44:49,700
can detect any attack!

1822
01:44:50,159 --> 01:44:53,495
The stronger my opponent's
fighting spirit is,

1823
01:44:53,537 --> 01:44:56,457
the greater
my Compass Needle's reaction.

1824
01:44:57,833 --> 01:44:59,043
[quivers]

1825
01:44:59,627 --> 01:45:01,336
What is this?

1826
01:45:01,796 --> 01:45:04,465
What is this odd presence
he's emitting?

1827
01:45:04,506 --> 01:45:06,467
It feels like
he's turned himself

1828
01:45:06,508 --> 01:45:08,301
into some other creature.

1829
01:45:08,343 --> 01:45:09,637
It's like...

1830
01:45:11,055 --> 01:45:13,599
...his fighting spirit is gone.

1831
01:45:13,641 --> 01:45:14,934
But how?

1832
01:45:14,976 --> 01:45:17,728
I have to calm down. Focus!

1833
01:45:18,187 --> 01:45:19,563
[grunts]

1834
01:45:20,313 --> 01:45:21,774
[flame roaring]

1835
01:45:24,068 --> 01:45:26,112
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1836
01:45:26,154 --> 01:45:28,739
Setting Sun Transformation.

1837
01:45:28,781 --> 01:45:30,950
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1838
01:45:31,784 --> 01:45:33,911
[tinkling]

1839
01:45:46,841 --> 01:45:47,967
[gasps]

1840
01:45:50,219 --> 01:45:52,930
[Akaza straining]
This can't be possible.

1841
01:45:55,516 --> 01:45:57,893
[Tanjiro exhales]

1842
01:45:59,937 --> 01:46:02,231
[AKAZA] In the last
several hundred years,

1843
01:46:02,273 --> 01:46:05,734
I've never once seen a human
without any fighting spirit.

1844
01:46:06,194 --> 01:46:09,197
Even newborn children
had traces of it.

1845
01:46:09,780 --> 01:46:12,283
And yet, in that instant,

1846
01:46:12,325 --> 01:46:14,243
his fighting spirit vanished

1847
01:46:14,285 --> 01:46:16,704
as if it were never there
to begin with.

1848
01:46:20,208 --> 01:46:22,501
It's as if
I was facing an anomaly

1849
01:46:22,543 --> 01:46:24,253
that shouldn't even exist.

1850
01:46:24,295 --> 01:46:27,006
So, my senses
were thrown into confusion.

1851
01:46:27,464 --> 01:46:30,509
My Compass Needle
detected nothing.

1852
01:46:31,052 --> 01:46:32,511
[tinkling]

1853
01:46:32,553 --> 01:46:35,597
But that's not the biggest issue
at hand here.

1854
01:46:35,639 --> 01:46:37,350
When on the battlefield,

1855
01:46:37,390 --> 01:46:40,019
there's no telling
what could come your way.

1856
01:46:40,061 --> 01:46:42,730
It's vital that you're able
to deal with the unexpected

1857
01:46:42,771 --> 01:46:44,273
at a moment's notice.

1858
01:46:44,773 --> 01:46:47,026
And I'm able to do that!

1859
01:46:47,651 --> 01:46:50,571
Or at least... I thought so.

1860
01:46:51,488 --> 01:46:54,200
But during that short battle,

1861
01:46:54,242 --> 01:46:58,704
he was able to grasp something
and use it to surpass my speed.

1862
01:46:59,205 --> 01:47:01,665
Whatever it was he learned
was able to shatter

1863
01:47:01,707 --> 01:47:04,001
centuries' worth
of martial arts techniques

1864
01:47:04,043 --> 01:47:06,045
with a single head-on attack.

1865
01:47:06,754 --> 01:47:10,883
Within those eyes of his,
there was no hatred, no rage,

1866
01:47:10,925 --> 01:47:14,011
no killing intent
or fighting spirit.

1867
01:47:14,678 --> 01:47:17,639
He must have somehow seen
what I'd been looking for:

1868
01:47:17,681 --> 01:47:22,061
the domain that lies
within the realm of the highest.

1869
01:47:23,771 --> 01:47:26,315
None other than
the selfless state.

1870
01:47:28,441 --> 01:47:31,112
For some time now,
I've had a vague sense

1871
01:47:31,153 --> 01:47:33,197
that this state of mind existed.

1872
01:47:33,655 --> 01:47:36,242
And yet, even after
all these centuries,

1873
01:47:36,284 --> 01:47:38,077
I've yet to attain it.

1874
01:47:45,584 --> 01:47:46,627
[gasps]

1875
01:47:47,211 --> 01:47:48,837
[AKAZA] Not yet!

1876
01:47:48,879 --> 01:47:50,589
I can still fight!

1877
01:47:50,631 --> 01:47:53,259
I will continue
to become stronger!

1878
01:47:59,514 --> 01:48:02,601
[TANJIRO] This is bad.
He's reattaching his head!

1879
01:48:03,060 --> 01:48:05,187
[effort grunting]

1880
01:48:06,855 --> 01:48:09,066
- [thuds]
- [gasps]

1881
01:48:11,735 --> 01:48:14,113
[AKAZA] I can't die here.

1882
01:48:15,488 --> 01:48:17,325
Not like this.

1883
01:48:20,328 --> 01:48:23,080
I have to become stronger.

1884
01:48:25,166 --> 01:48:28,501
Stronger than anyone else
in the whole world!

1885
01:48:28,543 --> 01:48:30,338
Stronger!

1886
01:48:30,796 --> 01:48:32,589
- [thuds]
- [fizzles out]

1887
01:48:32,631 --> 01:48:35,801
I have to find a way
to become stronger.

1888
01:48:37,886 --> 01:48:39,013
[clatters]

1889
01:48:42,933 --> 01:48:44,268
[body thuds]

1890
01:48:45,227 --> 01:48:48,147
[TANJIRO] That's it. It's over.

1891
01:48:49,857 --> 01:48:51,275
We won!

1892
01:48:52,234 --> 01:48:53,568
[sighs in relief]

1893
01:48:53,944 --> 01:48:55,863
[grunts in pain]

1894
01:48:56,238 --> 01:48:57,906
So lightheaded.

1895
01:48:59,741 --> 01:49:01,910
My muscles are cramping up.

1896
01:49:01,952 --> 01:49:04,079
My body's reached its limit.

1897
01:49:06,707 --> 01:49:09,502
Tanjiro, are you all ri--
[gasps]

1898
01:49:10,336 --> 01:49:13,047
His body
hasn't disintegrated yet.

1899
01:49:13,088 --> 01:49:15,716
Does... Does this mean...

1900
01:49:16,175 --> 01:49:17,218
Tan--

1901
01:49:17,885 --> 01:49:19,303
[♪ intense music playing]

1902
01:49:19,345 --> 01:49:20,679
[grunts]

1903
01:49:27,560 --> 01:49:31,357
[TANJIRO] He's moving!
His body is still intact!

1904
01:49:31,399 --> 01:49:33,650
The severed part is closing up!

1905
01:49:34,860 --> 01:49:36,737
[strained grunting]

1906
01:49:36,778 --> 01:49:38,655
I can't see straight.

1907
01:49:38,697 --> 01:49:40,282
I can't.

1908
01:49:43,618 --> 01:49:44,828
[impact grunts]

1909
01:49:49,875 --> 01:49:51,210
[strained gasping]

1910
01:49:51,252 --> 01:49:54,046
No. No way.

1911
01:49:54,088 --> 01:49:56,465
Slashing his neck
didn't kill him!

1912
01:49:56,507 --> 01:49:59,968
Is there some kind of condition
like with Gyutaro and Daki?

1913
01:50:00,428 --> 01:50:01,470
That can't be it.

1914
01:50:02,012 --> 01:50:05,516
His head disintegrated,
yet he hasn't given up!

1915
01:50:06,016 --> 01:50:09,353
It's like he's trying to evolve!

1916
01:50:11,188 --> 01:50:12,481
[impact grunts]

1917
01:50:15,650 --> 01:50:17,111
If we don't do something,

1918
01:50:17,152 --> 01:50:19,988
his head will stop
being his weak point like Muzan!

1919
01:50:20,655 --> 01:50:22,699
This battle isn't over yet.

1920
01:50:22,741 --> 01:50:24,659
I have to fight...

1921
01:50:25,411 --> 01:50:26,537
Tanjiro!

1922
01:50:26,579 --> 01:50:28,163
He's fainted.

1923
01:50:28,205 --> 01:50:29,748
Of course he has.

1924
01:50:29,790 --> 01:50:32,376
He's long since
passed his limit.

1925
01:50:37,214 --> 01:50:38,882
[grunts]

1926
01:50:42,010 --> 01:50:45,180
Water Breathing, Fourth Form:

1927
01:50:45,222 --> 01:50:47,682
[♪ epic music playing]

1928
01:50:47,724 --> 01:50:49,518
Striking Tide!

1929
01:50:54,482 --> 01:50:56,108
Ridiculous!

1930
01:50:56,150 --> 01:50:59,194
He lost his head and can still
regenerate that quickly?

1931
01:50:59,945 --> 01:51:02,072
[sword clanking]

1932
01:51:03,198 --> 01:51:05,326
[grunting]

1933
01:51:11,957 --> 01:51:14,876
[yelling]

1934
01:51:19,256 --> 01:51:21,216
- [coughs]
- [blood splatters]

1935
01:51:23,552 --> 01:51:25,929
I can't hear out of my left ear,

1936
01:51:25,971 --> 01:51:28,056
and my right hand has gone numb.

1937
01:51:29,475 --> 01:51:33,020
I can still grip my sword,
but who knows for how long.

1938
01:51:41,694 --> 01:51:42,779
Wait!

1939
01:51:43,864 --> 01:51:44,990
I...

1940
01:51:45,616 --> 01:51:48,701
I'm here. I'm still alive!

1941
01:51:49,203 --> 01:51:53,748
If you wanna kill Tanjiro,
you'll have to defeat me first!

1942
01:51:57,836 --> 01:52:00,088
[AKAZA] An indomitable spirit.

1943
01:52:00,130 --> 01:52:01,632
It will never bend,

1944
01:52:01,674 --> 01:52:04,717
no matter what crisis
it finds itself in.

1945
01:52:05,511 --> 01:52:08,180
We don't fight the way
samurai do.

1946
01:52:08,222 --> 01:52:10,265
We don't carry weapons,

1947
01:52:10,307 --> 01:52:13,435
though we carry our convictions
like swords.

1948
01:52:14,978 --> 01:52:18,273
[MAN] Though we carry
our convictions like swords,

1949
01:52:18,982 --> 01:52:23,028
our battles are waged
with our fists.

1950
01:52:24,446 --> 01:52:27,533
[AKAZA] You are such an eyesore!

1951
01:52:30,327 --> 01:52:31,704
[soft thump]

1952
01:52:38,043 --> 01:52:39,587
[GIRL] Please stop.

1953
01:52:45,800 --> 01:52:47,386
[AKAZA] Who is that?

1954
01:52:52,725 --> 01:52:54,685
Mr. Hakuji,

1955
01:52:54,727 --> 01:52:56,520
please, that's enough!

1956
01:52:56,562 --> 01:52:58,105
[♪ poignant music playing]

1957
01:52:59,648 --> 01:53:03,776
[AKAZA] Let go.
Let go of my hand.

1958
01:53:04,236 --> 01:53:05,778
Just who are you?

1959
01:53:07,573 --> 01:53:10,867
Stop. You don't
have to keep going. [sniffles]

1960
01:53:10,909 --> 01:53:13,454
Let's leave this place together.

1961
01:53:13,828 --> 01:53:15,748
[AKAZA] I can't.

1962
01:53:15,788 --> 01:53:19,126
I've still got unfinished
business with those two.

1963
01:53:20,502 --> 01:53:22,504
[GIRL]
What do you mean by that?

1964
01:53:23,088 --> 01:53:25,299
[AKAZA]
I've got to become stronger.

1965
01:53:25,340 --> 01:53:26,759
I've got to!

1966
01:53:27,259 --> 01:53:30,304
I'll kill anyone
who gets in my way.

1967
01:53:31,012 --> 01:53:33,724
Why do you want that? [sniffles]

1968
01:53:33,766 --> 01:53:36,809
For what reason
do you need to become stronger?

1969
01:53:38,353 --> 01:53:42,483
[AKAZA] Because...
unless I'm strong enough,

1970
01:53:42,524 --> 01:53:45,860
I won't be able to bring
any more back home to him.

1971
01:53:47,988 --> 01:53:50,282
He needs medicine.

1972
01:53:52,326 --> 01:53:55,162
I must become stronger.

1973
01:53:55,912 --> 01:53:57,205
[grunts angrily]

1974
01:53:57,539 --> 01:54:00,875
If I don't, I won't be able to
get away with the money I stole.

1975
01:54:02,210 --> 01:54:04,004
If I happen to be caught,

1976
01:54:04,045 --> 01:54:06,381
I won't be able
to defend myself.

1977
01:54:07,800 --> 01:54:09,551
If I'm not strong enough,

1978
01:54:09,593 --> 01:54:13,221
the magistrate will catch me
and have me beaten and lashed.

1979
01:54:13,681 --> 01:54:15,766
[whipping]

1980
01:54:16,642 --> 01:54:18,101
[MAGISTRATE]
We've already given you

1981
01:54:18,143 --> 01:54:21,021
three tattoos on each arm
for stealing.

1982
01:54:21,062 --> 01:54:23,607
Next time,
we'll chop off your hand.

1983
01:54:23,649 --> 01:54:25,192
[Hakuji chuckling]

1984
01:54:27,902 --> 01:54:29,904
[laughing]

1985
01:54:31,615 --> 01:54:33,659
[ATTENDANT]
Bow your head and repent!

1986
01:54:33,701 --> 01:54:36,036
If you're gonna chop it off,
then do it!

1987
01:54:36,077 --> 01:54:38,955
Go ahead and take both of them
if you're really serious.

1988
01:54:38,997 --> 01:54:41,166
I'll just use my feet to steal.

1989
01:54:41,208 --> 01:54:44,169
You're not gonna catch me again,
so make it count!

1990
01:54:46,630 --> 01:54:50,091
[MAGISTRATE] To hear this from
someone at such a young age.

1991
01:54:50,133 --> 01:54:52,761
This boy of 11 has already
taken on punishments

1992
01:54:52,803 --> 01:54:55,222
that would make
a grown man faint.

1993
01:54:56,473 --> 01:54:58,433
You are a demon child!

1994
01:54:58,475 --> 01:55:00,644
Go and call me
whatever names you want.

1995
01:55:00,686 --> 01:55:03,355
"Demon child" suits me
just damn fine!

1996
01:55:03,397 --> 01:55:05,649
They say I already had teeth
when I was born,

1997
01:55:05,691 --> 01:55:06,650
so I guess I am.

1998
01:55:06,692 --> 01:55:08,943
- Be quiet!
- Dirty little punk!

1999
01:55:08,985 --> 01:55:12,072
[HAKUJI] Don't you mean
"demon child," you bastard?

2000
01:55:12,113 --> 01:55:14,366
[grunts]

2001
01:55:15,826 --> 01:55:16,869
Hmph!

2002
01:55:16,909 --> 01:55:20,414
SOUTH TOWN MAGISTRATE'S OFFICE

2003
01:55:20,455 --> 01:55:21,540
[birds calling]

2004
01:55:21,582 --> 01:55:22,708
[MAN 1] Hakuji!

2005
01:55:22,750 --> 01:55:25,001
[MAN 2] Oh! [panting]
There you are!

2006
01:55:25,043 --> 01:55:27,504
[voice breaking] When you were
caught for stealing again,

2007
01:55:27,546 --> 01:55:30,758
word about it made its way
back to your father.

2008
01:55:31,299 --> 01:55:33,802
He hung himself, Hakuji!

2009
01:55:34,261 --> 01:55:35,303
Huh?

2010
01:55:38,515 --> 01:55:40,768
[Hakuji's father weakly]
"Dear Hakuji,

2011
01:55:41,894 --> 01:55:44,020
live an honest life.

2012
01:55:44,605 --> 01:55:46,815
You can still start over."

2013
01:55:47,608 --> 01:55:49,777
- [wind blowing]
- [leaves rustling]

2014
01:55:51,737 --> 01:55:52,780
[♪ poignant music continues]

2015
01:55:52,821 --> 01:55:54,030
[paper fluttering]

2016
01:55:54,072 --> 01:55:56,450
[HAKUJI]
What kind of world is this?

2017
01:55:56,491 --> 01:55:59,202
Are the poor
not even allowed to live?

2018
01:56:04,207 --> 01:56:05,375
[voice breaking] Dad.

2019
01:56:07,628 --> 01:56:09,755
To hell with this rotten world.

2020
01:56:09,797 --> 01:56:12,006
To all of it! [sobbing]

2021
01:56:14,509 --> 01:56:18,722
Every rotten human,
they can all burn in hell!

2022
01:56:18,764 --> 01:56:20,973
[grunts angrily]

2023
01:56:22,643 --> 01:56:26,062
Why do scumbags like them
get the privilege of living

2024
01:56:26,104 --> 01:56:29,357
when my father had to die
in such a horrible way?

2025
01:56:29,399 --> 01:56:31,984
He was never a burden to me.

2026
01:56:32,026 --> 01:56:34,112
So why would he feel that way?

2027
01:56:34,571 --> 01:56:37,908
You didn't do anything wrong,
Dad. You didn't!

2028
01:56:39,910 --> 01:56:42,203
I never cared
about getting beaten

2029
01:56:42,245 --> 01:56:44,122
after I was caught stealing.

2030
01:56:44,164 --> 01:56:47,960
Even if they beat me until every
bone in my body was broken,

2031
01:56:48,000 --> 01:56:50,044
I could take it all
for you, Dad.

2032
01:56:50,086 --> 01:56:51,463
For centuries even.

2033
01:56:51,505 --> 01:56:54,174
Learn your lesson!
Live an honest life!

2034
01:56:54,925 --> 01:56:57,928
[HAKUJI] Why don't you
shut the hell up, you scumbag?

2035
01:56:57,970 --> 01:56:59,930
Medicine's expensive.

2036
01:56:59,972 --> 01:57:02,641
The hell do you expect me
to do about that?

2037
01:57:04,100 --> 01:57:07,729
My dad's only getting thinner
and thinner by the day.

2038
01:57:08,814 --> 01:57:11,900
He's so malnourished,
you can see his bones.

2039
01:57:12,484 --> 01:57:15,863
I just want him to have
something better to eat.

2040
01:57:18,114 --> 01:57:20,826
I would have happily
given my life...

2041
01:57:22,744 --> 01:57:24,955
[voice breaking]
...if it meant saving his.

2042
01:57:31,085 --> 01:57:35,089
I'd have done anything...
for my father!

2043
01:57:37,968 --> 01:57:40,178
[breathing heavily]

2044
01:57:40,220 --> 01:57:43,097
- [clapping]
- Huh?

2045
01:57:43,139 --> 01:57:44,224
SORYU

2046
01:57:44,307 --> 01:57:46,351
[MAN] Well, well.
I am quite impressed.

2047
01:57:46,393 --> 01:57:48,979
I was called over
because someone said that

2048
01:57:49,021 --> 01:57:50,480
a child was about to be killed.

2049
01:57:50,522 --> 01:57:53,942
But you've laid out seven
grown-ups with your bare fists.

2050
01:57:53,984 --> 01:57:56,319
You've got some talent,
don't ya?

2051
01:57:56,361 --> 01:58:00,114
Not just anyone can take on
that many guys and still win.

2052
01:58:00,156 --> 01:58:02,784
[chuckling] That's the kind of
spunk I like to see.

2053
01:58:04,995 --> 01:58:07,121
[AKAZA] What's going on here?

2054
01:58:07,163 --> 01:58:09,165
Who is this man?

2055
01:58:10,166 --> 01:58:12,502
Could these be my memories?

2056
01:58:12,544 --> 01:58:14,546
How about you join my dojo?

2057
01:58:14,588 --> 01:58:16,798
I don't have any students
at the moment.

2058
01:58:17,257 --> 01:58:19,259
Stay out of my way,
you old fart!

2059
01:58:19,300 --> 01:58:20,761
You lookin' to die?

2060
01:58:20,802 --> 01:58:22,679
- Those tattoos.
- Uh?

2061
01:58:22,721 --> 01:58:24,347
You're a criminal from Edo.

2062
01:58:25,015 --> 01:58:26,892
I'm guessing
after being thrown out,

2063
01:58:26,934 --> 01:58:29,603
you eventually
found your way here.

2064
01:58:29,644 --> 01:58:31,646
I never asked for your opinion.

2065
01:58:31,688 --> 01:58:34,148
Now shut up
and get the hell out of my way!

2066
01:58:34,190 --> 01:58:37,778
[scoffs] All right.
Time to be reborn!

2067
01:58:38,653 --> 01:58:40,196
You ready?

2068
01:58:41,073 --> 01:58:45,410
That's it. Drop dead, old man!
[grunting]

2069
01:58:46,160 --> 01:58:47,412
[impact grunts]

2070
01:58:55,629 --> 01:58:58,090
[strained grunt, coughs, gasps]

2071
01:58:58,130 --> 01:58:59,466
[body thuds]

2072
01:59:03,135 --> 01:59:04,471
SORYU

2073
01:59:04,512 --> 01:59:06,473
[MAN] I'll give it to you.
You're tough.

2074
01:59:06,514 --> 01:59:07,474
DOJO

2075
01:59:07,515 --> 01:59:09,141
After that beating I gave you,

2076
01:59:09,183 --> 01:59:11,311
you came to
in less than an hour.

2077
01:59:12,353 --> 01:59:13,730
The name's Keizo.

2078
01:59:14,397 --> 01:59:16,316
I teach
the Soryu style of fighting

2079
01:59:16,357 --> 01:59:18,819
which uses only your bare hands.

2080
01:59:18,860 --> 01:59:21,989
Like I said, I don't have
any other students.

2081
01:59:22,489 --> 01:59:26,200
So I get by by doing whatever
odd jobs I can for people.

2082
01:59:28,787 --> 01:59:31,498
I have a daughter
who's in rather poor health.

2083
01:59:31,539 --> 01:59:33,917
I'd like you
to help look after her.

2084
01:59:34,417 --> 01:59:37,838
I'd be here if I could,
but I have to work.

2085
01:59:38,839 --> 01:59:41,299
My wife was pushed
to the edge of exhaustion

2086
01:59:41,341 --> 01:59:42,801
and drowned herself.

2087
01:59:43,802 --> 01:59:46,346
Life sure takes a bite
out of you, doesn't it?

2088
01:59:50,475 --> 01:59:52,435
If I were a more capable man,

2089
01:59:52,477 --> 01:59:55,229
my wife and daughter wouldn't
have suffered like this.

2090
01:59:58,232 --> 02:00:00,568
You said you knew
I was a criminal.

2091
02:00:00,610 --> 02:00:03,822
Are you really all right leaving
your daughter around me?

2092
02:00:05,197 --> 02:00:06,783
Why wouldn't I be?

2093
02:00:06,825 --> 02:00:09,577
I pummeled the criminal
out of you earlier, didn't I?

2094
02:00:09,619 --> 02:00:10,704
It's fine.

2095
02:00:11,579 --> 02:00:13,790
[♪ tender music playing]

2096
02:00:13,832 --> 02:00:15,959
[AKAZA] They are alike.

2097
02:00:23,591 --> 02:00:25,468
I get it now.

2098
02:00:26,761 --> 02:00:29,430
The reason
you disgusted me earlier.

2099
02:00:29,931 --> 02:00:31,141
It was because you would've

2100
02:00:31,183 --> 02:00:34,310
dredged up memories
of my worthless past.

2101
02:00:39,273 --> 02:00:41,818
[KEIZO]
This is my daughter, Koyuki.

2102
02:00:42,485 --> 02:00:43,862
[coughing]

2103
02:00:44,821 --> 02:00:47,281
[AKAZA] My worthless past.

2104
02:00:50,535 --> 02:00:51,953
Worthless.

2105
02:00:56,083 --> 02:00:58,919
[coughing]

2106
02:01:01,088 --> 02:01:04,507
Hakuji, I'm so sorry.

2107
02:01:05,383 --> 02:01:07,594
[chuckles] How are you feeling?

2108
02:01:07,635 --> 02:01:09,637
[coughing]

2109
02:01:09,679 --> 02:01:11,389
You okay being up?

2110
02:01:12,390 --> 02:01:13,433
[KOYUKI] Hmm.

2111
02:01:14,101 --> 02:01:17,395
Looks like you've got more color
in your cheeks this morning.

2112
02:01:17,437 --> 02:01:19,189
[chuckles] That's good.

2113
02:01:19,856 --> 02:01:20,941
Hmm.

2114
02:01:21,524 --> 02:01:24,778
- Huh?
- Oh, yeah. This boy.

2115
02:01:24,819 --> 02:01:26,863
His name is... [chuckles]

2116
02:01:26,905 --> 02:01:30,158
Well, I've asked him countless
times, and he won't say.

2117
02:01:30,200 --> 02:01:32,326
- Go on, get inside.
- [grunts]

2118
02:01:34,037 --> 02:01:35,247
Have a seat.

2119
02:01:37,040 --> 02:01:40,043
I wanna know his name
when I get back. Okay?

2120
02:01:51,638 --> 02:01:52,889
Um...

2121
02:01:53,347 --> 02:01:56,392
Your... Your face.

2122
02:01:56,977 --> 02:01:58,394
You're hurt.

2123
02:01:58,979 --> 02:02:00,521
Are you all right?

2124
02:02:03,775 --> 02:02:05,777
[AKAZA] "I'll make you better.

2125
02:02:05,819 --> 02:02:07,612
I'll save you.

2126
02:02:07,654 --> 02:02:09,030
Protect you."

2127
02:02:09,656 --> 02:02:14,202
In that past life, all I did
was spew a bunch of lies.

2128
02:02:14,661 --> 02:02:16,370
I was so pathetic.

2129
02:02:18,248 --> 02:02:20,708
[birds chirping]

2130
02:02:25,839 --> 02:02:28,258
[coughing]

2131
02:02:32,971 --> 02:02:34,639
Oh, thank you.

2132
02:02:36,141 --> 02:02:38,893
[HAKUJI] You don't have to
thank me every time, you know.

2133
02:02:38,935 --> 02:02:40,687
Just focus on resting.

2134
02:02:42,438 --> 02:02:46,318
I'm sorry for causing you
trouble like this.

2135
02:02:46,358 --> 02:02:48,486
It's fine. Really.

2136
02:02:50,322 --> 02:02:53,116
Koyuki, you want this closed?

2137
02:02:53,908 --> 02:02:57,329
Hmm. You can leave it open.

2138
02:02:59,247 --> 02:03:02,042
[HAKUJI] Koyuki was very
delicate and frail.

2139
02:03:03,459 --> 02:03:07,297
I would change out her towels
and nightgown and give her water

2140
02:03:07,339 --> 02:03:08,965
even throughout the night.

2141
02:03:09,549 --> 02:03:12,344
And whenever she needed
to use the lavatory,

2142
02:03:12,384 --> 02:03:14,721
obviously she was too weak
to be able to go

2143
02:03:14,762 --> 02:03:16,306
without needing assistance.

2144
02:03:20,268 --> 02:03:23,521
I was used to taking care
of the sick because of my dad,

2145
02:03:23,563 --> 02:03:27,275
and since I had an almost
inhuman physical endurance,

2146
02:03:27,317 --> 02:03:29,569
it really wasn't a big deal
for me.

2147
02:03:32,113 --> 02:03:34,532
[crows cawing]

2148
02:03:34,574 --> 02:03:37,035
Sorry to make you help me
all day.

2149
02:03:43,624 --> 02:03:46,460
[HAKUJI] Why do people
who are suffering from illness

2150
02:03:46,502 --> 02:03:48,922
always feel the need to say
they're sorry?

2151
02:03:49,797 --> 02:03:52,217
"Sorry to make you
do things for me."

2152
02:03:52,759 --> 02:03:55,345
"Sorry if my coughing's
bothering you."

2153
02:03:55,970 --> 02:03:59,099
"Sorry I can't put food
on the table like I should."

2154
02:04:01,184 --> 02:04:04,062
They didn't choose
to have to live this way.

2155
02:04:04,104 --> 02:04:06,314
Of course
they wanna breathe normally.

2156
02:04:06,356 --> 02:04:08,733
They can't help it
if they start coughing.

2157
02:04:09,984 --> 02:04:11,485
Out of everyone,

2158
02:04:11,527 --> 02:04:14,030
they're the ones
suffering the most.

2159
02:04:16,783 --> 02:04:19,244
Sorry again to make you do this.

2160
02:04:19,786 --> 02:04:21,621
Because of my sickness,

2161
02:04:21,662 --> 02:04:24,165
you're not able to do
your training,

2162
02:04:24,207 --> 02:04:26,542
or even go out and have fun.

2163
02:04:27,419 --> 02:04:29,421
[HAKUJI]
I don't care about having fun.

2164
02:04:29,461 --> 02:04:30,797
I never have.

2165
02:04:31,589 --> 02:04:34,759
As far as training goes,
I squeeze it in whenever I can,

2166
02:04:34,801 --> 02:04:36,303
so, it's fine.

2167
02:04:37,595 --> 02:04:38,679
Are you sure?

2168
02:04:39,347 --> 02:04:42,392
Even you need to take
a little break.

2169
02:04:43,226 --> 02:04:46,771
I hear there are fireworks
happening tonight.

2170
02:04:46,813 --> 02:04:48,480
You should go see them.

2171
02:04:49,816 --> 02:04:51,609
Fireworks, huh?

2172
02:04:51,651 --> 02:04:54,112
If you don't feel nauseous
at night,

2173
02:04:54,154 --> 02:04:57,657
I could carry you on my back
and go see them on the bridge.

2174
02:04:57,698 --> 02:04:58,908
Huh?

2175
02:05:02,454 --> 02:05:04,538
If you're not feeling up to it,

2176
02:05:04,580 --> 02:05:07,708
they'll do fireworks again
next year, and after that.

2177
02:05:07,750 --> 02:05:09,919
So, we can just go
when you're better.

2178
02:05:14,841 --> 02:05:16,759
[crying softly]

2179
02:05:18,510 --> 02:05:21,014
There was one thing
that was hard

2180
02:05:21,055 --> 02:05:22,514
about taking care of her.

2181
02:05:22,682 --> 02:05:25,601
And that was whenever she would
suddenly break out into tears

2182
02:05:25,643 --> 02:05:27,519
in the middle
of our conversations.

2183
02:05:28,188 --> 02:05:32,233
I can imagine how she felt,
bedridden and sick as she was,

2184
02:05:32,692 --> 02:05:35,111
but it still made me
uncomfortable.

2185
02:05:35,153 --> 02:05:36,446
[insects trilling]

2186
02:05:36,488 --> 02:05:39,032
SORYU

2187
02:05:46,747 --> 02:05:48,291
[impact grunts, wheezes]

2188
02:05:49,417 --> 02:05:52,253
[sighs] Ah, now I understand.

2189
02:05:52,795 --> 02:05:54,588
The symbol used for Hakuji,

2190
02:05:54,630 --> 02:05:56,174
it's the same as komainu.

2191
02:05:56,216 --> 02:05:58,301
[chuckles] That makes sense.

2192
02:05:58,343 --> 02:06:00,512
You and I really are the same,
after all.

2193
02:06:00,552 --> 02:06:03,764
We only thrive when we have
something to protect.

2194
02:06:03,806 --> 02:06:05,225
Just like the komainu

2195
02:06:05,266 --> 02:06:07,977
who protect the entrance
to the shrines. [chuckles]

2196
02:06:08,436 --> 02:06:10,562
[laughs heartily]

2197
02:06:11,147 --> 02:06:12,606
[♪ gentle music playing]

2198
02:06:12,815 --> 02:06:15,776
[HAKUJI] There was a story as to
how my master owned this land,

2199
02:06:15,818 --> 02:06:18,988
even though he wasn't a samurai
or anything like that.

2200
02:06:19,030 --> 02:06:22,492
He had rescued an elderly man
from a group of bandits.

2201
02:06:23,076 --> 02:06:25,286
The old man,
who had no living heirs,

2202
02:06:25,328 --> 02:06:27,579
was so impressed
by his Soryu technique

2203
02:06:27,621 --> 02:06:29,623
that he left him
not only his land,

2204
02:06:29,665 --> 02:06:31,583
but the dojo that lay upon it.

2205
02:06:34,754 --> 02:06:37,882
However, there were those
with envious eyes

2206
02:06:37,924 --> 02:06:40,927
who wished to have the land
and dojo all to themselves.

2207
02:06:41,593 --> 02:06:44,055
The Kenjutsu Dojo next door

2208
02:06:44,097 --> 02:06:46,849
started harassing
the Soryu Dojo.

2209
02:06:48,600 --> 02:06:51,687
Because of that,
the Soryu Dojo had a hard time

2210
02:06:51,729 --> 02:06:53,147
keeping any students.

2211
02:07:00,572 --> 02:07:05,452
But now, thanks to my training
here and caring for Koyuki...

2212
02:07:06,702 --> 02:07:09,872
...my heart has finally
found salvation.

2213
02:07:10,915 --> 02:07:13,084
[effort grunting]

2214
02:07:23,428 --> 02:07:25,472
[chuckles]

2215
02:07:29,016 --> 02:07:32,937
Three short years went by
and I turned 18.

2216
02:07:34,063 --> 02:07:35,689
Koyuki was 16.

2217
02:07:36,149 --> 02:07:38,859
She was almost never
bedridden anymore

2218
02:07:38,901 --> 02:07:41,404
and was now able
to live a normal life.

2219
02:07:42,572 --> 02:07:44,031
[chuckles]

2220
02:07:44,616 --> 02:07:45,866
[birds chirping]

2221
02:07:45,908 --> 02:07:47,868
Hakuji! Come here.

2222
02:07:48,620 --> 02:07:49,661
Yes, sir.

2223
02:07:50,121 --> 02:07:51,581
[insects trilling]

2224
02:07:51,623 --> 02:07:52,915
This dojo,

2225
02:07:53,040 --> 02:07:56,002
would you be willing
to take it over for me, Hakuji?

2226
02:07:56,710 --> 02:08:00,047
Koyuki's told me that
she's quite fond of you as well.

2227
02:08:01,007 --> 02:08:02,300
[exclaims in surprise]

2228
02:08:09,849 --> 02:08:12,977
[HAKUJI] As someone branded
with the tattoos of a criminal,

2229
02:08:13,019 --> 02:08:16,481
picturing any kind of future
for myself was hard enough.

2230
02:08:17,815 --> 02:08:22,153
But a future in which someone
could like a person like me?

2231
02:08:22,195 --> 02:08:24,238
I couldn't have even dreamed it.

2232
02:08:26,199 --> 02:08:28,826
My dad asked me
to lead an honest life,

2233
02:08:28,868 --> 02:08:30,953
something I never thought
was possible.

2234
02:08:31,454 --> 02:08:33,705
But perhaps it really is.

2235
02:08:35,166 --> 02:08:37,835
The faint hope
of being able to start over

2236
02:08:37,877 --> 02:08:40,087
began to swell within me

2237
02:08:40,129 --> 02:08:42,923
until it felt like
it was about to burst.

2238
02:08:48,012 --> 02:08:49,472
[♪ tender music playing]

2239
02:08:49,514 --> 02:08:52,141
But I could never have predicted
in that moment

2240
02:08:52,183 --> 02:08:54,143
that the two people
I wanted to protect

2241
02:08:54,185 --> 02:08:56,521
more than anything else
in this life...

2242
02:08:57,522 --> 02:09:00,066
...would end up
meeting the fate they did.

2243
02:09:04,987 --> 02:09:08,241
I had made a trip to Edo
to visit my dad's grave.

2244
02:09:09,033 --> 02:09:12,119
I wanted to let him know
that I was getting married.

2245
02:09:21,921 --> 02:09:25,757
I returned before even a full
day and night had passed.

2246
02:09:28,678 --> 02:09:31,556
Yet a sense of dread
came over me.

2247
02:09:32,557 --> 02:09:35,017
My chest started to feel tight

2248
02:09:35,059 --> 02:09:38,187
and a terrible feeling of nausea
overtook me.

2249
02:09:38,896 --> 02:09:40,231
[retches]

2250
02:09:40,690 --> 02:09:43,192
[MAN] Someone put poison
in the well!

2251
02:09:44,026 --> 02:09:45,570
[voice breaking]
The other school was so angry

2252
02:09:45,612 --> 02:09:47,530
they couldn't beat you
or Mr. Keizo,

2253
02:09:47,572 --> 02:09:49,781
they went and did this
out of spite!

2254
02:09:49,823 --> 02:09:52,368
It's atrocious. Unthinkable!

2255
02:09:52,410 --> 02:09:54,454
They even killed Koyuki!

2256
02:09:57,873 --> 02:09:59,292
[HAKUJI] Why?

2257
02:09:59,500 --> 02:10:02,962
Why is it whenever the ones I
care about are in mortal peril,

2258
02:10:03,003 --> 02:10:05,256
I'm never there for them?

2259
02:10:10,637 --> 02:10:11,971
[fireworks bursting in distance]

2260
02:10:12,597 --> 02:10:14,098
[crickets chirping]

2261
02:10:14,140 --> 02:10:17,226
I had even gone
and made a promise to her.

2262
02:10:19,312 --> 02:10:21,939
Are you sure
that I'm the one for you?

2263
02:10:24,024 --> 02:10:25,610
When we were children,

2264
02:10:26,068 --> 02:10:28,571
do you remember
when you talked to me

2265
02:10:28,613 --> 02:10:30,573
about seeing the fireworks?

2266
02:10:31,198 --> 02:10:35,536
- Huh? Uh... no, not really.
- [giggles softly]

2267
02:10:36,788 --> 02:10:39,499
Because of those little talks
we used to have,

2268
02:10:39,540 --> 02:10:42,209
there were a lot of things
which I took with me

2269
02:10:42,251 --> 02:10:44,337
that gave me hope
for the future.

2270
02:10:45,546 --> 02:10:49,008
You said even if we couldn't see
the fireworks that year,

2271
02:10:49,049 --> 02:10:52,512
we could go to the one
happening next year,

2272
02:10:52,553 --> 02:10:54,263
or the year after that.

2273
02:10:54,972 --> 02:10:58,225
The truth is,
I could never imagine a future

2274
02:10:58,267 --> 02:11:00,645
where I'd still be alive
a year later,

2275
02:11:00,687 --> 02:11:03,481
and certainly not
any longer than that.

2276
02:11:04,649 --> 02:11:06,818
My mother couldn't either.

2277
02:11:06,858 --> 02:11:09,987
I think that's why she ended up
taking her own life,

2278
02:11:10,488 --> 02:11:12,948
'cause she didn't
want to see me die.

2279
02:11:12,990 --> 02:11:14,784
Not just her.

2280
02:11:14,826 --> 02:11:17,662
I could tell my father
had given up hope, too,

2281
02:11:17,704 --> 02:11:19,455
deep down inside.

2282
02:11:20,581 --> 02:11:22,916
Because I was just so weak.

2283
02:11:24,251 --> 02:11:26,838
But you never treated me
that way.

2284
02:11:26,878 --> 02:11:29,549
You were able to see
a future for me.

2285
02:11:30,383 --> 02:11:33,885
You talked to me about
doing things as if...

2286
02:11:33,927 --> 02:11:37,014
As if it were obvious
that I'd still be here.

2287
02:11:37,056 --> 02:11:40,309
[crying softly]
That made me so very happy.

2288
02:11:51,654 --> 02:11:54,741
So, yes, I am sure
you're the one for me.

2289
02:11:56,784 --> 02:11:58,160
Would you...

2290
02:11:58,703 --> 02:12:00,830
Would you be my husband?

2291
02:12:01,247 --> 02:12:02,540
[distant explosion]

2292
02:12:07,837 --> 02:12:08,920
[fireworks bursting]

2293
02:12:08,962 --> 02:12:10,047
Yes.

2294
02:12:10,673 --> 02:12:13,300
I promise to become stronger
than anyone,

2295
02:12:13,925 --> 02:12:16,470
and protect you
for the rest of my life.

2296
02:12:17,847 --> 02:12:19,098
[exclaims]

2297
02:12:20,932 --> 02:12:24,270
[HAKUJI]
In the end, I was all talk.

2298
02:12:24,771 --> 02:12:27,899
I wasn't able to fulfill
any of my promises.

2299
02:12:28,441 --> 02:12:29,817
[chuckles]

2300
02:12:35,489 --> 02:12:37,658
[♪ foreboding music playing]

2301
02:12:40,453 --> 02:12:43,122
What do you want? [gasps]

2302
02:12:43,664 --> 02:12:45,374
You've got some nerve.

2303
02:12:45,416 --> 02:12:48,210
Wait. You're from the Soryu--

2304
02:12:49,086 --> 02:12:50,880
[screaming]

2305
02:12:50,922 --> 02:12:52,548
[♪ somber music playing]

2306
02:12:56,510 --> 02:12:57,845
[man grunts]

2307
02:13:01,390 --> 02:13:04,351
[Hakuji grunts, yells]

2308
02:13:04,393 --> 02:13:06,395
[groans angrily]

2309
02:13:11,567 --> 02:13:14,654
The family, the Soryu Dojo,
were recently poisoned.

2310
02:13:14,695 --> 02:13:16,988
And we believe
that a student of theirs

2311
02:13:17,030 --> 02:13:19,742
retaliated against
the Kenjutsu Dojo.

2312
02:13:19,784 --> 02:13:22,578
Sixty-seven people
were murdered inside.

2313
02:13:22,620 --> 02:13:25,289
He shattered their skulls
and crushed their organs,

2314
02:13:25,331 --> 02:13:26,749
all barehanded.

2315
02:13:27,291 --> 02:13:28,751
Not only were most of the bodies

2316
02:13:28,793 --> 02:13:31,295
mangled and mutilated
beyond recognition,

2317
02:13:31,337 --> 02:13:34,590
most had limbs missing
that we couldn't even locate.

2318
02:13:34,632 --> 02:13:36,968
Organs, limbs, brain matter,

2319
02:13:37,008 --> 02:13:39,052
even jaws and eyeballs
were found

2320
02:13:39,094 --> 02:13:42,222
strewn across the walls
and the ceiling of the premises.

2321
02:13:43,014 --> 02:13:46,059
This killer
was no ordinary human.

2322
02:13:47,436 --> 02:13:49,730
[wet squelching]

2323
02:13:51,106 --> 02:13:54,234
[breathing shakily]

2324
02:14:09,291 --> 02:14:11,418
[MUZAN] I heard
there was some commotion

2325
02:14:11,460 --> 02:14:13,337
about a demon sighting here,

2326
02:14:13,379 --> 02:14:15,882
even though I know
I never sent one.

2327
02:14:16,423 --> 02:14:19,301
So, I decided to come
see for myself.

2328
02:14:19,343 --> 02:14:21,512
Yet all I find is a human.

2329
02:14:22,095 --> 02:14:24,306
How utterly disappointing.

2330
02:14:25,391 --> 02:14:28,519
[HAKUJI] Move, or I'll kill you!

2331
02:14:29,687 --> 02:14:32,023
- [thuds]
- [splatters]

2332
02:14:33,440 --> 02:14:34,775
It just so happens

2333
02:14:34,817 --> 02:14:38,445
I was contemplating
creating 12 powerful demons.

2334
02:14:39,030 --> 02:14:41,281
I wonder if you'll be
able to withstand

2335
02:14:41,323 --> 02:14:43,826
the amount of blood
I'm about to give you.

2336
02:14:45,828 --> 02:14:48,039
You... [grunts]

2337
02:14:49,415 --> 02:14:53,044
...do whatever you want.

2338
02:14:53,920 --> 02:14:56,672
None of it matters.

2339
02:15:02,553 --> 02:15:04,597
[thunder rumbling]

2340
02:15:04,638 --> 02:15:06,766
[♪ somber music playing]

2341
02:15:07,558 --> 02:15:09,685
[grunting]

2342
02:15:11,228 --> 02:15:14,273
[AKAZA] After becoming a demon,
I lost my memories...

2343
02:15:14,857 --> 02:15:17,944
and once again,
started to seek out power.

2344
02:15:18,402 --> 02:15:19,737
- [thuds]
- [grunts]

2345
02:15:19,779 --> 02:15:21,112
- [flesh squelches]
- [grunts]

2346
02:15:27,995 --> 02:15:29,455
[clangs]

2347
02:15:30,330 --> 02:15:32,083
- [wet squelching]
- [sword clatters]

2348
02:15:33,208 --> 02:15:34,877
It's not enough!

2349
02:15:34,919 --> 02:15:36,754
It will never be enough!

2350
02:15:36,796 --> 02:15:38,672
[thunderclap]

2351
02:15:40,758 --> 02:15:44,011
Even though I had nothing
left to my name.

2352
02:15:44,053 --> 02:15:47,306
Even though I had nothing
worth fighting for anymore.

2353
02:15:49,558 --> 02:15:52,686
Even though my family
was no longer around

2354
02:15:52,728 --> 02:15:56,649
and I had no desire
to live in a world without them.

2355
02:15:59,192 --> 02:16:02,613
For over a century,
I committed senseless massacres

2356
02:16:02,655 --> 02:16:04,490
over and over again.

2357
02:16:05,407 --> 02:16:08,619
Thinking about it now,
it's pathetic.

2358
02:16:08,661 --> 02:16:10,329
It's absurd.

2359
02:16:11,204 --> 02:16:13,958
All those deaths
were meaningless.

2360
02:16:19,379 --> 02:16:21,465
Even if I died now,

2361
02:16:21,507 --> 02:16:25,011
I couldn't go where the other
three were waiting for me.

2362
02:16:26,177 --> 02:16:31,100
Damn you for dredging up
these memories. You bastard!

2363
02:16:32,977 --> 02:16:34,895
Pathetic humans,

2364
02:16:34,937 --> 02:16:38,273
clinging on to life
with their fragile bodies!

2365
02:16:39,399 --> 02:16:43,154
Even their strongest
eventually die

2366
02:16:43,194 --> 02:16:45,531
and vanish into thin air!

2367
02:16:46,157 --> 02:16:48,241
[flesh squelching]

2368
02:16:48,868 --> 02:16:50,703
[GIYU] He's still not dead?

2369
02:16:50,744 --> 02:16:52,579
You can't be serious.

2370
02:16:53,747 --> 02:16:56,458
I have to kill him
before it's too late.

2371
02:16:57,459 --> 02:17:01,630
If we let him regenerate,
there will be no stopping him.

2372
02:17:03,340 --> 02:17:04,758
- [loud thump]
- [gasps]

2373
02:17:06,719 --> 02:17:08,929
[grunts] I must have passed out.

2374
02:17:08,971 --> 02:17:10,430
What's going on?

2375
02:17:12,141 --> 02:17:16,103
His head's back!
But how is that even possible?!

2376
02:17:17,270 --> 02:17:19,356
I decapitated him!

2377
02:17:20,024 --> 02:17:22,193
[♪ intense music playing]

2378
02:17:25,487 --> 02:17:28,407
Destructive Death:
Annihilation Type.

2379
02:17:29,116 --> 02:17:31,284
Stop it!

2380
02:17:31,326 --> 02:17:34,038
[AKAZA] Seriously?
He can still move?

2381
02:17:34,080 --> 02:17:36,749
[TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu and I
are going to win!

2382
02:17:36,790 --> 02:17:40,711
Akaza, I'll behead you
as many times as it takes!

2383
02:17:43,589 --> 02:17:45,091
My sword!

2384
02:17:46,383 --> 02:17:48,802
[GIYU] It slipped
out of his hands.

2385
02:17:49,803 --> 02:17:51,430
[TANJIRO] I lost my grip.

2386
02:17:53,724 --> 02:17:54,975
[effort grunts]

2387
02:18:00,564 --> 02:18:02,399
[KEIZO] All right, young man.

2388
02:18:03,150 --> 02:18:04,860
Time to be reborn.

2389
02:18:06,987 --> 02:18:09,823
[AKAZA] I despise
those who are weak.

2390
02:18:11,909 --> 02:18:16,038
Weaklings... Instead of
fighting you fair and square,

2391
02:18:16,080 --> 02:18:18,624
they always resort
to cheap tricks.

2392
02:18:19,416 --> 02:18:21,210
They're atrocious.

2393
02:18:21,710 --> 02:18:23,837
They have no patience.

2394
02:18:23,879 --> 02:18:26,132
And they quickly grow desperate.

2395
02:18:26,173 --> 02:18:28,759
Just thinking about them
makes me sick.

2396
02:18:30,803 --> 02:18:34,473
I killed people
with my fists for protection.

2397
02:18:35,015 --> 02:18:38,727
I desecrated my master's
beloved Soryu with blood.

2398
02:18:40,020 --> 02:18:43,149
And I couldn't follow
my father's last wishes!

2399
02:18:45,567 --> 02:18:47,111
That's right.

2400
02:18:47,653 --> 02:18:50,072
The one I wanted to kill...

2401
02:18:51,782 --> 02:18:53,284
[clatters]

2402
02:18:55,535 --> 02:18:58,247
[TANJIRO] This couldn't be
worse. I dropped my sword!

2403
02:18:58,289 --> 02:19:00,082
[♪ foreboding music playing]

2404
02:19:00,124 --> 02:19:02,668
My fists aren't enough
to stop him!

2405
02:19:13,095 --> 02:19:15,597
He's about to unleash
the Annihilation Type move

2406
02:19:15,639 --> 02:19:17,474
he used on Mr. Rengoku!

2407
02:19:20,644 --> 02:19:23,856
I've got to take Mr. Giyu
with me out of the attack range!

2408
02:19:28,068 --> 02:19:30,696
[GIYU] Leave me! Save yourself!

2409
02:19:36,285 --> 02:19:38,329
[AKAZA] I've got to kill...

2410
02:19:40,789 --> 02:19:42,415
...that weakling

2411
02:19:42,875 --> 02:19:45,044
I've come to hate!

2412
02:20:03,729 --> 02:20:05,898
[♪ dramatic music playing]

2413
02:20:11,362 --> 02:20:12,988
[thudding]

2414
02:20:15,908 --> 02:20:18,035
[grunts, gasps]

2415
02:20:18,618 --> 02:20:20,746
[flesh squelching]

2416
02:20:24,875 --> 02:20:25,918
[blood spurts]

2417
02:20:27,961 --> 02:20:30,381
[TANJIRO]
He just attacked himself.

2418
02:20:33,133 --> 02:20:35,468
Why would he turn on himself
like that?

2419
02:20:36,387 --> 02:20:37,554
Why?

2420
02:20:39,139 --> 02:20:40,974
[♪ melancholic music playing]

2421
02:20:41,016 --> 02:20:42,393
For a second,

2422
02:20:42,433 --> 02:20:45,520
I could pick up the scent
of gratitude from him.

2423
02:20:46,772 --> 02:20:48,982
Why did he smile at me?

2424
02:20:52,778 --> 02:20:55,406
[AKAZA] That's enough! Stop it!

2425
02:20:55,446 --> 02:20:57,866
I don't want to regenerate!

2426
02:20:58,449 --> 02:21:00,286
Don't you get it?

2427
02:21:00,327 --> 02:21:02,162
The battle is over!

2428
02:21:04,123 --> 02:21:07,418
In that decisive moment, I lost.

2429
02:21:07,458 --> 02:21:09,753
That technique
he beheaded me with

2430
02:21:09,795 --> 02:21:11,964
was nothing short of perfection.

2431
02:21:13,215 --> 02:21:17,636
He anticipated my movements
and pivoted at the last second,

2432
02:21:17,677 --> 02:21:21,181
then struck me down before
I could unleash my attack.

2433
02:21:22,099 --> 02:21:23,934
It's over now.

2434
02:21:24,643 --> 02:21:29,231
Let me accept my fate
and go to hell.

2435
02:21:32,401 --> 02:21:34,361
[TANJIRO]
Where's he trying to go?

2436
02:21:40,575 --> 02:21:43,578
[gasps softly]
He stopped in his tracks.

2437
02:21:46,497 --> 02:21:47,791
[HAKUJI] Dad.

2438
02:21:49,668 --> 02:21:51,586
Are you feeling better now?

2439
02:21:52,129 --> 02:21:54,131
Are you in pain anymore?

2440
02:21:55,382 --> 02:21:58,010
No need to worry, son. I'm fine.

2441
02:21:58,802 --> 02:22:00,846
Thank you, Hakuji.

2442
02:22:07,269 --> 02:22:09,021
I'm sorry, Father.

2443
02:22:09,520 --> 02:22:12,899
I'm sorry I couldn't start over
like you wanted.

2444
02:22:12,941 --> 02:22:14,651
I failed you.

2445
02:22:17,696 --> 02:22:19,656
[KEIZO] Do not despair.

2446
02:22:20,240 --> 02:22:22,493
Regardless of
who you grow up to be,

2447
02:22:22,533 --> 02:22:26,079
you're still my son
and still my student.

2448
02:22:26,121 --> 02:22:28,332
Heaven may not accept you...

2449
02:22:29,666 --> 02:22:31,293
...but you needn't worry.

2450
02:22:31,335 --> 02:22:33,420
Our hearts will be with you.

2451
02:22:35,714 --> 02:22:37,216
Master.

2452
02:22:38,425 --> 02:22:39,550
[gasps]

2453
02:22:40,093 --> 02:22:43,722
Didn't you say you were seeking
to become stronger than anyone?

2454
02:22:43,763 --> 02:22:48,727
Don't tell me you intend
to let it end like this, Akaza.

2455
02:22:50,687 --> 02:22:54,066
[AKAZA] That's right.
I can't die here.

2456
02:22:54,107 --> 02:22:56,151
I have to get stronger!

2457
02:22:57,444 --> 02:22:59,321
So what if I got beheaded?

2458
02:22:59,363 --> 02:23:02,074
Who cares
if I win or lose the fight?

2459
02:23:02,782 --> 02:23:05,411
If I kill those
who stand in my way...

2460
02:23:06,203 --> 02:23:09,164
then there's still hope
for me to get stronger!

2461
02:23:11,624 --> 02:23:13,085
I made a promise!

2462
02:23:13,126 --> 02:23:15,128
I'm not about to break it!

2463
02:23:21,009 --> 02:23:23,345
[breathing shakily]

2464
02:23:24,388 --> 02:23:25,514
[♪ tender music playing]

2465
02:23:25,556 --> 02:23:27,266
Mr. Hakuji,

2466
02:23:27,974 --> 02:23:29,809
thank you so much.

2467
02:23:30,310 --> 02:23:32,229
You've done more than enough.

2468
02:23:36,567 --> 02:23:37,984
It's okay.

2469
02:23:38,485 --> 02:23:40,195
We're all right now.

2470
02:23:40,237 --> 02:23:41,821
Akaza!

2471
02:23:41,863 --> 02:23:43,990
[♪ epic cinematic music playing]

2472
02:23:47,618 --> 02:23:50,497
[wailing]

2473
02:23:51,831 --> 02:23:53,208
Sorry!

2474
02:23:53,250 --> 02:23:55,961
I'm sorry
I couldn't protect you!

2475
02:23:56,587 --> 02:23:59,923
I wasn't there
when you needed me to be!

2476
02:24:00,549 --> 02:24:03,718
I couldn't keep
a single promise I made.

2477
02:24:03,760 --> 02:24:07,638
I'm sorry. [sobbing] Please
try to forgive me, Koyuki.

2478
02:24:07,680 --> 02:24:11,017
I'm so sorry.
[continues sobbing]

2479
02:24:13,937 --> 02:24:16,398
I'm so happy you remembered us.

2480
02:24:16,440 --> 02:24:19,151
I can't tell you
how happy that makes me.

2481
02:24:19,818 --> 02:24:23,071
And to see you now
as the man that I once knew,

2482
02:24:23,113 --> 02:24:24,906
I'm so grateful.

2483
02:24:33,165 --> 02:24:36,126
Welcome home, Hakuji.

2484
02:24:40,464 --> 02:24:42,257
Hey, Hakuji.

2485
02:24:42,633 --> 02:24:44,009
Welcome home.

2486
02:24:52,725 --> 02:24:54,353
[HAKUJI] I'm back now.

2487
02:24:54,894 --> 02:24:57,147
I'm finally back home.

2488
02:25:00,442 --> 02:25:02,194
Welcome back home...

2489
02:25:03,195 --> 02:25:04,695
...my darling.

2490
02:25:08,992 --> 02:25:10,118
[gasps softly]

2491
02:25:11,328 --> 02:25:13,497
[♪ gentle music playing]

2492
02:25:32,349 --> 02:25:34,059
[Tanjiro breathing shakily]

2493
02:25:34,100 --> 02:25:35,644
He vanished.

2494
02:25:38,605 --> 02:25:39,939
[gasps]

2495
02:25:41,149 --> 02:25:42,693
[inhales deeply]

2496
02:25:43,652 --> 02:25:45,153
[exhales sharply]

2497
02:25:47,030 --> 02:25:49,241
It's over. Right?

2498
02:25:53,370 --> 02:25:54,745
Gotta hurry...

2499
02:25:55,746 --> 02:25:59,209
...and get to where
Ms. Tamayo is.

2500
02:26:00,168 --> 02:26:01,378
And then...

2501
02:26:08,343 --> 02:26:10,387
[grunts weakly] Tanjiro.

2502
02:26:16,351 --> 02:26:17,477
[exhales]

2503
02:26:19,730 --> 02:26:22,649
[Kasugai Crow cawing]

2504
02:26:23,483 --> 02:26:28,321
Tanjiro! Giyu!
Have defeated Upper Three!

2505
02:26:28,363 --> 02:26:32,325
They are unable to stay
conscious due to exhaustion!

2506
02:26:32,367 --> 02:26:33,952
They've passed out!

2507
02:26:39,332 --> 02:26:45,255
Tanjiro! Giyu!
Have defeated Upper Three!

2508
02:26:45,297 --> 02:26:47,090
Upper Three!

2509
02:26:51,762 --> 02:26:53,179
[♪ haunting
choral music playing]

2510
02:26:53,221 --> 02:26:55,181
[KOKUSHIBO] Akaza!

2511
02:26:55,223 --> 02:26:58,059
His presence has vanished.

2512
02:26:59,978 --> 02:27:02,731
What a baffling conclusion.

2513
02:27:05,692 --> 02:27:07,152
Akaza...

2514
02:27:08,528 --> 02:27:12,699
...what happened to your burning
ambition to defeat me?

2515
02:27:14,618 --> 02:27:19,038
To think you'd abandoned
everything you stood for...

2516
02:27:20,165 --> 02:27:23,960
...and turned your back
on the path to greatness.

2517
02:27:24,795 --> 02:27:26,588
[♪ music intensifies]

2518
02:27:30,676 --> 02:27:33,720
Your weakness appalls me.

2519
02:27:38,849 --> 02:27:39,976
Huh?

2520
02:27:40,977 --> 02:27:42,187
[exclaims]

2521
02:27:42,562 --> 02:27:43,730
This feeling.

2522
02:27:44,272 --> 02:27:46,817
Could Lord Akaza be dead?

2523
02:27:48,276 --> 02:27:49,611
Very strange.

2524
02:27:49,653 --> 02:27:53,198
Surely my imagination
must be running wild, right?

2525
02:27:53,699 --> 02:27:58,537
It almost felt like Lord Akaza
had turned into some creature.

2526
02:28:01,039 --> 02:28:03,792
But now that he's dead,
I guess it doesn't matter.

2527
02:28:03,834 --> 02:28:05,960
- [laughs]
- [rattling]

2528
02:28:07,003 --> 02:28:08,797
Let's see,

2529
02:28:08,839 --> 02:28:10,215
where was I?

2530
02:28:10,799 --> 02:28:12,967
Oh, I remember.

2531
02:28:13,426 --> 02:28:16,179
I had just asked for your name,
hadn't I?

2532
02:28:17,305 --> 02:28:19,098
[Kanao breathing shakily]

2533
02:28:29,067 --> 02:28:31,528
[KASUGAI CROW] Tanjiro! Giyu!

2534
02:28:31,570 --> 02:28:33,988
Have defeated Upper Three!

2535
02:28:34,030 --> 02:28:35,532
Upper Three!

2536
02:28:36,199 --> 02:28:37,450
Did you hear that?

2537
02:28:37,492 --> 02:28:40,911
Yes. Excellent work, Tomioka.

2538
02:28:41,454 --> 02:28:43,582
Excellent work, Kamado.

2539
02:28:44,290 --> 02:28:46,501
[♪ closing theme song playing]

2540
02:28:48,670 --> 02:28:52,173
Mr. Tomioka and Tanjiro.
They did it!

2541
02:28:52,215 --> 02:28:54,925
[IGURO] Now it's our turn
to follow their lead.

2542
02:28:55,468 --> 02:28:56,803
Right!

2543
02:29:04,185 --> 02:29:05,437
[demon snarling]

2544
02:29:11,234 --> 02:29:13,612
Hang in there, Agatsuma!

2545
02:29:17,616 --> 02:29:18,991
[cawing]

2546
02:29:19,033 --> 02:29:21,035
[INOSUKE] Start flapping
those wings faster,

2547
02:29:21,077 --> 02:29:22,621
or I'm gonna keep poking!

2548
02:29:23,162 --> 02:29:24,581
You're gonna use those wings

2549
02:29:24,623 --> 02:29:26,541
to show me where
the strongest demon is!

2550
02:29:26,583 --> 02:29:27,876
You hear me?

2551
02:29:28,376 --> 02:29:30,587
I'm coming through!

2552
02:29:31,087 --> 02:29:32,255
Hyah!

2553
02:29:32,297 --> 02:29:33,757
Now we're talkin'!

2554
02:29:33,799 --> 02:29:36,551
I'm sensing a powerful
demon over here.

2555
02:29:36,593 --> 02:29:38,177
[cawing]

2556
02:29:43,433 --> 02:29:45,393
Where is Big Brother?

2557
02:29:55,487 --> 02:29:57,489
Where are all the Upper Ranks?

2558
02:29:57,530 --> 02:29:59,741
Tell me! Come on!

2559
02:30:00,241 --> 02:30:02,953
I'm gonna bury you all!

2560
02:30:10,794 --> 02:30:12,671
[KANATA] The passageway
leading north

2561
02:30:12,712 --> 02:30:14,589
on the 88th level is clear.

2562
02:30:14,631 --> 02:30:16,299
No sign of Muzan.

2563
02:30:16,967 --> 02:30:18,802
[KUINA]
The 100th and 27th levels

2564
02:30:18,844 --> 02:30:21,471
in the southeast are clear.
No sign of Muzan.

2565
02:30:22,472 --> 02:30:24,140
He's in here.

2566
02:30:24,182 --> 02:30:25,517
He has to be.

2567
02:30:25,558 --> 02:30:26,768
But where is he?

2568
02:30:27,686 --> 02:30:29,938
[KANATA] There's no sign
of Muzan on any of the levels

2569
02:30:29,980 --> 02:30:32,398
from 90 to 100, either.

2570
02:30:34,150 --> 02:30:37,153
[KUINA] Covering the entire
100th and 33rd levels.

2571
02:30:37,195 --> 02:30:38,738
No sign of Muzan.

2572
02:30:40,239 --> 02:30:42,450
Our crows will find you.

2573
02:30:42,492 --> 02:30:45,244
You can only hide from us
for so long.

2574
02:30:45,787 --> 02:30:49,039
We'll search every inch
of this Infinity Castle.

2575
02:30:49,081 --> 02:30:53,169
Even if you try to run from us,
we will hunt you down.

2576
02:30:53,628 --> 02:30:55,254
[plucking]

2577
02:30:57,256 --> 02:30:58,675
FOUR

2578
02:30:59,258 --> 02:31:01,427
[continues plucking
biwa strings]

2579
02:31:07,767 --> 02:31:10,854
Multi-layered structures
are headed northeast.

2580
02:31:11,354 --> 02:31:14,983
Attention! The castle's
expanding in every direction.

2581
02:31:15,025 --> 02:31:16,776
Folding over themselves!

2582
02:31:16,818 --> 02:31:20,070
[Nakime plucking
biwa strings faster]

2583
02:31:20,822 --> 02:31:22,574
[BOTH] And becoming one!

2584
02:31:28,329 --> 02:31:30,916
[gasps] You can't be serious.

2585
02:31:32,042 --> 02:31:33,459
No.

2586
02:31:33,501 --> 02:31:34,669
It's fine.

2587
02:31:34,711 --> 02:31:36,713
We've come too far to lose.

2588
02:31:37,463 --> 02:31:39,465
Crows, push forward,

2589
02:31:39,507 --> 02:31:41,467
and find Muzan!

2590
02:31:46,222 --> 02:31:49,350
[MUZAN] Try all you want,
Demon Slayers!

2591
02:31:49,392 --> 02:31:51,519
But each one of you
will meet your end

2592
02:31:51,561 --> 02:31:53,145
before ever reaching me!

2593
02:31:53,688 --> 02:31:57,483
You may be feeling smug after
beheading one of my Upper Ranks,

2594
02:31:57,525 --> 02:32:01,571
but unless you could kill me,
your triumph is meaningless!

2595
02:32:02,405 --> 02:32:05,533
[laughs maliciously]

2596
02:32:05,575 --> 02:32:08,286
You're all going to die
the most pointless deaths

2597
02:32:08,327 --> 02:32:11,247
all the while
never seeing my face!

2598
02:32:11,289 --> 02:32:15,543
I can't think of a more fitting
end for the Demon Slayer Corps.

2599
02:32:16,044 --> 02:32:18,504
Mark my words.
When I'm done here,

2600
02:32:18,546 --> 02:32:21,340
I'm going to make you regret
the day you were born!

2601
02:32:22,425 --> 02:32:23,718
Just wait.

2602
02:32:23,760 --> 02:32:26,930
You're each going to squirm
and writhe in pain.

2603
02:32:26,972 --> 02:32:28,848
Draw your final breaths

2604
02:32:28,890 --> 02:32:31,977
because for every one
of you Demon Slayers,

2605
02:32:32,018 --> 02:32:35,563
there is no tomorrow!

2606
02:32:45,657 --> 02:32:47,199
[KASUGAI CROW 1] Please, Giyu.

2607
02:32:50,703 --> 02:32:52,664
Don't die!

2608
02:32:59,629 --> 02:33:03,466
[KASUGAI CROW 2] We can't
have you dying on us, Tanjiro.

2609
02:33:15,854 --> 02:33:18,106
[music ends]

2610
02:33:18,148 --> 02:33:20,316
[♪ closing theme song playing]

2611
02:34:43,816 --> 02:34:46,360
[song ends]



